window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0010", [{"word":"consistent","ipa_uk":"/kənˈsɪstənt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈsɪstənt/","definition_zh":"一致的；始终如一的；相符的；连贯的","definition_en":"staying the same over time, agreeing with something else, or free from internal contradiction","core_image":"三根柱子并排立在同一块地基上，高低一样、方向一致","scene":"实验室里，三名同学用同一台天平重复称量同一份样品，三次读数每次都相同。老师说：The three readings are consistent.","sceneCN":"这里 consistent 是「彼此相符、结果一致」（第 1、3 个义项：各部分站在一起、与证据相符）；句意：三次读数彼此一致。图中可辨识物件：天平、样品瓶、记录纸、三名同学。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"一致的；始终如一的；前后连贯的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"与……相符的；与……相一致的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"consistent with","zh":"与……一致；与……相符"},{"phrase":"consistent results","zh":"一致的结果；稳定的结果"},{"phrase":"consistent quality","zh":"稳定的品质；始终如一的质量"},{"phrase":"a consistent policy","zh":"一贯的政策"},{"phrase":"consistent across","zh":"在……范围内保持一致"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more consistent"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most consistent"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"consistency","pos":"n.","zh":"一致性；连贯性；稠度"},{"word":"consistently","pos":"adv.","zh":"一贯地；始终如一地"},{"word":"inconsistent","pos":"adj.","zh":"不一致的；自相矛盾的"},{"word":"inconsistency","pos":"n.","zh":"不一致；矛盾之处"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Standing together: parts that agree","titleCN":"站在一起：各部分彼此吻合","definition":"of parts, statements or numbers, agreeing with one another so that they form one coherent whole","definitionCN":"（各部分、陈述或数字）彼此吻合，从而构成一个连贯的整体","example":"The two reports are consistent in every important detail.","exampleCN":"两份报告在所有重要细节上都一致。","why":"The Latin verb consistere is com- 'together' + sistere 'to stand'. Things that stand together do not pull apart; their edges line up.","whyCN":"拉丁动词 consistere 由 com-“一起”加 sistere“站立”构成。站在一起的东西不会彼此拉开，它们的边缘对得上。"},{"no":"02","title":"The same over time: steady and unchanging","titleCN":"时间上的同一：稳定不变","definition":"remaining the same in quality, level or behaviour over a period of time","definitionCN":"在一段时间内质量、水平或行为保持不变","example":"The team has shown consistent improvement all season.","exampleCN":"这支队伍整个赛季都在稳定进步。","why":"If the parts keep standing in the same relation day after day, the whole looks steady. Consistency in time is the same 'standing together' repeated at every moment.","whyCN":"如果各部分日复一日保持同样的相对位置，整体看起来就稳定。时间上的一致性，就是同一个“站在一起”在每一刻重复出现。"},{"no":"03","title":"Agreeing with the evidence","titleCN":"与证据相符","definition":"matching or not contradicting known facts, measurements or another account","definitionCN":"与已知事实、测量结果或另一份叙述相符，不产生矛盾","example":"The damage is consistent with a fall from a low height.","exampleCN":"这些损伤与从低处坠落的情况相符。","why":"When a new fact is placed beside the old facts and they stand together without a gap, we call it consistent with them. The preposition with marks the second thing standing alongside.","whyCN":"当新事实被放到旧事实旁边、两者毫无缝隙地站在一起，我们就说它与旧事实相符。介词 with 标记的正是“并排站着的第二样东西”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Even in texture: the physical sense","titleCN":"质地均匀：物质层面的“一致”","definition":"of a substance, having an even texture or thickness throughout, with no lumps","definitionCN":"（物质）整体质地或稀稠程度均匀，没有结块","example":"Stir the sauce until it is smooth and consistent.","exampleCN":"搅拌酱汁，直到它细腻均匀。","why":"This is the oldest physical sense, kept alive in the noun consistency 'thickness'. A mixture is consistent when its particles all stand together in the same way.","whyCN":"这是最古老的具体义，保留在名词 consistency“稠度”里。混合物里的颗粒以同样的方式站在一起时，它就是均匀的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Logically coherent: no contradiction inside","titleCN":"逻辑自洽：内部没有矛盾","definition":"of an argument, story or set of beliefs, containing no two parts that cancel each other","definitionCN":"（论证、故事或信念体系）内部没有彼此抵消的两个部分","example":"His account of the accident is not consistent: he gives two different times.","exampleCN":"他对事故的叙述不自洽：他说了两个不同的时间。","why":"A contradiction is two statements that cannot stand together. Consistent thinking is thinking in which every pair of statements can still share the same ground.","whyCN":"矛盾就是两句话无法站在一起。自洽的思维，就是其中任意两句话都仍能共享同一块地面。"},{"no":"06","title":"A person you can rely on","titleCN":"为人始终如一：可靠","definition":"of a person, acting in the same way on different occasions, so that others can predict and trust the behaviour","definitionCN":"（人）在不同场合行为相同，使他人能够预测并信任其表现","example":"She is consistent: she treats every student the same way.","exampleCN":"她为人始终如一：对每个学生都一视同仁。","why":"A person whose words and actions stand together over time becomes predictable, and predictable behaviour is the basis of trust.","whyCN":"一个言行长期站在一起的人会变得可预测，而可预测的行为正是信任的基础。"},{"no":"07","title":"Consistent with a rule or theory","titleCN":"与规则或理论相合","definition":"in logic, law and science, compatible with a rule, principle or model","definitionCN":"在逻辑、法律与科学中，与某条规则、原则或模型相容","example":"The results are consistent with the predictions of the model.","exampleCN":"结果与该模型的预测相符。","why":"A theory lays down a line; a result is consistent when it falls on that line. Compatibility is spatial again: the two things can occupy the same place without conflict.","whyCN":"理论画出一条线；结果落在线上时就是“相符”。相容仍然是空间性的：两样东西能占据同一个位置而不冲突。"},{"no":"08","title":"Consistency as a measurable property","titleCN":"consistency：可测量的稠度、浓度","definition":"the noun consistency names how thick, firm or uniform a substance is","definitionCN":"名词 consistency 指物质有多稠、多硬或多均匀","example":"Add water until the mixture reaches the consistency of thick cream.","exampleCN":"加水，直到混合物达到浓奶油的稠度。","why":"Medieval Latin consistentia meant 'a standing together'. A thick substance holds its own parts together, so the word moved from 'how it coheres' to 'how thick it is'.","whyCN":"中世纪拉丁语 consistentia 意为“站在一起”。浓稠的物质能把自己的各部分保持在一起，于是这个词从“它如何聚合”变成了“它有多稠”。"},{"no":"09","title":"Consistently: the adverb of repeated sameness","titleCN":"consistently：一贯地、每次都一样","definition":"the adverb consistently describes doing something in the same way on every occasion","definitionCN":"副词 consistently 指每一次都以同样的方式做某事","example":"He has consistently refused to take credit for the discovery.","exampleCN":"他一贯拒绝把这一发现的功劳归于自己。","why":"The -ly suffix turns the standing-together into a manner of acting: each occasion is placed beside the last, and the line stays straight.","whyCN":"-ly 后缀把“站在一起”变成一种行为方式：每一次都被放到上一次旁边，线条始终保持笔直。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Consistent comes straight from Latin: consistere 'to stand firm, take a standing position', from com- 'together' + sistere 'to stand (something)'. The word began as 'consisting' and only later came to mean 'agreeing'.","cn":"consistent 直接来自拉丁语：consistere“站稳、站定”，由 com-“一起”加 sistere“使站立”构成。这个词最初表示“由……构成”，后来才发展出“一致、相符”的意思。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Consistere meant 'to stand firm, take a standing position, stop, halt'. It was also used of things that 'consist of' certain parts, because parts that stand together make up a whole.","cn":"consistere 意为“站稳、站定、停住”。它也用于表示某物“由某些部分构成”，因为站在一起的部分正好组成一个整体。"},{"era":"LATIN VERB FAMILY","en":"Sistere 'to place, set up' is a causative of stare 'to stand'. Both go back to PIE *sta- 'to stand, make firm', one of the best-attested roots in the family.","cn":"sistere“放置、使立起”是 stare“站立”的使役形式。两者都追溯到原始印欧语 *sta-“站立、使牢固”，这是该语系中证据最充分的词根之一。"},{"era":"1570s ENGLISH","en":"English first recorded consistent in the 1570s with the now obsolete sense 'consisting (of), made up of'. The parts were still the subject.","cn":"英语最早在 16 世纪 70 年代记录 consistent，当时的含义是“由……构成”，现已废弃。那时主语仍然是“部分”。"},{"era":"1640s ENGLISH","en":"The modern sense 'standing together in agreement' (with with) is first attested in the 1640s. Two accounts now stand side by side instead of parts inside one object.","cn":"现代义“彼此一致、相符”（与 with 连用）最早记录于 17 世纪 40 年代。此时并排站立的变成了两份叙述，而不再是一个物体内部的部分。"},{"era":"1732 ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'marked by consistency, uniform in behaviour' appears in 1732. Sameness over time is the same standing-together stretched along the timeline.","cn":"“具有一致性、行为一贯”的义项出现于 1732 年。时间上的同一，就是同一个“站在一起”沿时间轴被拉长。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN → ENGLISH","en":"Medieval Latin consistentia 'a standing together' gave English consistency (1590s) for firmness of matter, then 'agreement' (1650s), then 'steady adherence to principles' (1716).","cn":"中世纪拉丁语 consistentia“站在一起”给出英语 consistency（16 世纪 90 年代），先指物质的坚实度，再指“一致”（17 世纪 50 年代），后指“对原则的坚守”（1716 年）。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the Latin sist- stem; the near-meaning group contains words that also describe sameness, each from a different angle.","cn":"形近组共享拉丁词干 sist-；近义组里的词也从不同角度描述“相同”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"consist","ipa":"/kənˈsɪst/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"to be made up of; to have as parts. It is the base verb behind consistent and keeps the original 'stand together' idea.","definitionCN":"由……组成；包含某些部分。它是 consistent 背后的基础动词，保留了最初的“站在一起”。"},{"word":"insistent","ipa":"/ɪnˈsɪstənt/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"demanding something forcefully and repeatedly. It uses in- 'upon' + sistere 'stand', literally 'standing upon' a demand.","definitionCN":"坚持要求、一再强求。它由 in-“在……之上”加 sistere“站立”构成，字面是“站在要求上不走”。"},{"word":"constant","ipa":"/ˈkɒnstənt/","tag":"near spelling, different verb","definition":"unchanging; happening all the time. It comes from constare 'stand firm' (com- + stare), a cousin rather than the same word.","definitionCN":"不变的；持续不断的。它来自 constare“站稳”（com- + stare），是同族词而不是同一个词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"constant","ipa":"/ˈkɒnstənt/","tag":"no change","definition":"staying the same without interruption. It stresses absence of change, while consistent stresses absence of contradiction.","definitionCN":"不间断地保持不变。它强调“没有变化”，而 consistent 强调“没有矛盾”。"},{"word":"steady","ipa":"/ˈstiːdi/","tag":"even rate","definition":"regular and controlled, not changing suddenly. It is used of rates, progress and hands, and implies smooth motion rather than logical fit.","definitionCN":"有规律、受控制的，不突然变化。它用于速度、进展和手法，暗示平稳运动而非逻辑吻合。"},{"word":"coherent","ipa":"/kəʊˈhɪərənt/","tag":"logical whole","definition":"well organized and easy to follow, with parts that fit together. It focuses on the reader's understanding of a whole text or argument.","definitionCN":"条理清楚、易于理解，各部分衔接良好。它强调的是读者对整段文字或论证的理解。"},{"word":"uniform","ipa":"/ˈjuːnɪfɔːm/","tag":"same in form","definition":"the same in all parts or cases. It describes sameness of form or appearance, not agreement between statements.","definitionCN":"各部分或各情况下都相同。它描述外形或形式上的同一，而不是陈述之间的相符。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: con- 'together', sistere 'stand', the noun consistency and the everyday patterns consistent with and consistently.","cn":"只用真实构件：con-“一起”、sistere“站立”，以及名词 consistency 和固定搭配 consistent with、consistently。"},"normal":[{"en":"Con- means 'together' and sistere means 'stand'. Consistent things literally stand together: the parts line up and none of them falls out of line.","cn":"con- 意为“一起”，sistere 意为“站立”。consistent 的东西字面上就是“站在一起”：各部分排成一条线，没有谁掉队。"},{"en":"Compare constant and consistent: constant says 'it does not change', consistent says 'it does not contradict itself'. A constant noise is steady; a consistent story has no gaps.","cn":"对比 constant 与 consistent：constant 说“它不变”，consistent 说“它不自相矛盾”。constant 的噪音是持续的；consistent 的故事是没有漏洞的。"},{"en":"Inconsistent is simply in- 'not' + consistent: the parts refuse to stand together.","cn":"inconsistent 就是 in-“不”加 consistent：各部分不肯站在一起。"},{"en":"Consistency also names the thickness of a sauce or cement, because a thick substance holds its own parts together.","cn":"consistency 还指酱汁或水泥的稠度，因为浓稠的物质能把自己的各部分保持在一起。"},{"en":"The fixed patterns are consistent with a fact and consistently do something; the preposition tells you what the second thing is standing beside.","cn":"固定搭配是 consistent with a fact（与事实相符）和 consistently do something（一贯做某事）；介词告诉你第二样东西站在什么旁边。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a row of fence posts on one stone base. Consistency is the base: remove it and each post leans its own way.","cn":"想象一排篱笆柱立在同一块石基上。一致性就是那块石基：抽掉它，每根柱子都会朝各自的方向倾斜。"},{"en":"The same image stretches in two directions: sideways across parts (no gaps) and forward in time (no sudden change). English uses one word for both.","cn":"同一个意象向两个方向延伸：横向跨越各部分（没有缝隙），纵向贯穿时间（没有突变）。英语用同一个词覆盖两者。"},{"en":"A person is consistent when their words and actions keep standing on the same base, which is why consistency feels like trustworthiness rather than mere repetition.","cn":"一个人的言行始终立在同一块基上时，他就是始终如一的；所以 consistency 给人的感觉是可靠，而不只是重复。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Her test scores have been consistent from month to month.","cn":"她的测验成绩每个月都保持稳定。"},{"en":"The witness's story is consistent with the video record.","cn":"证人的叙述与录像记录相符。"},{"en":"Mix the paint until it has the consistency of thin cream.","cn":"把颜料调匀，直到它达到稀奶油的稠度。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·西斯·腾特”——肯（定）让西斯腾（出）同一个位置站好，每次都站同一格 → consistent 始终如一的、一致的","word":"consistent"},"root":"源自拉丁语 consistere“站稳、站定”，由 com-“一起”+ sistere“站立”构成，核心是“各部分站在一起、不散开”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of consistent, all built on one posture: things standing together. Parts, numbers, evidence, textures, arguments, people and rules are each placed side by side, and consistency is the absence of a gap between them.","cn":"consistent 的九个义项都建立在一个姿态上：东西站在一起。部分、数字、证据、质地、论证、人、规则依次被并排摆放，而一致性就是它们之间没有缝隙。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: separate posts standing on one shared base, all at the same height.","cn":"核心意象：几根分开的柱子立在同一块共享的地基上，高度齐平。"},"chain":["SEPARATE PARTS","STAND TOGETHER","NO GAP","AGREE","SAME OVER TIME","TRUSTWORTHY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 03 · 07","en":"AGREEMENT BETWEEN THINGS: statements, readings, evidence and theories are placed beside one another and line up.","cn":"事物之间的相符：陈述、读数、证据与理论被并排摆放，并且对齐。"},{"senses":"02 · 06 · 09","en":"AGREEMENT ACROSS TIME: the same posture repeated every day becomes steadiness in results and reliability in a person.","cn":"时间上的一致：同一姿态每天重复，就成为结果的稳定和人的可靠。"},{"senses":"04 · 08","en":"AGREEMENT INSIDE MATTER: a substance whose particles hold together evenly is smooth, and its degree of holding is its consistency.","cn":"物质内部的一致：颗粒均匀地保持在一起的物质是细腻的，而这种“保持”的程度就是稠度。"},{"senses":"05","en":"AGREEMENT INSIDE THOUGHT: an argument is consistent when no two of its statements pull the ground apart.","cn":"思想内部的一致：论证中没有任何两句话把地基拉开时，它就是自洽的。"},{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"THE WITH-PATTERN: consistent with marks the second thing standing alongside, which is why the phrase answers 'in agreement with what?'.","cn":"with 结构：consistent with 标记并排站着的第二样东西，所以这个短语回答的是“与什么相符”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Consistent is a Latin participle used as an adjective: con- + sist- + -ent. English adds only ordinary suffixes and the negative prefix in-.","cn":"consistent 是拉丁语分词用作形容词：con- + sist- + -ent。英语只再加普通后缀和否定前缀 in-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is real and small: consistere 'stand firm', sistere 'place', stare 'stand', and the derived nouns consistentia and consistentem.","cn":"拉丁词族真实而精简：consistere“站稳”、sistere“放置”、stare“站立”，以及派生名词 consistentia、consistentem。"},"items":[{"word":"consistent","structure":"con- (together) + sist- (stand) + -ent (adjective from participle)","meaning":"standing together; agreeing or unchanging","meaningCN":"一致的；始终如一的（con- 表一起，-ent 构成形容词）","example":"The two sets of figures are consistent.","exampleCN":"两组数字是一致的。"},{"word":"consistently","structure":"consistent + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in the same way every time","meaningCN":"一贯地；始终如一地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She consistently arrives before nine.","exampleCN":"她一贯九点前到。"},{"word":"consistency","structure":"consistent + -ency (noun of state)","meaning":"the state of agreeing, or the thickness of a substance","meaningCN":"一致性；连贯性；稠度（-ency 构成状态名词）","example":"The consistency of the results surprised us.","exampleCN":"结果的一致程度让我们吃惊。"},{"word":"consistence","structure":"consistent + -ence (older noun form)","meaning":"the older spelling of consistency, still used for texture","meaningCN":"consistency 的旧式拼写，仍用于指质地","example":"The clay had a stiff consistence.","exampleCN":"这黏土质地硬实。"},{"word":"inconsistent","structure":"in- (not) + consistent","meaning":"not agreeing; self-contradictory","meaningCN":"不一致的；自相矛盾的（in- 表否定）","example":"His answers were inconsistent.","exampleCN":"他的回答前后不一致。"},{"word":"inconsistency","structure":"in- (not) + consistency","meaning":"a point where things fail to agree","meaningCN":"不一致之处；矛盾","example":"The report contains several inconsistencies.","exampleCN":"这份报告有几处前后矛盾。"},{"word":"consist","structure":"con- (together) + sist- (stand)","meaning":"to be composed of; to have as parts","meaningCN":"由……组成（同一词根的动词）","example":"The team consists of five members.","exampleCN":"这个团队由五名成员组成。"},{"word":"self-consistent","structure":"self + consistent (compound adjective)","meaning":"internally coherent, with no part contradicting another","meaningCN":"自洽的；内部无矛盾的复合形容词","example":"A good theory must be self-consistent.","exampleCN":"好的理论必须自洽。"},{"word":"consistently","structure":"consistent + -ly (repeated manner)","meaning":"with steady repetition, without exceptions","meaningCN":"稳定重复地、无例外地","example":"Prices have risen consistently since spring.","exampleCN":"自春季以来价格持续上涨。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"consistere","structure":"con- + sistere","meaning":"to stand firm, take a position, consist of","meaningCN":"站稳；站定；由……构成"},{"word":"sistere","structure":"causative of stare","meaning":"to place, set up, cause to stand","meaningCN":"放置；使立起"},{"word":"stare","structure":"PIE *sta-","meaning":"to stand, be standing","meaningCN":"站立"}]}},{"word":"constitute","ipa_uk":"/kənˈstɪtjuːt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈstɪtuːt/","definition_zh":"构成；组成；设立；任命；相当于","definition_en":"to form or make up a whole, to set up an institution, to appoint someone, or to amount to something","core_image":"三块积木依次摆好，撑起一道完整的拱门","scene":"博物馆修复室里，三块残片被拼回一只完整的陶罐。修复师说：The three fragments constitute the whole vessel.","sceneCN":"这里 constitute 是「构成、组成整体」（第 1、6 个义项：部分组成整体）；句意：三块残片构成了整只陶罐。图中可辨识物件：陶罐残片、修复台、毛刷、胶带。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"构成；组成；设立；任命"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"相当于；算作；被视为"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"constitute a majority","zh":"构成多数"},{"phrase":"constitute a threat","zh":"构成威胁"},{"phrase":"constitute a committee","zh":"设立一个委员会"},{"phrase":"constitute evidence","zh":"构成证据"},{"phrase":"be constituted of","zh":"由……构成"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"constitutes"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"constituted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"constituted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"constituting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"constitution","pos":"n.","zh":"宪法；构成；体质"},{"word":"constitutional","pos":"adj.","zh":"宪法的；符合宪法的；体质的"},{"word":"constituent","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"成分；选民；构成的"},{"word":"constituency","pos":"n.","zh":"选区；选民群体"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Make up a whole: parts forming one thing","titleCN":"构成：若干部分组成一个整体","definition":"of parts, to form or make up a whole when taken together","definitionCN":"（各部分）合在一起构成一个整体","example":"Twelve members constitute the governing board.","exampleCN":"十二名成员构成了管理委员会。","why":"Con- 'together' + statuere 'to set, place': the parts are set in place together. Constitute looks at the parts from the whole's side, while consist looks at the whole from the parts' side.","whyCN":"con-“一起”加 statuere“放置、设立”：各部分被一起摆到位。constitute 是从整体看部分，而 consist 是从部分看整体。"},{"no":"02","title":"Amount to: what something counts as","titleCN":"相当于：某事物算作什么","definition":"to be equivalent to something in effect or in the eyes of the law","definitionCN":"在效果上或在法律上等同于某事物","example":"Refusing to answer constitutes a failure to cooperate.","exampleCN":"拒绝回答即构成不配合。","why":"Once a set of facts is 'set up' as one legal or logical unit, it counts as that unit. The verb moves from building a whole to naming what the whole amounts to.","whyCN":"当一组事实被“立”成一个法律或逻辑单元，它就算作那个单元。动词从“搭出整体”转为“命名这个整体算什么”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Set up an institution","titleCN":"设立：把机构立起来","definition":"to establish an organization, committee, court or system officially","definitionCN":"正式建立组织、委员会、法庭或制度","example":"The city constituted a special committee to study the problem.","exampleCN":"该市设立了一个专门委员会来研究这个问题。","why":"Statuere means 'to cause to stand'. To constitute a body is to make it stand on its own feet as an institution, not merely to gather people in a room.","whyCN":"statuere 意为“使站立”。constitute 一个机构，就是让它作为机构独立站住脚，而不只是把人聚在一间屋子里。"},{"no":"04","title":"Appoint someone to an office","titleCN":"任命：把人放到职位上","definition":"to appoint or formally place a person in a position of authority","definitionCN":"任命或正式把某人放到有权力的职位上","example":"The board constituted her chief financial officer last spring.","exampleCN":"董事会去年春天任命她为财务总监。","why":"This is the oldest English sense (c. 1400): a person is 'set' into a seat of authority. The image of placing something firmly explains why the word also means 'appoint'.","whyCN":"这是英语中最古老的义项（约 1400 年）：把人“安放”到权威的座位上。“把事情稳稳放好”的意象解释了它为什么也能表示“任命”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Give legal or official character","titleCN":"依法设定：赋予正式身份","definition":"to give a group or arrangement its official legal form or status","definitionCN":"赋予某个团体或安排正式的合法形式或地位","example":"The landowners constituted themselves into a water district.","exampleCN":"这些土地所有者把自己组成为一个水务区。","why":"When people constitute themselves into a body, they set themselves up as a legal person. The reflexive form marks the group both as builder and as building.","whyCN":"当人们 constitute themselves into a body（把自己组成为一个团体），他们就把自己立成了一个法律主体。反身形式表明这个群体既是建造者又是被建造物。"},{"no":"06","title":"Form a person's nature or constitution","titleCN":"构成体质与性情","definition":"of qualities or conditions, to make up the character, health or nature of a person or thing","definitionCN":"（品质或条件）构成一个人或事物的性格、体质或本性","example":"Genes and habits together constitute a person's health.","exampleCN":"基因与习惯共同构成一个人的健康状况。","why":"The noun constitution first meant 'the way a thing is constituted', and only later 'the body's condition'. What is built into a person is literally their constitution.","whyCN":"名词 constitution 最初指“一个事物被构成的方式”，后来才指“身体状况”。被“搭进”一个人身上的东西，字面上就是他的体质。"},{"no":"07","title":"Constituted: already set up","titleCN":"constituted：已成立的、依章程设立的","definition":"the past participle used as an adjective for bodies that have been formally established","definitionCN":"过去分词作形容词，指已正式建立的机构或团体","example":"The newly constituted council met for the first time in May.","exampleCN":"新成立的理事会于五月首次开会。","why":"The participle freezes the act of setting-up into a state: the standing has been done, and the institution now simply exists.","whyCN":"分词把“设立”这一动作冻结成状态：站立已经完成，机构现在只是存在着。"},{"no":"08","title":"Constitution: the fundamental law","titleCN":"constitution：宪法、根本章程","definition":"the noun for the set of fundamental rules by which a state or organization is governed","definitionCN":"指国家或组织据以治理的一套根本规则","example":"The constitution guarantees freedom of speech.","exampleCN":"宪法保障言论自由。","why":"A constitution is what has been 'set up' as the frame within which all other laws stand. The 1730s sense of a written document grew out of the older sense 'body of rules'.","whyCN":"constitution 就是被“立”起来、作为其他一切法律站立框架的东西。18 世纪 30 年代“成文文件”的义项，是从更早的“规则体系”义发展出来的。"},{"no":"09","title":"Constituent: a part, and a voter","titleCN":"constituent：成分，也是选民","definition":"the noun constituent names a part that makes up a whole, and also a voter in a district","definitionCN":"名词 constituent 指构成整体的一个成分，也指选区里的选民","example":"Protein is a key constituent of every cell.","exampleCN":"蛋白质是每个细胞的关键成分。","why":"A constituent is 'one who stands (as a part)'. The political sense extends the same idea: the voters are the parts that make up the representative body.","whyCN":"constituent 是“站立（作为一个部分）的东西”。政治义延伸了同一想法：选民正是构成代议机构的那些部分。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Constitute is Latin constituere, 'to cause to stand, set up, establish', from com- (here an intensive) + statuere 'to set', itself from stare 'to stand'. The same root gives statue, statute, institute and substitute.","cn":"constitute 来自拉丁语 constituere“使站立、设立、建立”，由 com-（此处表加强）加 statuere“放置”构成，而 statuere 又来自 stare“站立”。同一词根还给出 statue、statute、institute、substitute。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Constituere meant 'to cause to stand, set up, fix, place, establish, set in order; form something new; resolve'. It was used both of objects and of officials.","cn":"constituere 意为“使站立、设立、固定、安置、建立、整顿；形成新事物；决定”。它既用于物体，也用于官员。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Statuere 'to set, place' is built on stare 'to stand, be standing', from PIE *sta- 'to stand, make firm'. Statue and statute are its direct relatives: something stood up, or something stood as law.","cn":"statuere“放置”建立在 stare“站立”之上，后者来自原始印欧语 *sta-“站立、使牢固”。statue 与 statute 是它的直系亲属：一个是立起来的像，一个是立为法律的东西。"},{"era":"c. 1400 ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'to appoint or elect to an office or position of power' is recorded from about 1400, the earliest English use.","cn":"“任命或选举某人担任有权力的职位”这一义项约在 1400 年被记录，是英语中最早的用法。"},{"era":"MID-15C ENGLISH","en":"From the mid-15c. comes 'to enter into the formation of as a necessary part' — the modern 'make up, compose' sense.","cn":"15 世纪中期出现“作为必要部分参与形成”的义项，即现代的“构成、组成”。"},{"era":"14C–1730s ENGLISH","en":"Constitution first meant 'law, regulation, body of rules' (mid-14c.), then 'the way a thing is constituted' (c. 1600) and 'physical health' (1550s). The political sense of a written fundamental law dates from the 1730s.","cn":"constitution 最初指“法律、规章、规则体系”（14 世纪中期），再指“事物被构成的方式”（约 1600 年）和“身体健康”（16 世纪 50 年代）。作为成文根本法的政治义则始于 18 世纪 30 年代。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern legal and academic English keeps both halves: constitute a committee (set up) and constitute a breach (amount to). The participle constituted and the noun constituent carry the same 'standing' image.","cn":"现代法律与学术英语保留了两半：constitute a committee（设立委员会）与 constitute a breach（构成违约）。分词 constituted 和名词 constituent 都带着同一个“站立”意象。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is built on the same Latin statuere family; the near-meaning group separates verbs that also describe parts and wholes.","cn":"形近组建立在同一个拉丁语 statuere 词族上；近义组区分同样描述“部分与整体”的动词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"constituent","ipa":"/kənˈstɪtjuənt/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"a part that makes up a whole, or a voter. It is the present participle of the Latin verb used as a noun.","definitionCN":"构成整体的成分，或选民。它是拉丁动词的现在分词用作名词。"},{"word":"substitute","ipa":"/səbˈstɪtjuːt/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to put one thing in place of another. Sub- 'under, in place of' + statuere 'set' — something is set in another's place.","definitionCN":"用一物替代另一物。sub-“在下面、代替”加 statuere“放置”——把某物放到另一物的位置上。"},{"word":"construe","ipa":"/kənˈstruː/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to interpret or understand in a particular way. Its root is struere 'pile up', not statuere, so it means 'build a reading', not 'set up'.","definitionCN":"以某种方式解释或理解。它的词根是 struere“堆起”，不是 statuere，所以意思是“搭出一种读法”，而不是“设立”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"comprise","ipa":"/kəmˈpraɪz/","tag":"whole contains parts","definition":"to consist of; to have as parts. The subject is the whole, and the parts follow, the reverse of 'parts constitute the whole'.","definitionCN":"由……组成；包含这些部分。主语是整体，部分是宾语，正好与“部分构成整体”相反。"},{"word":"compose","ipa":"/kəmˈpəʊz/","tag":"parts make whole","definition":"of parts, to make up a whole. It is close to constitute but more often used of physical or artistic wholes.","definitionCN":"（部分）组成整体。它与 constitute 接近，但更常用于物理或艺术上的整体。"},{"word":"establish","ipa":"/ɪˈstæblɪʃ/","tag":"set up","definition":"to set something up permanently. It stresses lasting foundation, while constitute can also mean 'amount to'.","definitionCN":"永久地建立某物。它强调持久的基础，而 constitute 还可以表示“相当于”。"},{"word":"amount to","ipa":"/əˈmaʊnt tuː/","tag":"count as","definition":"to be equal to or count as something in effect. It overlaps with constitute in legal and formal writing.","definitionCN":"在效果上等于或算作某事物。它在法律和正式写作中与 constitute 重叠。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: con- 'together', statuere 'set', the relatives statue, statute and substitute, and the modern legal phrases constitute a committee and constitute a breach.","cn":"只用真实构件：con-“一起”、statuere“放置”，同族词 statue、statute、substitute，以及现代法律短语 constitute a committee、constitute a breach。"},"normal":[{"en":"Con- 'together' + statuere 'set': the parts are set down together, and a whole stands up.","cn":"con-“一起”加 statuere“放置”：各部分被一起摆好，一个整体就立起来了。"},{"en":"Statue, statute and substitute are all relatives: a statue is stood up, a statute is stood as law, a substitute is set in someone's place.","cn":"statue、statute、substitute 都是亲戚：雕像被立起来，法规被立为法律，替代物被放到别人的位置上。"},{"en":"Constitute and consist point in opposite directions: parts constitute the whole; the whole consists of the parts.","cn":"constitute 与 consist 指向相反：部分 constitute 整体；整体 consist of 部分。"},{"en":"Constitute a committee means 'set it up'; constitute a breach means 'amount to a breach'. The same verb covers building and counting.","cn":"constitute a committee 意为“设立委员会”；constitute a breach 意为“构成违约”。同一个动词同时覆盖“搭建”和“算作”。"},{"en":"Constitution is the frame that was set up first, so all other laws have somewhere to stand.","cn":"constitution 是最先立好的框架，其他一切法律因此才有地方站立。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture three blocks set down in order until they hold up an arch. Constitute is that last setting-down that turns separate pieces into one structure.","cn":"想象三块积木按顺序摆好，直到撑起一道拱门。constitute 就是最后那次“放好”，把分散的块变成一座结构。"},{"en":"The same gesture can set up a physical whole, a legal body, a person in office, or a fact that counts as a breach.","cn":"同一个动作可以立起一个实物整体、一个法律团体、一个任职的人，或一个算作违约的事实。"},{"en":"The word always looks from the parts toward the whole; that is why the passive 'be constituted of' reverses the subject and sounds natural.","cn":"这个词总是从部分看向整体；所以被动式 be constituted of 把主语反过来，读起来依然自然。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Women constitute nearly half of the workforce here.","cn":"女性构成了这里近一半的劳动力。"},{"en":"The delay constituted a serious breach of the agreement.","cn":"这次延误构成了对协议的严重违反。"},{"en":"The university was constituted by royal charter in 1836.","cn":"这所大学于 1836 年依据皇家特许状设立。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·斯提·求特”——肯（定）把斯提（这）求（来的）特（殊）人选安进班子 → constitute 组成、设立、任命","word":"constitute"},"root":"源自拉丁语 constituere“使站立、设立”，由 com-“一起”（或表加强）+ statuere“放置”构成，而 statuere 又出自 stare“站立”，核心是“把各部分摆到一起立起来”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of constitute, all built on setting something in place. Parts are set into a whole, a body is set up as an institution, a person is set into office, and a fact is set down as something that counts.","cn":"constitute 的九个义项都建立在“把某物安放到位”上。部分被安进整体，团体被立为机构，人被安进职位，事实被摆成一个“算作”的东西。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: blocks set down one by one until they stand as one structure.","cn":"核心意象：积木一块块被放好，直到它们作为一座结构立起来。"},"chain":["PARTS","SET IN PLACE","STAND TOGETHER","WHOLE","OFFICIAL BODY","WHAT IT COUNTS AS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 06","en":"MATERIAL AND PERSONAL WHOLES: parts or qualities are set together to form a vessel, a board, a body or a character.","cn":"物质与人的整体：部分或品质被摆到一起，形成器物、委员会、身体或性格。"},{"senses":"02","en":"COUNTING AS: once the parts are set into one unit, the law or logic names what that unit amounts to.","cn":"算作：部分一旦被立成一个单元，法律或逻辑就为这个单元命名，说明它相当于什么。"},{"senses":"03 · 05 · 07","en":"INSTITUTIONS: a committee or district is made to stand on its own feet, and constituted marks the finished state.","cn":"机构：委员会或区划被立起来独立站住，而 constituted 标记这一完成状态。"},{"senses":"04","en":"OFFICE: a person is set into a seat of authority, the oldest English sense of the verb.","cn":"职位：人被安放到权威的座位上，这是该动词最古老的英语义项。"},{"senses":"08 · 09","en":"THE FRAME AND THE PARTS: constitution is the frame set up first, and constituent is any part that stands inside it, including a voter.","cn":"框架与部分：constitution 是最先立好的框架，constituent 是站在框架里的任何部分，包括选民。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Constitute is a Latin verb whose English derivatives are transparent: -tion, -tional, -ent, -ency and the negative un-. The stat- root stays visible in every one.","cn":"constitute 是一个拉丁动词，其英语派生结构清晰：-tion、-tional、-ent、-ency 以及否定前缀 un-。stat- 词根在每个派生词里都看得见。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is large and real: constituere, constitutio, constituens, statuere, stare, statutum and substituere. English borrowed several of them twice, directly and through French.","cn":"拉丁词族庞大而真实：constituere、constitutio、constituens、statuere、stare、statutum、substituere。英语曾两次借入其中若干词——直接借入和经法语借入。"},"items":[{"word":"constitute","structure":"con- (together, intensive) + statu- (set) + -e (verb)","meaning":"to set up, make up, or amount to","meaningCN":"构成；设立；相当于","example":"These four states constitute the region.","exampleCN":"这四个州构成了该地区。"},{"word":"constitution","structure":"constitute + -ion (noun of action or result)","meaning":"the act of constituting; a body of fundamental rules; a person's health","meaningCN":"构成；宪法；体质（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The constitution was amended in 1998.","exampleCN":"宪法于 1998 年修订。"},{"word":"constitutional","structure":"constitution + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to the constitution; allowed by it","meaningCN":"宪法的；合宪的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The court ruled the law constitutional.","exampleCN":"法院裁定该法律合宪。"},{"word":"unconstitutional","structure":"un- (not) + constitutional","meaning":"not allowed by the constitution","meaningCN":"违宪的（un- 表否定）","example":"The search was ruled unconstitutional.","exampleCN":"该搜查被裁定违宪。"},{"word":"constituent","structure":"con- + statu- + -ent (present participle)","meaning":"a part that makes up a whole; a voter","meaningCN":"成分；选民（-ent 构成分词与名词）","example":"Sulfur is a constituent of the alloy.","exampleCN":"硫是这种合金的一种成分。"},{"word":"constituency","structure":"constituent + -ency (collective noun)","meaning":"the body of voters in a district, or the district itself","meaningCN":"选区；选民群体（-ency 构成集合名词）","example":"The senator met voters across her constituency.","exampleCN":"参议员在她的选区各处会见选民。"},{"word":"constitutive","structure":"constitute + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"forming an essential part; having power to establish","meaningCN":"构成性的；有设立效力的","example":"Language is constitutive of human identity.","exampleCN":"语言对人的身份具有构成作用。"},{"word":"constituted","structure":"constitute + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"formally set up or appointed","meaningCN":"已成立的；被任命的","example":"The duly constituted authority took over.","exampleCN":"依法成立的当局接管了事务。"},{"word":"reconstitute","structure":"re- (again) + constitute","meaning":"to form again; to restore by adding water","meaningCN":"重新组成；加水复原（re- 表再次）","example":"Reconstitute the powder with warm water.","exampleCN":"用温水把粉末冲开复原。"},{"word":"statute","structure":"statutum (that which is set up) + -e","meaning":"a written law set up by authority","meaningCN":"成文法；法规（同一词根的近亲）","example":"The statute applies to all employers.","exampleCN":"该法规适用于所有雇主。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"constituere","structure":"con- + statuere","meaning":"to cause to stand, set up, establish","meaningCN":"使站立；设立；建立"},{"word":"statuere","structure":"from stare","meaning":"to set, place, fix, decide","meaningCN":"放置；固定；决定"},{"word":"stare","structure":"PIE *sta-","meaning":"to stand, be standing","meaningCN":"站立"},{"word":"constituens","structure":"present participle of constituere","meaning":"the part that sets up or makes up a whole","meaningCN":"构成整体的部分"}]}},{"word":"constrain","ipa_uk":"/kənˈstreɪn/","ipa_us":"/kənˈstreɪn/","definition_zh":"强迫；限制；约束；束缚","definition_en":"to force someone to do something, or to limit and restrict what someone or something can do","core_image":"一根绷紧的绳子把箱子牢牢捆在柱子上，绳子越勒越紧","scene":"货车上，两根绷紧的绑带把木箱死死压住，司机说：The straps constrain the load so it cannot shift.","sceneCN":"这里 constrain 是「物理束缚、限制移动」（第 2、3、5 个义项：把东西限制在范围内、用外力捆住）；句意：绑带把货物固定住，使其无法移动。图中可辨识物件：货车、木箱、尼龙绑带、司机。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"强迫；迫使；限制；约束"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"束缚；压制（行动或表达）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"be constrained by","zh":"受……限制；受……约束"},{"phrase":"constrain growth","zh":"抑制增长"},{"phrase":"constrain someone to do","zh":"迫使某人做某事"},{"phrase":"financial constraints","zh":"财务限制；资金约束"},{"phrase":"a constrained style","zh":"拘谨的文风"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"constrains"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"constrained"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"constrained"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"constraining"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"constraint","pos":"n.","zh":"限制；约束；拘束"},{"word":"constrained","pos":"adj.","zh":"受限制的；拘谨的；不自然的"},{"word":"unconstrained","pos":"adj.","zh":"不受约束的；自由的"},{"word":"constriction","pos":"n.","zh":"压缩；收紧；狭窄处"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Force someone to act","titleCN":"强迫：外力推着人去做","definition":"to compel a person to do something, whether by authority, necessity or pressure","definitionCN":"以权威、必要性或压力迫使一个人做某事","example":"Illness constrained him to give up the trip.","exampleCN":"疾病迫使他放弃了这次旅行。","why":"Latin constringere meant 'to bind tightly, fetter'. A bound person has no choice of movement, so the verb naturally covers 'force to act' as well as 'prevent from acting'.","whyCN":"拉丁语 constringere 意为“紧紧捆住、上镣铐”。被捆住的人没有行动自由，所以这个动词既覆盖“迫使行动”，也覆盖“阻止行动”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Limit what can happen","titleCN":"限制：给可能性画一条边界","definition":"to limit the size, amount, range or speed of something","definitionCN":"限制某物的大小、数量、范围或速度","example":"A small budget constrained the design from the start.","exampleCN":"预算有限，从一开始就限制了设计。","why":"The rope image turns abstract: a budget, a rule or a deadline can act as a rope around a project, holding it inside a boundary.","whyCN":"绳子的意象变得抽象：预算、规则或截止日期都能成为项目周围的绳子，把它圈在边界之内。"},{"no":"03","title":"Hold physically: tied or bound","titleCN":"物理束缚：被绑住、被固定","definition":"to hold a body or object physically, so that it cannot move freely","definitionCN":"在物理上固定住身体或物体，使其无法自由移动","example":"The patient's arms were constrained by soft straps.","exampleCN":"病人的双臂被软带固定住。","why":"This is the original bodily sense of constringere: stringere means 'draw tight', and the strap is drawn tight around the body.","whyCN":"这是 constringere 最初的肉体义：stringere 意为“拉紧”，绑带被拉紧缠在身上。"},{"no":"04","title":"Restrict freedom of action","titleCN":"制约：条件压住行动空间","definition":"of conditions, rules or circumstances, to make action narrower or harder","definitionCN":"（条件、规则或环境）压缩行动空间，使行动更窄或更难","example":"He felt constrained by what his family expected of him.","exampleCN":"他感到被家人的期望所束缚。","why":"Social expectations work exactly like a rope: nothing visible touches you, yet the range of possible moves is narrowed.","whyCN":"社会期望的作用就像绳子：看不见任何东西碰到你，可移动的范围却被缩小了。"},{"no":"05","title":"Tighten or narrow a space","titleCN":"收紧：把空间或通道勒窄","definition":"to make a passage, opening or movement narrower or tighter","definitionCN":"使通道、开口或运动变得更窄、更紧","example":"The narrow doorway constrained the flow of people.","exampleCN":"狭窄的门洞限制了人流的通行。","why":"When a tight band presses inward, the space inside shrinks. Constrict is the direct Latin doublet used for this physical squeezing.","whyCN":"当紧箍向内压时，内部空间就变小。constrict 是同一拉丁词直接借入的双式词，专门用于这种物理挤压。"},{"no":"06","title":"Constrained: forced and unnatural","titleCN":"constrained：拘谨的、不自然的","definition":"the adjective describes behaviour, style or a smile that looks forced rather than free","definitionCN":"形容词指行为、文风或笑容显得勉强、不自然，而非自在","example":"She gave a constrained smile and said nothing.","exampleCN":"她勉强笑了笑，什么也没说。","why":"A person who is held in by invisible ropes moves carefully. The participle keeps that physical picture: the movement is correct but not free.","whyCN":"被无形绳索束住的人动作会小心翼翼。分词保留了这幅画面：动作正确，却不自由。"},{"no":"07","title":"Constraint: the rope itself","titleCN":"constraint：限制条件本身","definition":"the noun for a rule, limit or condition that keeps something within bounds","definitionCN":"指把某物限制在范围内的规则、限度或条件","example":"Time and money are the main constraints on the project.","exampleCN":"时间和金钱是这个项目的主要限制条件。","why":"The -t noun turns the act of binding into the thing that binds. A constraint is the rope, not the pulling.","whyCN":"-t 名词把“捆”这个动作变成“捆的东西”。constraint 是那根绳子，而不是拉绳的动作。"},{"no":"08","title":"Constrain a variable in science","titleCN":"科学中的约束：给变量加限定","definition":"in mathematics, engineering and statistics, to restrict a variable or parameter to a set of allowed values","definitionCN":"在数学、工程与统计中，把变量或参数限制在允许的取值范围内","example":"The model constrains the temperature to stay above zero.","exampleCN":"该模型把温度约束在零度以上。","why":"A mathematical constraint is a boundary drawn around possible values, the same boundary a rope draws around a body.","whyCN":"数学上的约束就是画在可能取值周围的边界，与绳子在身体周围画出的边界完全相同。"},{"no":"09","title":"Constrain a feeling or a sound","titleCN":"抑制：把情绪或声音压回去","definition":"to hold back an emotion, a reaction or a sound so that it does not show","definitionCN":"压住情绪、反应或声音，使其不外露","example":"He constrained his anger until the meeting ended.","exampleCN":"他压住怒火，直到会议结束。","why":"A feeling that is held in is literally kept inside the body by tension, which is why constrain can mean suppress rather than merely limit.","whyCN":"被“收住”的情绪 literally 靠身体的紧张被关在里面，所以 constrain 可以表示“压抑”，而不只是“限制”。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Constrain came through Old French from Latin constringere 'to bind together, tie tightly, fetter'. Its root stringere 'draw tight' also gives strict, strain, restrict and constrict, so the whole family is about tightening.","cn":"constrain 经古法语来自拉丁语 constringere“捆在一起、紧紧绑住、上镣铐”。其词根 stringere“拉紧”还给出 strict、strain、restrict、constrict，整个词族都围绕“收紧”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Constringere meant 'to bind together, tie tightly, fetter, shackle, chain', from com- 'together' + stringere 'to draw tight, compress'.","cn":"constringere 意为“捆在一起、紧紧绑住、上镣铐、加锁链”，由 com-“一起”加 stringere“拉紧、压缩”构成。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Stringere is reconstructed to PIE *streig- 'to stroke, rub, press'. The reconstruction is standard but unattested, so the deepest step is a scholarly reconstruction rather than a recorded word.","cn":"stringere 被重构为原始印欧语 *streig-“抚摸、摩擦、压”。该重构是通行的，但没有书面记录，因此最深一步是学术重构而非有记载的词。"},{"era":"EARLY 14C ENGLISH","en":"English recorded constreyen in the early 14th century, from the stem of Old French constreindre, meaning both 'urge to action' and 'restrain from it'.","cn":"英语在 14 世纪早期记录 constreyen，来自古法语 constreindre 的词干，同时表示“催促行动”和“阻止行动”两个方向。"},{"era":"14C–16C ENGLISH","en":"The 'restrain, confine' branch grew stronger, and by the 16th century constrain was the ordinary verb for limiting movement or behaviour.","cn":"“抑制、限制”这一支逐渐增强，到 16 世纪，constrain 已成为表示限制移动或行为的常用动词。"},{"era":"c. 1600–1732","en":"Constringe (c. 1600) and constrict (1732, a back-formation from constriction) are the learned doublets of the same Latin word, used mainly for physical squeezing.","cn":"constringe（约 1600 年）与 constrict（1732 年，由 constriction 逆构）是同一个拉丁词的学术双式词，主要用于物理挤压。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English splits the work: constrain for abstract limits and forced behaviour, constrict for tubes and passages, and constraint for the limit itself.","cn":"现代英语分工明确：constrain 用于抽象限制与被迫行为，constrict 用于管道与通道，constraint 指限制本身。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group contains a different-root neighbour and two same-root doublets; the near-meaning group separates force from limit.","cn":"形近组包含一个异根近邻和两个同根双式词；近义组把“强迫”与“限制”分开。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"construct","ipa":"/kənˈstrʌkt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to build or put together. Its root is struere 'pile up', not stringere 'draw tight', so it builds rather than binds.","definitionCN":"建造；组装。它的词根是 struere“堆起”，不是 stringere“拉紧”，所以它是“搭起来”而不是“捆起来”。"},{"word":"constrict","ipa":"/kənˈstrɪkt/","tag":"same root, doublet","definition":"to make narrower by squeezing. It is the direct Latin borrowing of the same word that became constrain through French.","definitionCN":"挤压使变窄。它是同一个拉丁词直接借入英语的形式，而 constrain 是经法语传来的。"},{"word":"construe","ipa":"/kənˈstruː/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to interpret words or actions in a particular way. It comes from construere 'build', so it means 'build a meaning'.","definitionCN":"以特定方式解释词语或行为。它来自 construere“建造”，意思是“搭出一种意义”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"compel","ipa":"/kəmˈpel/","tag":"force to act","definition":"to force someone to do something. It is stronger and more formal than constrain and focuses on the pressure to act.","definitionCN":"强迫某人做某事。它比 constrain 更强、更正式，聚焦于“促使人行动”的压力。"},{"word":"restrain","ipa":"/rɪˈstreɪn/","tag":"hold back","definition":"to stop someone or something from acting. Re- 'back' marks the direction: holding back, whereas constrain presses from outside.","definitionCN":"阻止某人或某物行动。re-“向后”标出方向：往回拉住，而 constrain 是从外部压住。"},{"word":"restrict","ipa":"/rɪˈstrɪkt/","tag":"set limits","definition":"to keep something within fixed limits. It is the everyday word for rules and access, and less forceful than constrain.","definitionCN":"把某物保持在固定限度内。它是规则与权限方面的日常用词，力度弱于 constrain。"},{"word":"confine","ipa":"/kənˈfaɪn/","tag":"keep inside","definition":"to keep someone or something inside a space or a set of limits. It stresses the boundary rather than the pulling tight.","definitionCN":"把某人或某物关在某个空间或限度内。它强调边界，而不是“拉紧”。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: stringere 'draw tight', the same-root family strict, strain, restrict, constrict, and the noun constraint.","cn":"只用真实构件：stringere“拉紧”，同根词族 strict、strain、restrict、constrict，以及名词 constraint。"},"normal":[{"en":"Stringere means 'draw tight'. Constrain is to draw a tight band around someone's choices.","cn":"stringere 意为“拉紧”。constrain 就是在人的选择周围拉上一道紧箍。"},{"en":"Strict, strain, restrict, constrict, district and stringent all belong to this tightening family; each narrows something in its own way.","cn":"strict、strain、restrict、constrict、district、stringent 都属于这个“收紧”词族，各自以自己的方式把某物收窄。"},{"en":"Constrain and restrain pull in opposite directions: constrain presses you toward or inside a limit, restrain holds you back from acting.","cn":"constrain 与 restrain 的用力方向相反：constrain 把你压向或压进某个限度，restrain 则把你往回拉住、不让行动。"},{"en":"A constraint is the rope itself; a constrained smile is the result of the rope being there.","cn":"constraint 是绳子本身；constrained smile 是绳子存在造成的结果。"},{"en":"In science a constraint is a boundary on allowed values, which is exactly a rope drawn around a set of numbers.","cn":"科学中的 constraint 是允许取值上的边界，字面上就是在一组数字周围拉起的绳子。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a box tied to a post with one tight strap. Nothing is hurt, but every possible movement is now a smaller set.","cn":"想象一个箱子被一根紧带捆在柱子上。什么都没受伤，但所有可能的移动都变成了一个更小的集合。"},{"en":"The strap can be physical (a seatbelt), social (expectations), financial (a budget) or mathematical (a parameter range).","cn":"这根带子可以是物理的（安全带）、社会的（期望）、财务的（预算）或数学的（参数范围）。"},{"en":"Because the word names both the pressure and the boundary, English can constrain a person, a project, a variable or a smile with one verb.","cn":"因为这个词同时命名压力和边界，英语可以用一个动词 constrain 人、项目、变量或笑容。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Lack of funding constrained the scope of the study.","cn":"资金不足限制了这项研究的范围。"},{"en":"She felt constrained by the rules of the old laboratory.","cn":"她感到被旧实验室的规矩束缚。"},{"en":"The valve constrains the flow of water into the tank.","cn":"阀门控制进入水箱的水流。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·斯专”——肯（定）用斯（绳）专（门）把箱子捆紧在柱子上 → constrain 束缚、限制","word":"constrain"},"root":"源自拉丁语 constringere“捆紧、上镣铐”，由 com-“一起”+ stringere“拉紧”构成，核心是“用外力把范围勒紧”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of constrain, all built on one tight strap. It can press a person to act, fence a project in, bind a body, squeeze a passage, or hold a feeling inside; the strap changes material, not shape.","cn":"constrain 的九个义项都建立在一根绷紧的带子上。它可以逼人行动、把项目圈住、捆住身体、勒窄通道，或把情绪压在里面；变化的只是带子的材质，形状始终一样。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one strap drawn tight around a box, making every movement smaller.","cn":"核心意象：一根带子紧紧勒住箱子，使每一种移动都变小。"},"chain":["SLACK","DRAW TIGHT","NO FREE MOVEMENT","LIMIT","FORCE A DIRECTION","THE LIMIT ITSELF"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"PRESSURE ON PEOPLE: authority, illness or expectations push a person toward one action or away from others.","cn":"对人的压力：权威、疾病或期望把人推向某个行动，或推离其他行动。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"BOUNDARIES ON POSSIBILITY: budgets, rules and parameter ranges draw a line around what can happen.","cn":"可能性的边界：预算、规则与参数范围在“能发生什么”周围画出界线。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"PHYSICAL BINDING: straps, narrow doorways and constricted tubes show the strap literally.","cn":"物理束缚：绑带、狭窄门洞与收缩的管道把“带子”直接呈现出来。"},{"senses":"06 · 09","en":"WHAT THE STRAP DOES TO THE SELF: behaviour becomes stiff and a feeling is held inside.","cn":"带子对自我的作用：行为变得拘谨，情绪被收在里面。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE STRAP AS OBJECT: constraint is the limit itself rather than the act of limiting.","cn":"作为物体的带子：constraint 指限制本身，而不是施加限制的动作。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Constrain has an unusually clear Latin skeleton: con- + string- + -ain (French verb ending). Its English derivatives add -t, -ed, un- and the learned doublets constrict and constringe.","cn":"constrain 的拉丁骨架异常清晰：con- + string- + -ain（法语动词词尾）。英语派生词加 -t、-ed、un-，以及学术双式词 constrict、constringe。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin stringere family is broad and real: strictus 'drawn tight', constringere, restringere, districtus, and stringens 'binding'. English took some directly and some through French.","cn":"拉丁 stringere 词族庞大而真实：strictus“拉紧的”、constringere、restringere、districtus、stringens“束紧的”。英语有的直接借入，有的经法语借入。"},"items":[{"word":"constrain","structure":"con- (together) + string- (draw tight) + -ain (verb ending)","meaning":"to force, limit or bind","meaningCN":"强迫；限制；束缚","example":"Rules constrain how the money is spent.","exampleCN":"规则限制了这笔钱的使用方式。"},{"word":"constraint","structure":"constrain + -t (noun of result)","meaning":"a limit or restriction","meaningCN":"限制；约束（-t 构成名词）","example":"Space is the main constraint on the design.","exampleCN":"空间是这项设计的主要限制。"},{"word":"constrained","structure":"constrain + -ed (past participle and adjective)","meaning":"limited, or forced and unnatural","meaningCN":"受限制的；拘谨的（-ed 构成分词与形容词）","example":"His voice sounded constrained.","exampleCN":"他的声音听起来很拘谨。"},{"word":"constraining","structure":"constrain + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"acting as a limit; restricting","meaningCN":"起限制作用的（-ing 构成现在分词）","example":"The rules are constraining but fair.","exampleCN":"这些规则虽有约束，但公平。"},{"word":"unconstrained","structure":"un- (not) + constrained","meaning":"free from limits","meaningCN":"不受约束的；自由的（un- 表否定）","example":"She laughed with unconstrained delight.","exampleCN":"她毫无拘束地开心大笑。"},{"word":"constrict","structure":"con- + strict- (drawn tight) + -Ø","meaning":"to squeeze or make narrower","meaningCN":"压缩；使变窄（同根直接借入）","example":"Cold air constricted the pipes.","exampleCN":"冷空气使管道收缩。"},{"word":"constriction","structure":"constrict + -ion (noun)","meaning":"a narrow or squeezed place; the act of squeezing","meaningCN":"压缩；狭窄处（-ion 构成名词）","example":"A constriction in the artery blocked the flow.","exampleCN":"动脉中的一处狭窄阻断了血流。"},{"word":"constringe","structure":"con- + stringere (learned borrowing)","meaning":"to draw together, compress","meaningCN":"使收缩；压缩（学术借词）","example":"The muscle constringes the duct.","exampleCN":"肌肉使导管收缩。"},{"word":"strict","structure":"strictus (drawn tight, past participle)","meaning":"demanding tight obedience to rules","meaningCN":"严格的（同一词根的形容词）","example":"The school has strict rules about lateness.","exampleCN":"这所学校对迟到有严格规定。"},{"word":"restrict","structure":"re- (back) + string- + -t","meaning":"to keep within limits","meaningCN":"限制；限定（同根，re- 表向后）","example":"Access is restricted to staff.","exampleCN":"仅限员工进入。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"constringere","structure":"con- + stringere","meaning":"to bind together, tie tightly, fetter","meaningCN":"捆在一起；紧紧绑住；上镣铐"},{"word":"stringere","structure":"PIE *streig- (reconstructed)","meaning":"to draw tight, compress, touch lightly","meaningCN":"拉紧；压缩；轻触"},{"word":"strictus","structure":"past participle of stringere","meaning":"drawn tight; strict","meaningCN":"拉紧的；严格的"}]}},{"word":"construct","ipa_uk":"/kənˈstrʌkt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈstrʌkt/","definition_zh":"建造；构建；构造；构想；（思维或语言）建构体","definition_en":"to build something by putting parts together, or an idea, sentence or object that is formed that way","core_image":"一根根钢梁被吊起、对齐、拼成完整的桥架","scene":"河岸工地上，吊车把钢梁一根根放到桥墩上，工人用螺栓固定。工头说：They construct the bridge piece by piece.","sceneCN":"这里 construct 是「按部件搭建实体结构」（第 1 个义项：把各部分拼装起来）；句意：他们一段一段地建造这座桥。图中可辨识物件：吊车、钢梁、桥墩、螺栓、工人。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"建造；构建；构作；组成"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"建构体；概念结构；构式（重音在前）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"construct a bridge","zh":"建造一座桥"},{"phrase":"construct a theory","zh":"构建一套理论"},{"phrase":"construct an argument","zh":"组织一个论证"},{"phrase":"social construct","zh":"社会建构"},{"phrase":"construct validity","zh":"构念效度"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"constructs"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"constructed"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"constructed"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"constructing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"construction","pos":"n.","zh":"建造；建筑业；结构；解释"},{"word":"constructive","pos":"adj.","zh":"建设性的；有助益的"},{"word":"reconstruction","pos":"n.","zh":"重建；复原；重构"},{"word":"constructor","pos":"n.","zh":"建造者；构造函数"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Build by putting parts together","titleCN":"建造：把部件拼成实体","definition":"to build a physical structure by assembling materials in a planned order","definitionCN":"按计划顺序组装材料，建成实体结构","example":"The company constructed a new terminal in two years.","exampleCN":"这家公司用两年建成了一座新航站楼。","why":"Latin construere is com- 'together' + struere 'to pile up'. Building is literally piling materials in an ordered stack until the structure stands.","whyCN":"拉丁语 construere 由 com-“一起”加 struere“堆起”构成。建造就是把材料按顺序堆叠，直到结构立起来。"},{"no":"02","title":"Build in the mind: devise a theory or model","titleCN":"构想：在头脑中搭出理论或模型","definition":"to form an idea, argument, theory or system by arranging its parts deliberately","definitionCN":"有意识地安排各部分，形成想法、论证、理论或体系","example":"She constructed a model that explains the data.","exampleCN":"她构建了一个能解释这些数据的模型。","why":"The 1755 sense 'devise and form in the mind' applies the same piling to thoughts: premises are the beams, and the conclusion is the span they carry.","whyCN":"1755 年出现的“在头脑中构想”义把同样的“堆叠”用于思想：前提是钢梁，结论是它们撑起的跨度。"},{"no":"03","title":"Form a sentence or a figure by rules","titleCN":"按规则构造句子或图形","definition":"in grammar and geometry, to form a sentence or figure according to a fixed set of rules","definitionCN":"在语法和几何中，按一套固定规则造出句子或图形","example":"Students were asked to construct a sentence with the passive voice.","exampleCN":"学生被要求用被动语态造一个句子。","why":"Grammar and geometry both give you parts and rules for joining them; 'construct' marks the rule-governed joining rather than free invention.","whyCN":"语法和几何都给出部件与拼接规则；construct 标记的是受规则支配的拼接，而不是自由发明。"},{"no":"04","title":"A construct: an idea built by the mind","titleCN":"construct（名词）：头脑搭出的概念","definition":"a noun for an idea or category that the mind builds rather than finds ready-made in nature","definitionCN":"名词，指由头脑搭建、而非在自然中现成存在的观念或类别","example":"'Race' is a social construct, not a biological fact.","exampleCN":"“种族”是一种社会建构，而不是生物学事实。","why":"The noun sense appeared in psychology in 1890 for 'an object in the mind formed by sense-impressions'. What the mind assembles is a construct.","whyCN":"名词义 1890 年出现在心理学中，指“由感官印象在头脑中形成的对象”。头脑组装出来的东西就是 construct。"},{"no":"05","title":"A construction in language","titleCN":"语言中的构式、句法结构","definition":"in linguistics, a phrase or pattern whose parts are combined according to grammar","definitionCN":"语言学中按语法组合起来的短语或句式","example":"The 'verb + object' construction is common in English.","exampleCN":"“动词 + 宾语”这一构式在英语中很常见。","why":"The first noun use (1871) was exactly this: 'a group of words forming a phrase'. Words are piled into a pattern, so the pattern is a construct.","whyCN":"最早的名词用法（1871 年）正是这个意思：“构成短语的一组词”。词被堆进一个模式，这个模式就是一个 construct。"},{"no":"06","title":"Constructed: made rather than natural","titleCN":"constructed：人为构造的","definition":"the adjective describes something deliberately made or artificially arranged","definitionCN":"形容词指有意制造或人为安排的事物","example":"The whole scene was carefully constructed for the camera.","exampleCN":"整个场景都是为镜头精心构造出来的。","why":"The participle marks the result of assembly: whatever stands there did not grow, it was put together.","whyCN":"分词标记组装的结果：立在那里的东西不是长出来的，而是被拼出来的。"},{"no":"07","title":"Reconstruct: build again","titleCN":"reconstruct：重建、复原","definition":"to build something again after it has been destroyed, or to rebuild an event in thought","definitionCN":"在被毁之后重新建造，或在思想中重建一个事件","example":"Historians reconstructed the route from old letters.","exampleCN":"历史学家根据旧书信重建了那条路线。","why":"Re- adds 'again' to the same piling. Whether the materials are bricks or clues, the method is to put the pieces back in order.","whyCN":"re- 给同一个“堆叠”加上“再次”。无论材料是砖块还是线索，方法都是把碎片按顺序放回去。"},{"no":"08","title":"Construction: the process, the industry, the reading","titleCN":"construction：建造过程、建筑业、解释","definition":"the noun covers the act of building, the trade that builds, the built structure, and the act of interpreting words","definitionCN":"名词覆盖建造行为、建筑行业、建成的结构，以及解释词语的行为","example":"The bridge is still under construction.","exampleCN":"这座桥仍在施工中。","why":"The 'interpretation' sense comes from the doublet construe, which meant 'arrange words in their natural order'. Even reading is a building of meaning.","whyCN":"“解释”这一义来自双式词 construe，原意是“把词语按自然顺序排好”。连阅读也是在对意义进行搭建。"},{"no":"09","title":"Constructive: building up, not tearing down","titleCN":"constructive：建设性的","definition":"helpful and improving, especially of criticism or suggestions that build rather than destroy","definitionCN":"有帮助、能改进的，尤指建设性而非破坏性的批评或建议","example":"She gave me constructive feedback on the draft.","exampleCN":"她针对草稿给了我建设性的反馈。","why":"The -ive suffix turns 'build' into a tendency: constructive remarks add something to the structure instead of knocking pieces out.","whyCN":"-ive 后缀把“建造”变成倾向：建设性的意见是在结构上添加东西，而不是把部件敲掉。"},{"no":"10","title":"Deconstruct: take apart to examine","titleCN":"deconstruct：拆解以审视","definition":"to take a text, idea or system apart in order to show how its parts were put together","definitionCN":"拆解文本、观念或体系，以显示其各部分是如何被拼起来的","example":"The essay deconstructs the advertisement's hidden assumptions.","exampleCN":"这篇文章拆解了这则广告隐藏的预设。","why":"De- 'down, apart' reverses the piling. Deconstruction is deliberately un-building: the joints are exposed by taking the structure down.","whyCN":"de-“向下、拆开”逆转了堆叠。解构就是有意地“拆建”：把结构拆下来，接缝便暴露出来。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Construct is Latin construere 'pile up together, build', from com- 'together' + struere 'to pile up'. The older English doublet construe came in the 14th century with the meaning 'interpret'; construct followed in the 17th century with the meaning 'build'.","cn":"construct 来自拉丁语 construere“堆在一起、建造”，由 com-“一起”加 struere“堆起”构成。较早的英语双式词 construe 在 14 世纪进入英语，意为“解释”；construct 则在 17 世纪带着“建造”义出现。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Construere meant 'pile up together, accumulate; build, make, erect'. It was used of walls, ships and also of arranging words.","cn":"construere 意为“堆在一起、积聚；建造、制作、竖立”。它既用于墙、船，也用于安排词语。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Struere 'to pile up' comes from PIE *streu-, an extended form of *stere- 'to spread'. The same root gives structure, instruct, obstruct and destroy's opposite, construct.","cn":"struere“堆起”来自原始印欧语 *streu-，它是 *stere-“铺开”的扩展形式。同一词根给出 structure、instruct、obstruct，以及 construct。"},{"era":"LATE 14C ENGLISH","en":"Construe entered first (late 14c.) meaning 'arrange the words of a translation in their natural order', hence 'interpret, explain'. It is the older doublet of construct.","cn":"construe 先进入英语（14 世纪晚期），意为“把译文词语按自然顺序排好”，由此引申为“解释、说明”。它是 construct 较早的双式词。"},{"era":"1660s ENGLISH","en":"Construct itself was recorded in the 1660s meaning 'put together the parts of in their proper place and order'. The physical builder's sense arrived last but became the dominant one.","cn":"construct 本身在 17 世纪 60 年代被记录，意为“把各部分按恰当位置和顺序拼起来”。实体建造义来得最晚，却成了主导义。"},{"era":"1755 ENGLISH","en":"The mental sense 'to devise and form in the mind' is from 1755. A theory is now something constructed, not merely discovered.","cn":"“在头脑中构思、形成”的思维义始于 1755 年。理论从此可以是“被建构的”，而不只是被发现的。"},{"era":"1871–1933 ENGLISH","en":"The noun arrived by stages: 1871 in linguistics ('a group of words forming a phrase'), 1890 in psychology ('an object in the mind formed by sense-impressions'), and 1933 in the general sense 'anything constructed'. The noun is stressed on the first syllable.","cn":"名词分阶段出现：1871 年用于语言学（“构成短语的一组词”），1890 年用于心理学（“由感官印象在头脑中形成的对象”），1933 年才有一般义“任何被构造之物”。名词重音在第一音节。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the con- + str- cluster, where three different Latin roots meet; the near-meaning group separates kinds of building and devising.","cn":"形近组是 con- + str- 这一簇，三个不同的拉丁词根在此相遇；近义组区分不同种类的“建造”和“构想”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"constrain","ipa":"/kənˈstreɪn/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to force or limit. Its root is stringere 'draw tight', not struere 'pile up', so it binds rather than builds.","definitionCN":"强迫；限制。它的词根是 stringere“拉紧”，不是 struere“堆起”，所以是“捆”而不是“建”。"},{"word":"construe","ipa":"/kənˈstruː/","tag":"same root, older doublet","definition":"to interpret in a particular way. It is the same Latin verb borrowed earlier, with the 'arrange words' sense surviving.","definitionCN":"以特定方式解释。它是同一个拉丁动词更早的借入形式，保留了“排列词语”的义。"},{"word":"structure","ipa":"/ˈstrʌktʃə/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"the arrangement of parts, or a built thing. It comes from Latin structura, the noun of struere.","definitionCN":"各部分的 arrangement（安排方式），或建成的物体。它来自拉丁语 structura，即 struere 的名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"build","ipa":"/bɪld/","tag":"general verb","definition":"to make something by putting materials together. It is the plain everyday word, while construct is more formal.","definitionCN":"用材料拼成某物。它是最朴素的日常词，而 construct 更正式。"},{"word":"assemble","ipa":"/əˈsembl/","tag":"parts to whole","definition":"to put separate parts together in order. It stresses the parts arriving one by one, as in a factory.","definitionCN":"把分开的部件按顺序装在一起。它强调部件一件件到位，常用于工厂。"},{"word":"erect","ipa":"/ɪˈrekt/","tag":"stand upright","definition":"to build something tall and upright. It focuses on the finished vertical stance, not on the assembly process.","definitionCN":"建造高耸直立之物。它聚焦于建成后的竖直姿态，而非组装过程。"},{"word":"devise","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪz/","tag":"mental creation","definition":"to invent a plan or method in the mind. It overlaps with construct only in the mental sense, and has no physical use.","definitionCN":"在头脑中发明计划或方法。它只在思维义上与 construct 重叠，没有物理用法。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: struere 'pile up', the same-root family structure, instruct, obstruct, reconstruct, and the older doublet construe.","cn":"只用真实构件：struere“堆起”，同根词族 structure、instruct、obstruct、reconstruct，以及较早的双式词 construe。"},"normal":[{"en":"Struere means 'pile up'. Construct is ordered piling: beams, bricks, premises or words stacked until they hold together.","cn":"struere 意为“堆起”。construct 是有序的堆叠：钢梁、砖块、前提或词语被堆到能彼此支撑为止。"},{"en":"Structure is the noun of the same verb: it is the arrangement the piling produced.","cn":"structure 是同一个动词的名词：它就是堆叠产生出来的安排方式。"},{"en":"Instruct is 'build into' someone's mind, obstruct is 'build against' the way, and deconstruct is 'un-build'.","cn":"instruct 是“搭进”某人的头脑，obstruct 是“挡在”路上搭，deconstruct 则是“拆掉”搭好的东西。"},{"en":"Construct, constrain and constitute look alike but do different work: construct builds, constrain binds, constitute makes up or sets up.","cn":"construct、constrain、constitute 形似而分工不同：construct 建，constrain 捆，constitute 组成或设立。"},{"en":"As a noun, construct is stressed con-TRACT style: CON-struct. The verb is con-STRUCT.","cn":"作名词时重音在前：CON-struct；作动词时重音在后：con-STRUCT。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a crane placing beams one by one. Nothing exists until the last piece finds its place; construct names the whole act of ordering.","cn":"想象吊车一根根放下钢梁。直到最后一块找到位置，东西才真正存在；construct 命名的是整个安排过程。"},{"en":"The same ordering happens with thoughts: premises are placed, and a conclusion appears where no single premise had it.","cn":"同样的安排在思想中也发生：前提被安放好，结论便出现在任何单个前提都不曾有的位置上。"},{"en":"A social construct is a structure built by people and then mistaken for a natural object, which is why the word carries a hint of 'made, not given'.","cn":"社会建构是人搭起来的结构，却被误当成自然物；所以这个词总带一点“是人造的，不是天给的”意味。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Engineers constructed the tunnel through solid rock.","cn":"工程师们开凿坚硬的岩石建成了这条隧道。"},{"en":"The committee constructed a budget from last year's figures.","cn":"委员会根据去年的数字编制了一份预算。"},{"en":"Gender is often described as a social construct.","cn":"性别常被描述为一种社会建构。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·斯抓克特”——肯（定）把斯（钢）抓（起）克（服）特（重）的梁一根根拼上 → construct 建造、构建","word":"construct"},"root":"源自拉丁语 construere“堆起、建造”，由 com-“一起”+ struere“堆起”构成，核心是“把材料按顺序堆叠成结构”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses of construct, all built on piling parts in order. Steel beams, premises, sentence patterns and social categories are each assembled from smaller pieces, and the noun construct names whatever the assembling produced.","cn":"construct 的十个义项都建立在“把部件按顺序堆起来”上。钢梁、前提、句式和社会类别都由更小的片段组装而成，名词 construct 则命名组装所产生的东西。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: beams lifted one by one and fixed in place until they span a gap.","cn":"核心意象：钢梁一根根被吊起、固定到位，直到跨过缺口。"},"chain":["PARTS","ORDER","PILE / JOIN","STRUCTURE STANDS","MENTAL BUILDING","THE BUILT THING"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"PHYSICAL BUILDING: materials are assembled, and reconstruction repeats the assembly after destruction.","cn":"实体建造：材料被组装起来；重建则是在毁坏之后重复这一组装。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"RULE-GOVERNED BUILDING: theories, arguments, sentences and figures are put together by allowed joins.","cn":"受规则支配的建造：理论、论证、句子和图形都靠允许的拼接方式组成。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"THE PRODUCT AS NOUN: a construct is a concept or a phrase pattern that people have assembled.","cn":"作为名词的产物：construct 是人们组装出来的概念或句式。"},{"senses":"06 · 09 · 10","en":"MADE, BUILDING UP, TAKEN DOWN: constructed marks the made state, constructive adds to the structure, deconstruct exposes the joints.","cn":"人造、增建、拆解：constructed 标记被造的状态，constructive 为结构添砖，deconstruct 则暴露接缝。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE PROCESS AND ITS READING: construction covers building, the trade, the result, and the building of meaning in interpretation.","cn":"过程与解读：construction 覆盖建造、行业、成果，以及解释中对意义的搭建。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Construct is con- + stru- + -ct (past participle stem). Every English relative keeps the 'pile up' image: structure, instruct, obstruct, reconstruct, deconstruct.","cn":"construct 是 con- + stru- + -ct（过去分词词干）。每个英语亲属都保留“堆起”的意象：structure、instruct、obstruct、reconstruct、deconstruct。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin struere family is large: structura 'a building', instructio 'arrangement', obstructio 'a building against', and construere itself. English borrowed them directly and through French.","cn":"拉丁 struere 词族庞大：structura“建筑”、instructio“安排”、obstructio“挡在前的构筑”，以及 construere 本身。英语有直接借入，也有经法语借入。"},"items":[{"word":"construct","structure":"con- (together) + struct- (piled) + -Ø (verb)","meaning":"to build or assemble","meaningCN":"建造；组装","example":"They construct houses from local stone.","exampleCN":"他们用当地石料建造房屋。"},{"word":"construction","structure":"construct + -ion (noun of action or result)","meaning":"the act or industry of building; a structure; an interpretation","meaningCN":"建造；建筑业；结构；解释（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The road is closed for construction.","exampleCN":"这条路因施工封闭。"},{"word":"constructive","structure":"construct + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"helpful and building up rather than destructive","meaningCN":"建设性的；有助益的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"Thank you for the constructive criticism.","exampleCN":"谢谢你的建设性批评。"},{"word":"constructor","structure":"construct + -or (person or thing that does)","meaning":"one who constructs; in programming, a function that builds an object","meaningCN":"建造者；构造函数（-or 表施动者）","example":"The constructor runs when a new object is created.","exampleCN":"创建新对象时会运行构造函数。"},{"word":"reconstruct","structure":"re- (again) + construct","meaning":"to build again or rebuild in thought","meaningCN":"重建；复原（re- 表再次）","example":"They reconstructed the palace from old plans.","exampleCN":"他们依据旧图纸重建了宫殿。"},{"word":"deconstruct","structure":"de- (down, apart) + construct","meaning":"to take apart in order to analyse","meaningCN":"解构；拆解分析（de- 表拆开）","example":"The class deconstructed the film's opening scene.","exampleCN":"课堂上拆解了这部电影的开场镜头。"},{"word":"structure","structure":"struct- (built) + -ure (noun)","meaning":"the arrangement of parts; a built thing","meaningCN":"结构；构造物（同一词根的名词）","example":"The structure of the essay is very clear.","exampleCN":"这篇文章的结构非常清楚。"},{"word":"instruct","structure":"in- (into) + struct- (build)","meaning":"to teach or give orders, literally 'build into' the mind","meaningCN":"指导；教授（字面“搭进头脑”，同一词根）","example":"The coach instructed the team to slow down.","exampleCN":"教练指示队伍放慢节奏。"},{"word":"obstruct","structure":"ob- (against) + struct- (build)","meaning":"to block the way, literally 'build against'","meaningCN":"阻挡；妨碍（字面“挡着搭”，同一词根）","example":"A fallen tree obstructed the road.","exampleCN":"一棵倒下的树挡住了道路。"},{"word":"construe","structure":"con- + stru- + -e (older borrowing)","meaning":"to interpret or explain","meaningCN":"解释；理解（同一拉丁词较早的借入形式）","example":"Her silence was construed as agreement.","exampleCN":"她的沉默被理解为同意。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"construere","structure":"con- + struere","meaning":"to pile up together, build, erect","meaningCN":"堆在一起；建造；竖立"},{"word":"struere","structure":"PIE *streu-","meaning":"to pile up, heap, arrange","meaningCN":"堆起；堆积；安排"},{"word":"structura","structure":"struct- + -ura","meaning":"a building, an arrangement","meaningCN":"建筑；构造；安排"}]}},{"word":"consult","ipa_uk":"/kənˈsʌlt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈsʌlt/","definition_zh":"咨询；请教；查阅；磋商；顾及","definition_en":"to ask someone for advice or information, to look something up, or to discuss something before deciding","core_image":"三个人围坐在桌前，把同一份问题摊开，共同出主意","scene":"图书馆里，学生遇到不懂的术语，转身抽出一本专业词典翻到对应词条。她说：I'll consult the dictionary.","sceneCN":"这里 consult 是「查阅参考资料」（第 2 个义项：从书本或资料中获取信息）；句意：我要查一下词典。图中可辨识物件：书架、专业词典、翻开的书页、学生。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"咨询；请教；查阅；考虑到"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"商议；磋商（常与 with 连用）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"consult a dictionary","zh":"查词典"},{"phrase":"consult with someone","zh":"与某人商议"},{"phrase":"consult a doctor","zh":"看医生；向医生咨询"},{"phrase":"consult a lawyer","zh":"咨询律师"},{"phrase":"consult the original source","zh":"查阅原始资料"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"consults"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"consulted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"consulted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"consulting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"consultant","pos":"n.","zh":"顾问；会诊医生"},{"word":"consultation","pos":"n.","zh":"磋商；咨询；会诊"},{"word":"consultative","pos":"adj.","zh":"顾问的；协商性的"},{"word":"consultancy","pos":"n.","zh":"咨询公司；顾问业务"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Ask a person for advice","titleCN":"向人请教：把问题交给懂的人","definition":"to ask someone with more knowledge or authority for advice before acting","definitionCN":"在行动之前向更有知识或权威的人寻求意见","example":"Consult your teacher before choosing the topic.","exampleCN":"选题之前先请教你的老师。","why":"Latin consulere meant 'take counsel, meet and consider'. The core act is gathering people to think together, not simply asking a question.","whyCN":"拉丁语 consulere 意为“商议、聚在一起考虑”。核心动作是把人聚起来共同思考，而不只是问一个问题。"},{"no":"02","title":"Look something up in a source","titleCN":"查阅：从书本或资料里取证","definition":"to go to a book, database or document to find information","definitionCN":"到书本、数据库或文件中查找信息","example":"Consult the manual before you reset the machine.","exampleCN":"重置机器之前先查阅手册。","why":"A dictionary or manual is a frozen council: many people's considered opinions are stored in it, waiting to be asked.","whyCN":"词典或手册是一个被冻结的议事会：许多人的审慎意见被存在里面，等着被询问。"},{"no":"03","title":"Discuss with others before deciding","titleCN":"磋商：做决定前和别人议一议","definition":"to exchange views with someone in order to reach a decision, usually with with","definitionCN":"为达成决定而与某人交换意见，通常与 with 连用","example":"The mayor consulted with local businesses before the vote.","exampleCN":"投票前市长与当地企业进行了磋商。","why":"The verb is symmetric here: two parties put their views on the same table. English marks the second party with with.","whyCN":"这里动词是对称的：两方把意见放到同一张桌上。英语用 with 标记第二方。"},{"no":"04","title":"See a professional for help","titleCN":"找专业人士：就医、找律师","definition":"to visit a doctor, lawyer or other expert for professional judgement","definitionCN":"为获得专业判断而去看医生、律师或其他专家","example":"You should consult a specialist about the pain.","exampleCN":"你应该找专科医生看看这处疼痛。","why":"The professional is the person whose counsel is worth gathering. The object is the expert, not the problem, which is why 'consult a doctor' needs no preposition.","whyCN":"专业人士就是其意见值得听取的人。宾语是专家而不是问题，所以 consult a doctor 不需要介词。"},{"no":"05","title":"Consultation: the meeting and the advice","titleCN":"consultation：磋商会议、咨询过程","definition":"the noun for a formal meeting to exchange views, or the act of seeking expert advice","definitionCN":"指交换意见的正式会议，或寻求专业意见的行为","example":"The plan was changed after public consultation.","exampleCN":"该计划在公众咨询之后作了修改。","why":"The -ation noun names the gathering itself. It can be a single meeting or a whole process of hearing opinions.","whyCN":"-ation 名词命名的是“聚集”本身。它既可以指一次会议，也可以指听取意见的整个过程。"},{"no":"06","title":"Consultant: the person consulted","titleCN":"consultant：被咨询的顾问","definition":"a person whose job is to give expert advice in a particular field","definitionCN":"以在特定领域提供专业意见为职业的人","example":"The firm hired a consultant to review its security.","exampleCN":"公司聘请了一名顾问来审查其安全状况。","why":"The -ant suffix marks the person who is consulted. Originally (1690s) the word meant 'one who consults an oracle'; the meaning shifted to the expert being asked.","whyCN":"-ant 后缀标记被咨询的人。最初（17 世纪 90 年代）这个词指“向神谕求问的人”，后来意义转向“被请教的那位专家”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Consultative: advisory, not decisive","titleCN":"consultative：协商性的、顾问性的","definition":"the adjective describes a body or role that gives advice but does not make the final decision","definitionCN":"形容词指只提供意见、不作最终决定的机构或角色","example":"The committee has only a consultative role.","exampleCN":"该委员会只起协商作用。","why":"The -ive suffix marks the function: the body exists for consultation, so its power is the power to be heard, not to decide.","whyCN":"-ive 后缀标记功能：该机构为“被咨询”而存在，所以它的权力是“被听见”，而不是“做决定”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Consult someone's interests or feelings","titleCN":"顾及：把别人的利益纳入考虑","definition":"to take a person's wishes or interests into account when acting","definitionCN":"行动时把某人的意愿或利益纳入考虑","example":"A good manager consults the team's feelings before announcing changes.","exampleCN":"好的管理者在宣布变动前会顾及团队的感受。","why":"To consult someone's interests is to let their view sit at the table even when they are not physically there.","whyCN":"consult someone's interests 就是让他们的视角坐在桌边，即使他们本人不在场。"},{"no":"09","title":"Consult an oracle: the historical sense","titleCN":"求问神谕：历史义","definition":"in older usage, to seek guidance from a god, an oracle or a supernatural sign","definitionCN":"在较早用法中，向神、神谕或超自然征兆寻求指引","example":"In the story, the king consulted the oracle before going to war.","exampleCN":"故事中，国王出征前求问了神谕。","why":"This is the sense that produced consultant 'one who consults an oracle'. The word has always meant going to a higher authority for counsel.","whyCN":"正是这一义项产生了 consultant“向神谕求问的人”。这个词一直表示“到更高的权威那里求教”。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Consult came from French consulter in the 1520s, from Latin consultare, a frequentative of consulere 'take counsel, meet and consider'. The deeper origin is debated: it may mean 'call together', but that reconstruction is marked uncertain.","cn":"consult 于 16 世纪 20 年代来自法语 consulter，源头是拉丁语 consultare——consulere“商议、聚在一起考虑”的反复动词。更深层的来源有争议：它可能意为“召集在一起”，但这一重构被标注为不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Consulere meant 'take counsel, meet and consider'. Romans consulted the senate (consulere senatum) before acting, so the verb began as a collective act.","cn":"consulere 意为“商议、聚在一起考虑”。罗马人行动前会“咨询元老院”（consulere senatum），所以这个动词一开始就是集体行为。"},{"era":"LATIN FORM","en":"Consultare is a frequentative of consulere, meaning 'consult repeatedly, take advice of'. Frequentatives describe repeated or intensive action, which is why consult feels like a deliberate, repeated asking.","cn":"consultare 是 consulere 的反复动词，意为“反复商议、向……求教”。反复动词描述重复或加强的动作，所以 consult 带有“慎重、反复求问”的感觉。"},{"era":"ORIGIN — UNCERTAIN","en":"It is probably 'to call together', from Proto-Italic *kom-sel-e-, with *kom- 'together' + *sel-e- 'take, gather'. De Vaan accepts this cautiously, so the deepest etymology is source uncertain rather than established fact.","cn":"它可能意为“召集在一起”，来自原始意大利语 *kom-sel-e-，由 *kom-“一起”加 *sel-e-“拿取、聚集”构成。de Vaan 谨慎接受这一说法，因此最深层词源属于来源不确定，而非既定事实。"},{"era":"1520s ENGLISH","en":"English recorded consult in the 1520s from French consulter, meaning both 'ask advice of' and 'take counsel together'.","cn":"英语在 16 世纪 20 年代从法语 consulter 记录 consult，同时表示“向……求教”和“共同商议”。"},{"era":"1540s–1690s ENGLISH","en":"Consultation is recorded in the 1540s for 'a meeting to consult together'; consultant appears in the 1690s meaning 'one who consults an oracle', and only later 'expert adviser'.","cn":"consultation 于 16 世纪 40 年代记录，指“共同商议的会议”；consultant 于 17 世纪 90 年代出现，意为“向神谕求问的人”，后来才指“专家顾问”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps two constructions: consult a person or a book directly, and consult with a person for a mutual discussion. The first object is the source; the second is the partner.","cn":"现代英语保留两种结构：直接 consult 某人或某书，以及 consult with 某人为共同讨论。前者宾语是信息来源，后者宾语是商谈伙伴。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the consul family from two near-spellings; the near-meaning group distinguishes asking advice from discussing and from checking a source.","cn":"形近组把 consul 词族与两个近形词分开；近义组区分“求教”“讨论”与“查证资料”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"consul","ipa":"/ˈkɒnsl/","tag":"near spelling, different word","definition":"an official who lives abroad and protects citizens, or a Roman magistrate. It is a noun from consul, not from consulere.","definitionCN":"驻外保护本国公民的官员，或古罗马执政官。它是来自 consul 的名词，而非来自 consulere。"},{"word":"consultant","ipa":"/kənˈsʌltənt/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"an expert who gives professional advice. It is consult + -ant, the person who is consulted.","definitionCN":"提供专业意见的专家。它是 consult + -ant，即被咨询的人。"},{"word":"insult","ipa":"/ɪnˈsʌlt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to speak or act with contempt. Its root is salire 'to leap', literally 'leap upon', not consulere.","definitionCN":"以轻蔑的方式说话或行事。它的词根是 salire“跳”，字面是“扑上去”，而非 consulere。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"confer","ipa":"/kənˈfɜː/","tag":"discuss formally","definition":"to discuss something with others before deciding. It is close to consult with but more formal and mutual.","definitionCN":"在做决定前与他人讨论。它接近 consult with，但更正式、更强调双向。"},{"word":"advise","ipa":"/əˈvaɪz/","tag":"give advice","definition":"to tell someone what you think they should do. The direction is opposite: the adviser speaks, the consulter asks.","definitionCN":"告诉某人你认为他该怎么做。方向相反：顾问说，求教者问。"},{"word":"refer to","ipa":"/rɪˈfɜː tuː/","tag":"check a source","definition":"to look at a book or document for information. It overlaps with consult in the lookup sense but has no 'ask a person' use.","definitionCN":"为获取信息而查看书本或文件。它在“查阅”义上与 consult 重叠，但没有“向人求教”的用法。"},{"word":"deliberate","ipa":"/dɪˈlɪbəreɪt/","tag":"weigh together","definition":"to consider carefully, often as a group. It names the thinking stage that consultation serves.","definitionCN":"仔细考虑，常指集体进行。它命名的是咨询所服务的那个思考阶段。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: consulere 'take counsel', consultare its frequentative, and the everyday derivatives consultant, consultation and consultative.","cn":"只用真实构件：consulere“商议”、其反复动词 consultare，以及日常派生词 consultant、consultation、consultative。"},"normal":[{"en":"Roman senators were 'consulted' as a body. Consulting still means putting a question in front of people who think together.","cn":"罗马元老院是作为一个整体被“咨询”的。consult 至今仍意味着把问题摆到会共同思考的人面前。"},{"en":"Consult a book is consulting a frozen meeting: the authors' considered views are stored inside.","cn":"consult a book 就是咨询一场被冻结的会议：作者们审慎的观点被存在书里。"},{"en":"Use consult + person or book for the source, and consult with + person for the partner. The preposition marks whether the person is answering or discussing.","cn":"用 consult + 人或书表示信息来源，用 consult with + 人表示商谈伙伴。介词标出这个人是“回答者”还是“讨论者”。"},{"en":"Consultant first meant someone who asks an oracle, then flipped to the expert who is asked. The -ant suffix still marks the person in the exchange.","cn":"consultant 最初指向神谕求问的人，后来翻转为被请教的专家。-ant 后缀仍标记交流中的那个人。"},{"en":"Consultative bodies advise; they do not decide. The -ive suffix marks a function, not a power.","cn":"协商性机构只提供意见，不做决定。-ive 后缀标记的是一种功能，而不是权力。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a table with a problem lying open on it and several chairs around. Consult is the act of pulling a chair up to that table.","cn":"想象一张桌子，问题摊在桌面上，周围摆着几把椅子。consult 就是把椅子拉到这张桌边的动作。"},{"en":"The chairs can be occupied by a teacher, a doctor, a dictionary, or the remembered interests of someone absent.","cn":"椅子上可以坐着老师、医生、词典，或某个不在场者被记住的利益。"},{"en":"The word is never about the answer alone; it is about placing the question where more than one mind can reach it.","cn":"这个词从来不只是关于答案，而是关于把问题放到不止一个头脑能够到的地方。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Please consult the schedule before booking the room.","cn":"订房间前请先查阅日程表。"},{"en":"The director consulted with the department heads for an hour.","cn":"主任与各部门负责人磋商了一个小时。"},{"en":"He consulted a lawyer about the contract.","cn":"他就这份合同咨询了一位律师。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·搜特”——肯（定）要搜（索）特（别难查的）资料，还要找人问 → consult 查阅、咨询","word":"consult"},"root":"源自拉丁语 consultare（consulere“商议、聚在一起考虑”的反复动词），可能由 com-“一起”+ 词根“拿取、聚集”构成，核心是“把问题摊到众人面前求教”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of consult, all built on one table. A teacher, a book, a doctor, a partner, a committee and even an oracle can sit at it; the constant is that the question is placed where another mind can reach it.","cn":"consult 的九个义项都建立在一张桌边。老师、书本、医生、伙伴、委员会甚至神谕都可以坐在这张桌旁；不变的是问题被放到了另一个头脑能够到的地方。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a problem laid open on a table with several chairs pulled up to it.","cn":"核心意象：问题摊开在桌上，几把椅子被拉到桌边。"},"chain":["QUESTION","GATHER COUNSEL","ASK","GET AN ANSWER","DECIDE","THE ADVISER"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04 · 09","en":"ASKING A HIGHER AUTHORITY: a teacher, a professional or an oracle is asked to give a judgement.","cn":"向更高权威求问：老师、专业人士或神谕被请求给出判断。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"CONSULTING WHAT IS NOT PRESENT: a book, a manual or someone's interests hold a view that can still be reached.","cn":"咨询不在场者：书本、手册或某人的利益保存着仍可被触及的视角。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"SITTING TOGETHER: consult with and consultation name the mutual meeting, not the one-way question.","cn":"围坐共议：consult with 与 consultation 命名的是双向会议，而不是单向提问。"},{"senses":"06 · 07","en":"THE ROLE OF THE ADVISER: consultant is the person asked, and consultative marks advice without decision power.","cn":"顾问的角色：consultant 是被请教的人，consultative 标记只有建议权而无决定权。"},{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"THE PREPOSITION SPLIT: consult + source is one-way; consult with + partner is two-way. English marks the difference with one small word.","cn":"介词分工：consult + 来源是单向；consult with + 伙伴是双向。英语用一个小词标出这个差别。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Consult is a Latin verb with a frequentative suffix -tare. English derivatives add -ant, -ation, -ative and -ancy, all naming people and processes of advice.","cn":"consult 是一个带反复后缀 -tare 的拉丁动词。英语派生词加 -ant、-ation、-ative、-ancy，都命名“建议”中的人与过程。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is real but partly obscure: consulere, consultare, consultum 'a decision, counsel', and the noun consul, whose link to the verb is debated. The English words come mainly through French.","cn":"拉丁词族真实但部分晦涩：consulere、consultare、consultum“决定、意见”，以及名词 consul——它与动词的联系有争议。英语词主要经法语传入。"},"items":[{"word":"consult","structure":"con- (together) + sult- (take counsel) + -Ø (verb)","meaning":"to ask advice, look up, or discuss","meaningCN":"咨询；查阅；商议","example":"Consult the map before you leave.","exampleCN":"出发前先看地图。"},{"word":"consultant","structure":"consult + -ant (person who does or is acted on)","meaning":"an expert who gives professional advice","meaningCN":"顾问；会诊医生（-ant 表人）","example":"They hired a safety consultant.","exampleCN":"他们聘请了一名安全顾问。"},{"word":"consultation","structure":"consult + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"a meeting to exchange views; the act of seeking advice","meaningCN":"磋商；咨询；会诊（-ation 构成名词）","example":"The decision followed months of consultation.","exampleCN":"这一决定经过了数月的咨询。"},{"word":"consultative","structure":"consult + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"advisory rather than decision-making","meaningCN":"协商性的；顾问性的（-ative 构成形容词）","example":"The panel plays a consultative role.","exampleCN":"该小组起协商作用。"},{"word":"consulting","structure":"consult + -ing (participle or gerund)","meaning":"the business of giving expert advice","meaningCN":"咨询业；提供顾问服务的（-ing 构成动名词）","example":"She works for a consulting firm.","exampleCN":"她在一家咨询公司工作。"},{"word":"consultancy","structure":"consultant + -cy (business or role)","meaning":"a company that gives expert advice, or the work it does","meaningCN":"咨询公司；顾问业务（-cy 构成名词）","example":"He runs a small design consultancy.","exampleCN":"他经营一家小型设计咨询公司。"},{"word":"consultable","structure":"consult + -able (adjective)","meaning":"available to be consulted or looked at","meaningCN":"可供查阅的（-able 表可能）","example":"The archive is consultable by appointment.","exampleCN":"该档案可预约查阅。"},{"word":"reconsult","structure":"re- (again) + consult","meaning":"to consult again","meaningCN":"再次咨询；重新查阅（re- 表再次）","example":"Reconsult the source after the revision.","exampleCN":"修订后再查一次原始资料。"},{"word":"consul","structure":"consul (Roman magistrate; modern diplomat)","meaning":"an official representing a state abroad","meaningCN":"领事；古罗马执政官（形近但不同来源的名词）","example":"She applied for a visa at the consulate.","exampleCN":"她在领事馆申请签证。"},{"word":"consulate","structure":"consul + -ate (office or place)","meaning":"the office or residence of a consul","meaningCN":"领事馆；领事职位（-ate 表职位或场所）","example":"The consulate handles emergency passports.","exampleCN":"领事馆办理紧急护照。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"consulere","structure":"prob. *kom- + *sel-e- (uncertain)","meaning":"to take counsel, meet and consider","meaningCN":"商议；聚在一起考虑"},{"word":"consultare","structure":"frequentative of consulere","meaning":"to consult repeatedly, take advice of","meaningCN":"反复商议；向……求教"},{"word":"consultum","structure":"neuter past participle used as noun","meaning":"a decision, a counsel","meaningCN":"决定；意见"}]}},{"word":"consume","ipa_uk":"/kənˈsjuːm/","ipa_us":"/kənˈsuːm/","definition_zh":"消耗；消费；吃喝；吞噬；使全神贯注","definition_en":"to use up something such as food, fuel, energy or money, or to take up all of someone's attention","core_image":"一支蜡烛被火焰一点点吃掉，越烧越短","scene":"地铁上，乘客开着高清视频通话，右上角的电量条几分钟就掉了一格。他叹气说：Video calls consume a lot of battery.","sceneCN":"这里 consume 是「消耗资源」（第 2 个义项：把燃料、电力等逐渐用光）；句意：视频通话非常耗电。图中可辨识物件：手机、电量条、耳机、地铁车厢。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"消耗；消费；吃喝；吞噬"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"使全神贯注；占据（心思）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"consume energy","zh":"消耗能源"},{"phrase":"consume resources","zh":"消耗资源"},{"phrase":"be consumed with","zh":"被（情绪）吞噬；满脑子都是"},{"phrase":"time-consuming","zh":"耗时的"},{"phrase":"consumer goods","zh":"消费品"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"consumes"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"consumed"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"consumed"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"consuming"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"consumer","pos":"n.","zh":"消费者；用户"},{"word":"consumption","pos":"n.","zh":"消耗；消费；消耗量"},{"word":"consumable","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"可消耗的；消耗品"},{"word":"consumptive","pos":"adj.","zh":"消耗性的；（旧）患肺结核的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Eat or drink something","titleCN":"吃喝：把食物送进身体","definition":"to eat or drink something, especially in quantity","definitionCN":"吃下或喝下某物，尤指大量地","example":"The hikers consumed two litres of water each.","exampleCN":"徒步者每人喝了两升水。","why":"Latin consumere is com- (intensive) + sumere 'take'. Food is taken completely into the body, so 'eat' is the most literal sense of taking up.","whyCN":"拉丁语 consumere 是 com-（表加强）加 sumere“拿取”。食物被完全拿进身体，所以“吃”是“取用”最字面的义项。"},{"no":"02","title":"Use up fuel, energy or time","titleCN":"消耗：把资源一点点用光","definition":"to use a resource such as fuel, electricity, money or time until less of it remains","definitionCN":"使用燃料、电力、金钱或时间等资源，使其余量变少","example":"Old fridges consume far more electricity than new ones.","exampleCN":"旧冰箱比新冰箱耗电多得多。","why":"The intensive com- makes the taking complete: the fuel is not borrowed, it is gone. That is why consume implies a shrinking supply.","whyCN":"加强的 com- 让“取”变得彻底：燃料不是借来的，而是没了。所以 consume 意味着供给在减少。"},{"no":"03","title":"Destroy by fire","titleCN":"吞噬：火把东西烧掉","definition":"of fire or a destructive force, to destroy something completely","definitionCN":"（火或破坏性力量）彻底摧毁某物","example":"The fire consumed the whole warehouse in an hour.","exampleCN":"大火一小时就吞噬了整个仓库。","why":"Fire takes the substance of a thing and leaves nothing to return. This physical annihilation is the strongest form of 'use up'.","whyCN":"火把物体的实体拿走，不留下任何可归还之物。这种物理上的彻底消灭，是“用光”最强的形式。"},{"no":"04","title":"Buy and use goods: the economic sense","titleCN":"消费：购买并使用商品","definition":"in economics, to buy and use goods and services, destroying their exchangeable value by using them","definitionCN":"在经济学中购买并使用商品与服务，通过使用消灭其交换价值","example":"Households consume more in December than in any other month.","exampleCN":"家庭在十二月的消费超过其他任何月份。","why":"The economist's consumer (from 1745) is the one who uses up goods. Consumption is simply the sum of all that using-up in an economy.","whyCN":"经济学意义上的 consumer（始于 1745 年）就是用光商品的人。消费就是一个经济体中所有“用光”的总和。"},{"no":"05","title":"Take up all of someone's attention","titleCN":"占据全部心思：全神贯注","definition":"of a feeling or interest, to fill someone's mind completely so that nothing else is noticed","definitionCN":"（情绪或兴趣）完全占满某人的心思，使其注意不到别的","example":"He was consumed with guilt after the argument.","exampleCN":"争吵之后，他满心都是愧疚。","why":"The 1570s sense 'to engage the full attention and energy of'. Attention is a resource too: once it is used up, nothing is left for anything else.","whyCN":"这一义项始于 16 世纪 70 年代，意为“占满某人的注意力与精力”。注意力也是一种资源：一旦被用光，就剩不下给别的东西了。"},{"no":"06","title":"Waste away: be slowly destroyed","titleCN":"消磨：被慢慢耗尽","definition":"of a person or thing, to be worn down or destroyed gradually by an illness, a worry or time","definitionCN":"（人或物）被疾病、忧虑或时间逐渐消磨、毁掉","example":"He was consumed by worry and stopped sleeping.","exampleCN":"他被忧虑消磨，开始失眠。","why":"The old medical word consumption named a disease that 'consumed' the body. Wasting away is consumption seen from the inside.","whyCN":"旧医学词 consumption 命名一种“吃掉”身体的病。逐渐消瘦就是consumption从内部看的样子。"},{"no":"07","title":"Consumer: the one who uses up","titleCN":"consumer：消费者、用户","definition":"the noun for a person or organization that buys and uses goods or services","definitionCN":"指购买并使用商品或服务的个人或组织","example":"Consumers are switching to cheaper brands.","exampleCN":"消费者正在转向更便宜的品牌。","why":"The -er suffix marks the doer. Early use (early 15c.) meant 'one who squanders or wastes'; the neutral economic sense dates from 1745.","whyCN":"-er 后缀标记施动者。早期用法（15 世纪早期）意为“挥霍、浪费的人”；中性的经济义始于 1745 年。"},{"no":"08","title":"Consumption: the amount used","titleCN":"consumption：消耗量、消费","definition":"the noun for the act of using something up, or the quantity used in a period","definitionCN":"指用光某物的行为，或一段时间内的使用量","example":"Fuel consumption has fallen by ten percent.","exampleCN":"燃料消耗量下降了百分之十。","why":"The -tion noun turns the act into a measurable quantity. Once you can measure the taking, you can compare it year by year.","whyCN":"-tion 名词把动作变成可测量的量。一旦“取用”能被测量，就能逐年比较。"},{"no":"09","title":"Consuming: intensely absorbing","titleCN":"consuming：极强烈的、占满人的","definition":"the adjective describes a passion or interest so strong that it takes up all one's energy","definitionCN":"形容词指某种热情或兴趣强烈到占满全部精力","example":"Restoring the boat became a consuming passion.","exampleCN":"修复那条船成了他全身心投入的爱好。","why":"This is the attention sense turned into an adjective: the passion eats the person's time and energy and leaves little else.","whyCN":"这是“占据注意力”义变成形容词：这份热情吃掉人的时间和精力，几乎不剩别的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Consume came from Old French consumer and Latin consumere 'use up, eat, waste', from com- (intensive) + sumere 'take'. The same sumere family gives assume, resume and presume, so the difference is entirely in the prefix.","cn":"consume 来自古法语 consumer 和拉丁语 consumere“用光、吃、浪费”，由 com-（表加强）加 sumere“拿取”构成。同一个 sumere 词族还给出 assume、resume、presume，区别全在前缀。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Consumere meant 'to use up, eat, waste, destroy'. Sumere 'to take' is sub- 'under' + emere 'to buy, take', so the base image is taking something into one's hand.","cn":"consumere 意为“用光、吃、浪费、毁掉”。sumere“拿取”由 sub-“在下面”加 emere“买、取”构成，基础意象是把东西拿到手里。"},{"era":"LATE 14C ENGLISH","en":"English recorded consume meaning 'to destroy by separating into parts which cannot be reunited, as by burning or eating', hence 'annihilate'.","cn":"英语记录的 consume 意为“通过分成无法复原的部分而毁掉，如烧掉或吃掉”，由此引申为“彻底消灭”。"},{"era":"c. 1400 ENGLISH","en":"The specific sense 'to destroy by use, wear out by applying to its natural use' is from about 1400. This is the modern resource sense in embryo.","cn":"“通过使用而毁坏、在正常用途中磨损”这一具体义约始于 1400 年。现代的资源消耗义在此已具雏形。"},{"era":"1570s ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'to engage the full attention and energy of' is from the 1570s, turning mental attention into something that can be used up.","cn":"“占满注意力与精力”的义项始于 16 世纪 70 年代，把心理注意力变成了可被用光的东西。"},{"era":"15C–1745 ENGLISH","en":"Consumer first meant 'one who squanders or wastes' (early 15c.). The economic sense 'one who uses up goods, opposite of producer' dates from 1745.","cn":"consumer 最初意为“挥霍、浪费的人”（15 世纪早期）。经济义“使用光商品的人，与生产者相对”始于 1745 年。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps the whole range: eat, use up fuel, be consumed by fire or guilt, and consume goods. The common thread is that something is taken completely and not returned.","cn":"现代英语保留完整范围：吃、耗尽燃料、被火或愧疚吞噬、消费商品。共同线索是某物被彻底取走且不再归还。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the sumere family, where the prefix changes the meaning; the near-meaning group separates eating, spending and destroying.","cn":"形近组是 sumere 词族，前缀改变意义；近义组区分“吃”“花费”与“毁掉”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"assume","ipa":"/əˈsjuːm/","tag":"same root, ad- prefix","definition":"to suppose something without proof, or to take on a role. Ad- 'to' + sumere 'take' = take to oneself; nothing is used up.","definitionCN":"未经证明就假定，或承担某个角色。ad-“向”加 sumere“取”＝拿到自己身上；没有任何东西被用光。"},{"word":"resume","ipa":"/rɪˈzjuːm/","tag":"same root, re- prefix","definition":"to begin again after a pause, or to take back. Re- 'back, again' + sumere 'take' = take back up.","definitionCN":"停顿后重新开始，或收回。re-“回、再”加 sumere“取”＝重新拿起来。"},{"word":"consumption","ipa":"/kənˈsʌmpʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the act or amount of using up; also the old name for tuberculosis. It is consume + -tion.","definitionCN":"消耗行为或消耗量；也曾是肺结核的旧称。它是 consume + -tion。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"devour","ipa":"/dɪˈvaʊə/","tag":"eat greedily","definition":"to eat something quickly and hungrily. It is vivid and literary, while consume is neutral and technical.","definitionCN":"狼吞虎咽地吃掉。它生动、文学化，而 consume 中性且技术化。"},{"word":"expend","ipa":"/ɪkˈspend/","tag":"spend resources","definition":"to use up money, energy or effort for a purpose. It is formal and stresses deliberate spending rather than depletion.","definitionCN":"为某个目的用掉金钱、精力或努力。它较正式，强调有意的支出而不是被耗尽。"},{"word":"use up","ipa":"/juːz ʌp/","tag":"phrasal verb","definition":"to take all of something until none is left. It is the plain conversational equivalent of the resource sense.","definitionCN":"把某物用尽，一点不剩。它是资源义的口语对应说法。"},{"word":"absorb","ipa":"/əbˈzɔːb/","tag":"take in","definition":"to take in liquid, heat, light or attention. The thing taken in is not destroyed but held; the direction is inward.","definitionCN":"吸收液体、热量、光或注意力。被吸收之物不是被毁掉，而是被容纳；方向是向内。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: sumere 'take', the prefix family assume, resume, presume, and the everyday derivatives consumer and consumption.","cn":"只用真实构件：sumere“取”，前缀词族 assume、resume、presume，以及日常派生词 consumer、consumption。"},"normal":[{"en":"Sumere means 'take'. Consume is 'take completely': the fuel, the food or the attention is taken and does not come back.","cn":"sumere 意为“取”。consume 是“彻底取走”：燃料、食物或注意力被取走，不再回来。"},{"en":"Assume is ad- 'to' + sumere: take to yourself, so you take on a role or take a guess. Nothing is used up.","cn":"assume 是 ad-“向”加 sumere：拿到自己身上，于是承担角色或作出假定。没有任何东西被用光。"},{"en":"Resume is re- 'again' + sumere: take up again after a pause.","cn":"resume 是 re-“再”加 sumere：停顿之后重新拿起来。"},{"en":"Presume is pre- 'before' + sumere: take something as true before you have checked it.","cn":"presume 是 pre-“之前”加 sumere：在核实之前就先把它当成真的。"},{"en":"Consumption also used to be the name of tuberculosis, because the disease seemed to consume the body from within.","cn":"consumption 还曾是肺结核的名称，因为这种病看起来是从内部把身体吃掉。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a candle burning down. Each minute of light is paid for by a piece of wax that will never come back.","cn":"想象一支蜡烛越烧越短。每一分钟的光，都是用一小截再也回不来的蜡换来的。"},{"en":"The same ledger applies to petrol, money, battery, time and attention: all are stocks that can only go down as they are used.","cn":"同样的账本适用于汽油、金钱、电量、时间和注意力：它们都是只会随着使用而下降的存量。"},{"en":"The word's intensity comes from com-: not merely taken, but taken all the way, which is why fire and obsession both consume.","cn":"这个词的强度来自 com-：不只是取走，而是一取到底；所以火焰与执念都用 consume。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"This old heater consumes too much gas.","cn":"这台旧取暖器太费燃气。"},{"en":"She consumed the whole book in one evening.","cn":"她一个晚上就把整本书读完了。"},{"en":"He was consumed by jealousy after seeing the letter.","cn":"看到那封信后，他满心都是嫉妒。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·苏姆”——肯（定）把苏（打）姆（的）电量全用光，一点都不留 → consume 消耗、消费","word":"consume"},"root":"源自拉丁语 consumere“用光、吃、浪费”，由 com-（表加强）+ sumere“取”构成，核心是“彻底取走、不再归还”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of consume, all built on taking something completely. Food, fuel, goods, attention, a body and even a house in a fire are taken up, and none of them is given back.","cn":"consume 的九个义项都建立在“把某物彻底取走”上。食物、燃料、商品、注意力、身体，甚至火中的房屋，都被取用，没有一样会被归还。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a candle burning down, its wax turning into light and heat and never returning.","cn":"核心意象：一支蜡烛越烧越短，蜡变成光与热，再也回不来。"},"chain":["TAKE","TAKE IN","TAKE UP","USE","NOTHING LEFT","ABSORBED"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"FOOD AND BUYERS: the body takes food in, and the economy's consumer takes goods in.","cn":"食物与消费者：身体把食物取进来，经济中的消费者把商品取进来。"},{"senses":"02 · 08","en":"STOCKS THAT FALL: fuel, electricity, money and time are drawn down, and their fall is measurable consumption.","cn":"会下降的存量：燃料、电力、金钱和时间被抽取，其下降就是可测量的消耗量。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"DESTRUCTION: fire consumes a building, and illness consumes a body; the taking leaves no remainder.","cn":"毁灭：火烧掉建筑，疾病消磨身体；这种“取”不留下残余。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"ATTENTION AS RESOURCE: guilt, passion and obsession fill the mind completely, leaving no attention for anything else.","cn":"注意力作为资源：愧疚、热情与执念完全占满头脑，不剩注意力给别的。"},{"senses":"09","en":"THE ADJECTIVE OF ABSORPTION: a consuming passion is one that has eaten all the person's energy.","cn":"吸收的形容词：consuming passion 是吃掉了这个人全部精力的热情。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Consume is com- + sum- + -e. The prefix does the semantic work: com- means 'completely', while ad-, re- and pre- produce assume, resume and presume from the same verb.","cn":"consume 是 com- + sum- + -e。意义主要由前缀承担：com- 表“彻底”，而 ad-、re-、pre- 用同一个动词造出 assume、resume、presume。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin sumere family is real and productive: sumere, sumptus 'taken, spent', consumere, assumere, resumere, praesumere. English borrowed each through French or directly.","cn":"拉丁 sumere 词族真实且能产：sumere、sumptus“取走的、花费的”、consumere、assumere、resumere、praesumere。英语或经法语、或直接借入。"},"items":[{"word":"consume","structure":"con- (completely) + sum- (take) + -e (verb)","meaning":"to eat, use up, destroy or absorb","meaningCN":"消耗；消费；吃喝；吞噬","example":"The plant consumes water quickly in summer.","exampleCN":"这株植物夏天耗水很快。"},{"word":"consumer","structure":"consume + -er (person who does)","meaning":"one who buys and uses goods","meaningCN":"消费者（-er 表施动者）","example":"Consumers want clearer labels.","exampleCN":"消费者想要更清楚的标签。"},{"word":"consumption","structure":"consume + -tion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or amount of using up","meaningCN":"消耗；消费；消耗量（-tion 构成名词）","example":"Energy consumption peaks in summer.","exampleCN":"能源消耗在夏季达到高峰。"},{"word":"consumable","structure":"consume + -able (adjective and noun)","meaning":"able to be used up; a item that is used up","meaningCN":"可消耗的；消耗品（-able 表可能）","example":"Printer ink is a consumable.","exampleCN":"打印机墨水是消耗品。"},{"word":"consuming","structure":"consume + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"taking up all one's energy or attention","meaningCN":"极耗精力的；占满心思的（-ing 构成分词）","example":"The project was all-consuming.","exampleCN":"这个项目占满了全部精力。"},{"word":"consumptive","structure":"consume + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"tending to consume; formerly describing tuberculosis","meaningCN":"消耗性的；旧指肺结核的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"Consumptive use leaves less water for the river.","exampleCN":"消耗性用水给河流留下的水更少。"},{"word":"assume","structure":"ad- (to) + sumere (take)","meaning":"to take to oneself, take on, or suppose","meaningCN":"假定；承担（同一词根，ad- 表朝向）","example":"I assume the meeting starts at nine.","exampleCN":"我假定会议九点开始。"},{"word":"resume","structure":"re- (again) + sumere (take)","meaning":"to take up again after a pause","meaningCN":"重新开始；恢复（re- 表再次）","example":"Talks resumed on Monday.","exampleCN":"谈判在周一恢复。"},{"word":"presume","structure":"pre- (before) + sumere (take)","meaning":"to take as true before checking","meaningCN":"推测；假定（pre- 表在前）","example":"I presume you have read the file.","exampleCN":"我想你已经读过文件了。"},{"word":"unconsumed","structure":"un- (not) + consumed","meaning":"not used up or eaten","meaningCN":"未被消耗的；未吃掉的（un- 表否定）","example":"Unconsumed food was donated.","exampleCN":"没吃完的食物被捐赠了。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"consumere","structure":"com- + sumere","meaning":"to use up, eat, waste, destroy","meaningCN":"用光；吃；浪费；毁掉"},{"word":"sumere","structure":"sub- + emere","meaning":"to take, take up, buy","meaningCN":"拿取；取用；购买"},{"word":"emere","structure":"PIE *em-","meaning":"to buy, take, distribute","meaningCN":"买；取；分配"}]}},{"word":"contact","ipa_uk":"/ˈkɒntækt/","ipa_us":"/ˈkɑːntækt/","definition_zh":"接触；联系；联络方式；联系人","definition_en":"the state of touching, communication between people, or a person and details you can use to reach someone","core_image":"两只手掌轻轻相触，接触处亮起一点微光","scene":"展会现场，两位负责人交换名片，把手机号和邮箱写在卡片背面。她说：Here are my contact details.","sceneCN":"这里 contact 是「联络方式、联系方式」（第 2、3 个义项：人与人建立往来、可被找到的信息）；句意：这是我的联系方式。图中可辨识物件：名片、手机号、邮箱、展台。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"接触；联系；联络方式；联系人"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"联系；联络（重音后移）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"contact details","zh":"联系方式"},{"phrase":"in contact with","zh":"与……有联系；与……接触"},{"phrase":"make contact with","zh":"与……取得联系"},{"phrase":"point of contact","zh":"接触点；联络人"},{"phrase":"contact lens","zh":"隐形眼镜"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"contacts"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contactless","pos":"adj.","zh":"非接触式的；感应式的"},{"word":"contactable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可联系到的"},{"word":"contactor","pos":"n.","zh":"接触器（电气元件）"},{"word":"contactee","pos":"n.","zh":"被接触者（多用于外星接触语境）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The state of touching","titleCN":"接触：两个表面碰到一起","definition":"the physical state in which two surfaces or bodies are touching","definitionCN":"两个表面或物体相互碰到的物理状态","example":"The paint dries only after contact with air.","exampleCN":"这种漆只有在接触空气后才会干。","why":"Latin contingere is com- 'together' + tangere 'to touch'. Two things are brought together until their surfaces meet; that meeting is contact.","whyCN":"拉丁语 contingere 由 com-“一起”加 tangere“触碰”构成。两个东西被带到一起，直到表面相接；这次相接就是 contact。"},{"no":"02","title":"Communication between people","titleCN":"联系：人与人之间的往来","definition":"the state of communicating or being in touch with someone, by speech, message or meeting","definitionCN":"通过言语、消息或见面而与某人保持往来的状态","example":"We stayed in contact after university.","exampleCN":"大学毕业后我们一直保持联系。","why":"The figurative sense 'a connection, communication' is recorded from 1818. A message is a way of touching someone across distance.","whyCN":"“联系、沟通”这一比喻义记录于 1818 年。一条消息就是跨越距离去“触碰”某人的方式。"},{"no":"03","title":"A person who can help you","titleCN":"联系人：能帮你搭上线的人","definition":"a person you know in an organization who can give you information or help","definitionCN":"你在某个机构认识、能提供信息或帮助的人","example":"My contact at the bank can check the transfer.","exampleCN":"我在银行的那个熟人可以查这笔转账。","why":"The sense 'a person who can be called upon for assistance' dates from 1931. The person is the point where your line touches the organization.","whyCN":"“可被求助的人”这一义项始于 1931 年。这个人正是你的线与机构相碰的那个点。"},{"no":"04","title":"To get in touch with someone","titleCN":"联系（动词）：主动去搭上话","definition":"to communicate with someone, especially for the first time or after a gap","definitionCN":"与某人沟通，尤指首次或中断一段时间之后","example":"Please contact us if the parcel does not arrive.","exampleCN":"如果包裹没有到，请联系我们。","why":"The verb appeared in 1834 meaning 'bring together or put in contact'; the modern 'get in touch with' sense is 1927 American English.","whyCN":"动词 1834 年出现，意为“使接触、使相连”；现代“与……取得联系”义是 1927 年的美式英语用法。"},{"no":"05","title":"Electrical contact","titleCN":"电接触：接通电路","definition":"the point where an electrical circuit is completed, or the act of closing it","definitionCN":"电路被接通的那个点，或接通电路的动作","example":"The switch closes the contact and the motor starts.","exampleCN":"开关闭合接触点，电机启动。","why":"To make contact (1860) began in electrical engineering: two conductors touch and current can pass. The metaphor of touch is literal again.","whyCN":"make contact（1860 年）最早用于电气工程：两个导体相碰，电流得以通过。这里“触碰”的比喻又变回了字面。"},{"no":"06","title":"Contact lens: touching the eye","titleCN":"隐形眼镜：直接贴在眼球上","definition":"a thin artificial lens placed directly on the surface of the eye","definitionCN":"直接贴在眼球表面的薄型人造镜片","example":"She wears contact lenses instead of glasses.","exampleCN":"她戴隐形眼镜，不戴框架眼镜。","why":"The term is recorded in 1888. The lens is named for the way it sits in direct contact with the eye, unlike spectacles that stand off the face.","whyCN":"该术语记录于 1888 年。镜片因直接与眼球接触而得名，不像框架眼镜那样离开脸部。"},{"no":"07","title":"In contact with: touch or communication","titleCN":"in contact with：有接触、有往来","definition":"the phrase describes either physical touching or ongoing communication with a person or group","definitionCN":"该短语既可指物理接触，也可指与某人或某群体持续沟通","example":"The doctor has been in contact with the family.","exampleCN":"医生一直与家属保持联系。","why":"The same preposition covers both halves of the word's life: surfaces touch, and people keep a line open.","whyCN":"同一个介词覆盖了这个词的两半生命：表面相触，人则保持一条线畅通。"},{"no":"08","title":"Point of contact: where the line meets","titleCN":"接触点：对接的那个位置或人","definition":"the place, moment or person where two systems or parties meet and exchange something","definitionCN":"两个系统或两方相遇并交换信息、物资的地点、时刻或人","example":"The reception desk is the first point of contact for visitors.","exampleCN":"接待台是访客的第一个接触点。","why":"In physics and in management alike, a point of contact is where the transfer happens. Everything else is approach.","whyCN":"无论在物理还是管理中，point of contact 都是“传递发生”的那一点，其余部分只是靠近。"},{"no":"09","title":"Contact sport and physical contact","titleCN":"身体接触：运动中撞到一起","definition":"in sport, the permitted bodily touching between players, as in rugby or boxing","definitionCN":"运动中允许的运动员之间身体碰撞，如橄榄球或拳击","example":"Rugby is a contact sport; tennis is not.","exampleCN":"橄榄球是身体接触型运动，网球不是。","why":"Contact sport (1922) names games where touching an opponent is part of the rules, not a foul.","whyCN":"contact sport（1922 年）指“碰到对手属于规则一部分、而非犯规”的运动。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Contact is from Latin contactus 'a touching', from contingere 'to touch, seize', com- 'together' + tangere 'to touch'. Tangere also gives tangent, tactile, contagious and contiguous, so the whole family is about touching.","cn":"contact 来自拉丁语 contactus“触碰”，源头是 contingere“碰到、抓住”，由 com-“一起”加 tangere“触碰”构成。tangere 还给出 tangent、tactile、contagious、contiguous，整个词族都与“触碰”有关。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Contingere meant 'to touch, seize, come into contact with'. Its past participle contactus meant 'a touching', especially 'a touching of something unclean, contamination'.","cn":"contingere 意为“碰到、抓住、接触”。其过去分词 contactus 意为“一次触碰”，尤指“碰到不洁之物、污染”。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Tangere 'to touch, handle' comes from PIE *tag- 'to touch, handle', which also gives tangent, tactile, contagion and contiguous — all still about contact.","cn":"tangere“触碰、操作”来自原始印欧语 *tag-“触碰、操作”，它还给出 tangent、tactile、contagion、contiguous——全都与接触有关。"},{"era":"1620s ENGLISH","en":"The noun contact entered English in the 1620s with the literal sense 'action, state, or condition of touching'.","cn":"名词 contact 于 17 世纪 20 年代进入英语，字面义为“触碰的动作、状态或情形”。"},{"era":"1818–1860 ENGLISH","en":"The figurative sense 'a connection, communication' is recorded from 1818, and make contact from 1860 in reference to electrical circuits.","cn":"比喻义“联系、沟通”记录于 1818 年；make contact 则自 1860 年起用于电路语境。"},{"era":"1834–1927 ENGLISH","en":"The verb appeared in 1834 meaning 'to bring together or put in contact'. The sense 'get in touch with' is 1927 American English.","cn":"动词 1834 年出现，意为“使接触、使相连”。“与……取得联系”义是 1927 年的美式英语用法。"},{"era":"1888–1931 ENGLISH","en":"Contact lens is recorded in 1888, and the sense 'a person who can be called upon for assistance' in 1931. Both extend the idea of a meeting point.","cn":"contact lens 记录于 1888 年；“可被求助的人”这一义项记录于 1931 年。两者都延伸了“相遇之点”的想法。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group contains two tangere relatives and one trahere neighbour; the near-meaning group separates physical touch, connection and communication.","cn":"形近组包含两个 tangere 亲属和一个 trahere 近邻；近义组区分物理接触、连接与沟通。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"contract","ipa":"/ˈkɒntrækt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"an agreement, or to shrink. Its root is trahere 'draw', so it means 'draw together', not 'touch'.","definitionCN":"协议，或收缩。它的词根是 trahere“拉”，所以是“拉到一起”，而不是“触碰”。"},{"word":"contagion","ipa":"/kənˈteɪdʒən/","tag":"same root","definition":"the spreading of disease by contact. It descends from contingere through the idea of touching something infected.","definitionCN":"疾病通过接触传播。它经由“碰到被感染之物”这一想法从 contingere 传下来。"},{"word":"contiguous","ipa":"/kənˈtɪɡjuəs/","tag":"same root","definition":"touching along a border; next to each other. It keeps the literal surface-to-surface sense.","definitionCN":"沿边界相接的；毗邻的。它保留了字面上的“面与面相接”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"touch","ipa":"/tʌtʃ/","tag":"physical","definition":"to put a hand or an object against something. It is the plain verb for physical contact.","definitionCN":"把手或物体放到某物上。它是表示物理接触的普通动词。"},{"word":"connection","ipa":"/kəˈnekʃn/","tag":"link","definition":"a link or relationship between things or people. It is broader than contact and can be structural or social.","definitionCN":"事物或人之间的联系或关系。它比 contact 更宽，可指结构联系或社会关系。"},{"word":"communication","ipa":"/ˌkɒmjʊnɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"exchange of information","definition":"the exchange of information or ideas. Contact can be a single act, while communication is the ongoing exchange.","definitionCN":"信息或观念的交换。contact 可以是一次动作，而 communication 是持续的交流。"},{"word":"liaison","ipa":"/liˈeɪzn/","tag":"go-between","definition":"communication between groups, or a person who arranges it. It is formal and organizational.","definitionCN":"团体之间的沟通，或负责联络的人。它较正式，多用于组织语境。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: tangere 'touch', the same-root family tangent, tactile, contagious, contiguous, and the modern compounds contact lens and contactless.","cn":"只用真实构件：tangere“触碰”，同根词族 tangent、tactile、contagious、contiguous，以及现代复合词 contact lens、contactless。"},"normal":[{"en":"Tangere means 'touch'. Contact is the moment two surfaces meet; every other sense is a distance crossed.","cn":"tangere 意为“触碰”。contact 是两个表面相遇的那一刻；其他义项都是被跨越的距离。"},{"en":"Tangent, tactile, contagious and contiguous are all tangere relatives: a touching line, the sense of touch, disease spread by touch, and lands touching at a border.","cn":"tangent、tactile、contagious、contiguous 都是 tangere 的亲属：相切的线、触觉、靠接触传播的病，以及边界相接的土地。"},{"en":"A contact is also a person: the point where your line reaches an organization.","cn":"contact 也可以是一个人：你的线触及某个机构的那个点。"},{"en":"Switch the stress: the noun is CON-tact, the verb is con-TACT. English often marks noun and verb this way.","cn":"重音会移动：名词是 CON-tact，动词是 con-TACT。英语常用这种方式区分名词与动词。"},{"en":"Contactless payment is named by negation: the card never touches the reader, yet the connection still happens.","cn":"contactless payment 用否定命名：卡根本没有碰到读卡器，可连接仍然发生了。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two circles approaching until their edges meet at one point. Everything that passes between them must pass through that point.","cn":"想象两个圆靠近，直到边缘在某一点相接。两圆之间传递的一切，都必须经过那一点。"},{"en":"The point can be physical (two surfaces), electrical (two conductors), social (two people), or informational (a message reaching someone).","cn":"这个点可以是物理的（两个表面）、电气的（两个导体）、社会的（两个人），或信息的（一条消息抵达某人）。"},{"en":"Because contact names the meeting point rather than the journey, one word covers a handshake, a phone call, and a live wire.","cn":"因为 contact 命名的是相遇之点而不是旅程，一个词就能覆盖握手、电话和带电的导线。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Wash your hands after contact with raw meat.","cn":"接触生肉后要洗手。"},{"en":"I lost contact with him after he moved abroad.","cn":"他移居国外后我就和他失去了联系。"},{"en":"The nurse is the family's main contact at the hospital.","cn":"这位护士是家属在医院的主要联系人。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·塔克特”——肯（定）塔（上）克（服）特（远）的距离，一碰就联系上 → contact 接触、联系","word":"contact"},"root":"源自拉丁语 contactus“触碰”，出自 contingere“碰到、抓住”，由 com-“一起”+ tangere“触碰”构成，核心是“两个表面相遇的那一点”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of contact, all built on one meeting point. Two surfaces, two wires, two people, a lens and an eye, or a visitor and a desk — the word names the point where something passes across.","cn":"contact 的九个义项都建立在一个相遇点上。两个表面、两根导线、两个人、镜片与眼球，或访客与接待台——这个词命名的都是“某物跨越过去”的那一点。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two edges meeting at a single point, with something passing through it.","cn":"核心意象：两条边缘在一点相接，有东西正从这一点穿过。"},"chain":["APPROACH","MEET","TOUCH","CONNECT","COMMUNICATE","THE POINT ITSELF"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 09","en":"PHYSICAL TOUCHING: surfaces meet in paint and air, and bodies meet in contact sports.","cn":"物理接触：表面在油漆与空气中相接，身体在接触型运动中相撞。"},{"senses":"02 · 04 · 07","en":"COMMUNICATION: messages and visits are ways of touching across distance, and in contact with keeps the line open.","cn":"沟通：消息与拜访是跨越距离的“触碰”，in contact with 则让这条线保持畅通。"},{"senses":"03 · 08","en":"THE MEETING POINT AS A PERSON OR PLACE: a contact is someone who can be reached, and a point of contact is where the transfer happens.","cn":"作为人或地点的相遇点：contact 是可以找到的人，point of contact 是传递发生的地方。"},{"senses":"05","en":"ELECTRICAL CONTACT: conductors touch so that current can pass; make contact began here.","cn":"电接触：导体相碰使电流通过；make contact 最早就在这里使用。"},{"senses":"06","en":"A LENS ON THE EYE: contact lens is named for sitting directly against the eye rather than standing off it.","cn":"贴在眼球上的镜片：contact lens 因直接贴住眼球、而非悬在眼前而得名。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Contact is a Latin participle used as a noun and then converted into a verb, with the stress shifting. English adds -less, -able, -or and -ee.","cn":"contact 是拉丁语分词，先用作名词，再转成动词，重音随之移动。英语加 -less、-able、-or、-ee 构词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin tangere family is broad and real: contingere, contactus, tangens 'touching', contagio 'contact, contagion', and contiguus 'touching, neighbouring'.","cn":"拉丁 tangere 词族庞大而真实：contingere、contactus、tangens“接触的”、contagio“接触、传染”、contiguus“相接的、毗邻的”。"},"items":[{"word":"contact","structure":"con- (together) + tact- (touched) + -Ø (noun or verb)","meaning":"a touching; communication; to get in touch","meaningCN":"接触；联系；联络","example":"Keep the two wires in contact.","exampleCN":"让两根导线保持接触。"},{"word":"contactless","structure":"contact + -less (without)","meaning":"working without physical touching","meaningCN":"非接触式的（-less 表没有）","example":"She paid with a contactless card.","exampleCN":"她用感应卡付款。"},{"word":"contactable","structure":"contact + -able (able to be)","meaning":"able to be reached","meaningCN":"可联系到的（-able 表可能）","example":"The doctor is contactable at night.","exampleCN":"这位医生夜间也能联系到。"},{"word":"contactor","structure":"contact + -or (device)","meaning":"an electrical switch operated by a coil","meaningCN":"接触器（-or 表装置）","example":"The contactor failed and the pump stopped.","exampleCN":"接触器失灵，泵停了。"},{"word":"contactee","structure":"contact + -ee (person acted on)","meaning":"a person who has been contacted, especially by aliens","meaningCN":"被接触者（-ee 表受动者）","example":"The contactee described a bright light.","exampleCN":"被接触者描述了一道强光。"},{"word":"contagion","structure":"con- + tag- (touch) + -ion (noun)","meaning":"the spreading of disease or ideas by contact","meaningCN":"传染；蔓延（同一词根的名词）","example":"The contagion spread through the dormitory.","exampleCN":"传染病在宿舍里蔓延。"},{"word":"contagious","structure":"contagion + -ous (adjective)","meaning":"able to be passed on by contact","meaningCN":"有传染性的（-ous 构成形容词）","example":"Her laughter was contagious.","exampleCN":"她的笑声很有感染力。"},{"word":"contiguous","structure":"con- + tig- (touch) + -uous (adjective)","meaning":"touching at a border; adjacent","meaningCN":"毗邻的；相接的（同一词根）","example":"The two states are contiguous.","exampleCN":"这两个州相邻。"},{"word":"tangent","structure":"tang- (touching) + -ent (adjective and noun)","meaning":"a line that touches a curve at one point","meaningCN":"切线（同一词根）","example":"Draw a tangent to the circle.","exampleCN":"画一条与圆相切的线。"},{"word":"tactile","structure":"tact- (touch) + -ile (adjective)","meaning":"relating to the sense of touch","meaningCN":"触觉的（同一词根）","example":"The fabric has a pleasant tactile feel.","exampleCN":"这种面料手感舒适。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"contingere","structure":"con- + tangere","meaning":"to touch, seize, come into contact","meaningCN":"碰到；抓住；接触"},{"word":"tangere","structure":"PIE *tag-","meaning":"to touch, handle","meaningCN":"触碰；操作"},{"word":"contactus","structure":"past participle of contingere","meaning":"a touching, contact","meaningCN":"触碰；接触"}]}},{"word":"contemporary","ipa_uk":"/kənˈtemprəri/","ipa_us":"/kənˈtempəreri/","definition_zh":"当代的；现代的；同时代的；同代人","definition_en":"belonging to the present time, or living or existing at the same time as someone or something else","core_image":"两条平行的时间线上，两个点在同一刻度上竖直对齐","scene":"展厅墙上挂着一幅抽象画，旁边的展签只写了年份。 The gallery label described the abstract painting as contemporary art from the year 2000 onward.","sceneCN":"这里 contemporary 是「当代的、当下的」（第 3、4 个义项：属于现今时代、当代艺术风格）；句意：展签把这幅抽象画归为 2000 年以来的当代艺术。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"当代的；现代的；同时代的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"同代人；同时期的人"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"contemporary art","zh":"当代艺术"},{"phrase":"contemporary society","zh":"当代社会"},{"phrase":"be contemporary with","zh":"与……处于同一时期"},{"phrase":"a contemporary of","zh":"……的同时代人"},{"phrase":"contemporary literature","zh":"当代文学"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more contemporary"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most contemporary"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contemporaneous","pos":"adj.","zh":"同时发生的；同一时期的"},{"word":"contemporaneously","pos":"adv.","zh":"同时地；在同一时期"},{"word":"contemporaneity","pos":"n.","zh":"同时代性；当代性"},{"word":"contemporarily","pos":"adv.","zh":"以当代的方式；在当代"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Living or existing at the same time","titleCN":"同时代的：活在同一段时间里","definition":"of two people or things, existing or happening in the same period of history","definitionCN":"（两个人或物）存在于或发生在同一个历史时期","example":"Mozart and Haydn were contemporary composers.","exampleCN":"莫扎特与海顿是同时代的作曲家。","why":"Latin com- 'together' + tempus 'time': the word literally means 'sharing time'. Two lives overlapping on the timeline are contemporary.","whyCN":"拉丁语 com-“一起”加 tempus“时间”：这个词字面就是“共享时间”。两条生命在时间线上重叠，就是同时代的。"},{"no":"02","title":"A person of the same period","titleCN":"同代人：同一时期里的人","definition":"the noun for a person living at the same time as another person","definitionCN":"名词，指与另一个人生活在同一时期的人","example":"She was a contemporary of the poet at university.","exampleCN":"她在大学时与那位诗人是同时代的人。","why":"The noun arrived in the 1630s, originally as cotemporary. A contemporary is literally a 'time-fellow', a word English also tried before settling on the Latin form.","whyCN":"名词在 17 世纪 30 年代出现，最初写作 cotemporary。contemporary 字面就是“时间同伴”，英语此前也试过同样意思的本族词。"},{"no":"03","title":"Belonging to the present","titleCN":"当代的：属于现在这个时代","definition":"belonging to the present period rather than the past","definitionCN":"属于现今时期，而非过去","example":"The course focuses on contemporary Chinese society.","exampleCN":"这门课程聚焦当代中国社会。","why":"The sense 'modern, characteristic of the present' is recorded from 1805. Once 'same time' is applied to the speaker's own time, it means 'now'.","whyCN":"“现代的、具有当下特征的”这一义项记录于 1805 年。当“同一时间”被用来指说话者自己所处的时间，它就成了“现在”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Contemporary art and style","titleCN":"当代艺术：当下正在发生的风格","definition":"in art, music and design, describing work produced in the present era, often with current techniques and concerns","definitionCN":"在艺术、音乐与设计中，指当下时代创作、常带当下技法与议题的作品","example":"The gallery shows contemporary painting from Asia.","exampleCN":"这家画廊展出亚洲的当代绘画。","why":"In art history, 'modern' and 'contemporary' are separate periods; contemporary means the art being made now, not a fixed historical movement.","whyCN":"在艺术史中，modern 与 contemporary 是两个不同时期；contemporary 指正在被创作的艺术，而不是一个固定的历史流派。"},{"no":"05","title":"Contemporary with: coexisting","titleCN":"与……同期：formal 的并存表达","definition":"the phrase contemporary with states that two things belong to the same period","definitionCN":"短语 contemporary with 表示两样事物属于同一时期","example":"The temple is contemporary with the first city wall.","exampleCN":"这座神庙与第一道城墙属于同一时期。","why":"With marks the second point on the timeline. The phrase is common in archaeology and history, where dates are approximate.","whyCN":"with 标记时间线上的第二个点。该短语常用于考古与历史，因为那里的年代只是近似值。"},{"no":"06","title":"Contemporaneous: the scientific doublet","titleCN":"contemporaneous：同时发生的（学术双式）","definition":"a formal adjective meaning happening at the same time, used in science and history","definitionCN":"正式的形容词，意为同时发生的，用于科学与历史","example":"The two eruptions were roughly contemporaneous.","exampleCN":"两次喷发大致同时发生。","why":"Contemporaneous comes from Latin contemporaneus, a parallel form. English keeps both, using the shorter word for people and art, the longer one for events.","whyCN":"contemporaneous 来自拉丁语 contemporaneus，是一个平行形式。英语两者都保留：短词用于人和艺术，长词用于事件。"},{"no":"07","title":"The contemporary period","titleCN":"当代：作为一段历史时期","definition":"the period of history that includes the present, especially the recent decades","definitionCN":"包含当下的历史时期，尤指最近数十年","example":"Contemporary history begins roughly in 1945.","exampleCN":"当代史大致从 1945 年开始。","why":"A period can be named by its relation to the speaker: whatever overlaps with now is contemporary, so the label moves forward with time.","whyCN":"一段时期可以按它与说话者的关系来命名：凡与“现在”重叠的都是当代，所以这个标签会随时间向前移动。"},{"no":"08","title":"Present-day: the adjective of now","titleCN":"现今的：描述此刻的状态","definition":"describing the state of something as it is now, in contrast to an earlier form","definitionCN":"描述某物此刻的状态，与早先的形式相对","example":"Contemporary readers find the novel's pace slow.","exampleCN":"当代读者觉得这部小说的节奏慢。","why":"This sense is relational: a 'contemporary reader' is not a type of person but a reader placed at the same time as the text's present.","whyCN":"这一义项是关系性的：“当代读者”不是一类人，而是被放在与文本当下同一时间点上的读者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Contemporary is Latin com- 'with' + tempus 'time', through Medieval Latin contemporarius. English took the adjective in the 1630s, the noun in the same decade (originally cotemporary), and the 'modern' sense in 1805.","cn":"contemporary 是拉丁语 com-“一起”加 tempus“时间”，经中世纪拉丁语 contemporarius 而来。英语在 17 世纪 30 年代借入形容词，同年代借入名词（最初写作 cotemporary），1805 年发展出“现代的”义项。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Tempus (genitive temporis) meant 'time, season, portion of time'. It is traced to Proto-Italic *tempos- 'stretch, measure', from PIE *temp-os 'stretched', root *ten- 'to stretch' — time as a stretch.","cn":"tempus（属格 temporis）意为“时间、季节、一段时间”。它被追溯到原始意大利语 *tempos-“延展、度量”，再往上为原始印欧语 *temp-os“伸展的”，词根 *ten-“拉伸”——时间就是一段被拉开的长度。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN","en":"Contemporarius combined com- 'with, together' and temporarius 'of time'. The word existed in Medieval Latin before English borrowed it.","cn":"contemporarius 把 com-“一起”与 temporarius“时间的”组合起来。这个词在英语借入之前已存在于中世纪拉丁语中。"},{"era":"1630s ENGLISH","en":"The adjective contemporary is recorded in the 1630s meaning 'occurring, living, or existing at the same time'. The noun followed in the same decade, first as cotemporary.","cn":"形容词 contemporary 在 17 世纪 30 年代被记录，意为“同时发生、生活或存在的”。名词在同一时期随后出现，最初写作 cotemporary。"},{"era":"18C ENGLISH","en":"The form cotemporary, built on co- + temporary, was common in the 18th century. The Latin-shaped contemporary eventually displaced it.","cn":"由 co- + temporary 构成的 cotemporary 在 18 世纪很常见。最终，拉丁形态的 contemporary 取代了它。"},{"era":"1805 ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'modern, characteristic of the present' (in art, literature and society) is recorded from 1805.","cn":"“现代的、具有当下特征的”（用于艺术、文学与社会）这一义项记录于 1805 年。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps both relations: contemporary with someone (same period) and contemporary art (the art of now). The overlap of 'same time' and 'our time' is built into the word.","cn":"现代英语保留两种关系：contemporary with someone（同一时期）与 contemporary art（当下的艺术）。“同一时间”与“我们的时间”的重叠，就写在这个词里。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the tempus family from one near-spelling; the near-meaning group contrasts 'now' with 'of the same period'.","cn":"形近组把 tempus 词族与一个近形词分开；近义组对比“当下的”与“同一时期的”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"temporary","ipa":"/ˈtempərəri/","tag":"near spelling, shorter prefix","definition":"lasting only for a limited time. It shares tempor- 'time' but has no con-, so it means short-lived rather than same-time.","definitionCN":"只持续有限时间的。它共享 tempor-“时间”，但没有 con-，所以意思是“短暂的”而非“同时的”。"},{"word":"contemporaneous","ipa":"/kənˌtempəˈreɪniəs/","tag":"same root, formal doublet","definition":"happening at the same time. It is the longer Latin form, used mainly of events rather than people or art.","definitionCN":"同时发生的。它是较长的拉丁形式，主要用于事件，而非人或艺术。"},{"word":"cotemporary","ipa":"/kəʊˈtempərəri/","tag":"older variant","definition":"an 18th-century variant of contemporary built on co- + temporary. It is now archaic.","definitionCN":"18 世纪由 co- + temporary 构成的 contemporary 变体，现已古旧。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"modern","ipa":"/ˈmɒdn/","tag":"of the recent era","definition":"belonging to a recent period, especially one that broke with tradition. It can name a historical period, not just 'now'.","definitionCN":"属于较近时期的，尤指与传统决裂的时期。它可以命名一个历史时期，而不只是“现在”。"},{"word":"current","ipa":"/ˈkʌrənt/","tag":"in use now","definition":"existing or in use at the present moment. It stresses validity now, as with prices and rules.","definitionCN":"此刻存在或正在使用的。它强调“此刻有效”，如价格与规则。"},{"word":"present-day","ipa":"/ˌpriːznt ˈdeɪ/","tag":"now, contrasted with past","definition":"existing now, used when comparing the present with an earlier time. It is a compound and needs no article.","definitionCN":"现今存在的，用于把现在与更早时期对比。它是复合词，不需要冠词。"},{"word":"coeval","ipa":"/kəʊˈiːvl/","tag":"same age, formal","definition":"of the same age or period. It is literary and precise, and does not mean 'modern' at all.","definitionCN":"同龄的；同一时期的。它文学化且精确，完全没有“现代”的意思。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: con- 'together' + tempus 'time', the relatives temporary, contemporaneous and coeval, and the art-world contrast modern / contemporary.","cn":"只用真实构件：con-“一起”+ tempus“时间”，亲属词 temporary、contemporaneous、coeval，以及艺术界的 modern / contemporary 对比。"},"normal":[{"en":"Con- 'together' + tempus 'time': contemporary people share a slice of the timeline.","cn":"con-“一起”加 tempus“时间”：同时代的人共享时间线上的一段。"},{"en":"Temporary is the same time-word without con-: it lasts for a time, but it does not share time with anyone.","cn":"temporary 是同一个“时间”词但没有 con-：它持续一段时间，但不与任何人共享时间。"},{"en":"In art history, modern is a period (roughly 1860s–1970s) and contemporary is the art of now; they are not synonyms.","cn":"在艺术史中，modern 是一个时期（大致 19 世纪 60 年代至 20 世纪 70 年代），contemporary 是当下的艺术；它们不是同义词。"},{"en":"Contemporaneous is the longer doublet for events, as in 'two contemporaneous eruptions'.","cn":"contemporaneous 是用于事件的较长双式词，如“两次同时期的喷发”。"},{"en":"A contemporary of Mozart is not a modern person; the 'same time' sense still points to the 18th century.","cn":"a contemporary of Mozart 不是现代人；“同一时间”这一义项仍指向 18 世纪。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two clocks started at different moments but running at the same rate. Whenever their hands point to the same hour, they are contemporary for that stretch.","cn":"想象两只在不同时刻启动、但走速相同的钟。只要指针指向同一刻度，那一段它们就是“同时的”。"},{"en":"Now tilt the picture: if one clock is the present, everything whose hands still move today is contemporary in the modern sense.","cn":"现在把图倾斜一下：如果一只钟代表现在，那么指针今天仍在走动的，都是现代意义上的“当代的”。"},{"en":"The word therefore holds two directions at once: sideways to other people, and forward to our own moment.","cn":"所以这个词同时持有两个方向：横向指向他人，纵向指向我们自己的此刻。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The building is contemporary with the oldest bridge in town.","cn":"这栋建筑与镇上最古老的桥属于同一时期。"},{"en":"Contemporary music often mixes live instruments with digital sound.","cn":"当代音乐常把原声乐器与数字音效混合。"},{"en":"As a contemporary of the king, he witnessed the whole court.","cn":"作为国王的同时代人，他见证了整套宫廷生活。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·坦普·惹瑞”——肯（定）和坦普（time 时间）惹（上）瑞（同一批）人，都是一个年代的 → contemporary 同时代的、当代的","word":"contemporary"},"root":"源自拉丁语 com-“一起”+ tempus“时间”，经中世纪拉丁语 contemporarius 而来，核心是“共享同一段时间”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of contemporary, all built on shared time. Two lives, two buildings, an artwork and a reader can each be placed on the same vertical line of the timeline; the only question is whose 'now' is being measured.","cn":"contemporary 的八个义项都建立在“共享时间”上。两条生命、两座建筑、一件艺术品和一位读者，都可以被放在时间线的同一竖直刻度上；唯一的问题是：衡量的是谁的“现在”。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two points on parallel timelines, aligned on the same vertical tick.","cn":"核心意象：两条平行时间线上的两个点，对齐在同一个竖直刻度上。"},"chain":["TIME","SHARED SLICE","SAME PERIOD","PEER","OUR PERIOD","OF NOW"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"SAME PERIOD: two people, buildings or events occupy the same span, marked by with.","cn":"同一时期：两个人、两座建筑或两个事件占据同一段跨度，用 with 标记。"},{"senses":"02 · 07","en":"PEERS AND PERIODS: a contemporary is a person of the era, and contemporary history is the period that includes now.","cn":"同代人与时期：contemporary 是那个时代的人，当代史则是包含现在的时期。"},{"senses":"03 · 04 · 08","en":"OUR OWN TIME: applied to the speaker's moment, 'same time' becomes 'modern', and contemporary art is the art being made now.","cn":"我们自己的时间：当用于说话者的此刻，“同一时间”就变成“现代的”，当代艺术就是正在被创作的艺术。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE FORMAL DOUBLET: contemporaneous keeps the Latin shape and is used for events, not people.","cn":"正式双式词：contemporaneous 保留拉丁形态，用于事件而非人。"},{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE NOUN TURN: cotemporary began as 'time-fellow', and the noun still names a person who shares the clock.","cn":"名词化：cotemporary 最初意为“时间同伴”，名词至今仍指共享同一只钟的人。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Contemporary is con- + tempor- + -ary. English adds -aneous, -aneously, -aneity and -arily to build the rest of the family, all still about time.","cn":"contemporary 是 con- + tempor- + -ary。英语再加 -aneous、-aneously、-aneity、-arily 构成其余词族，全都仍围绕时间。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin tempus family is real: temporarius 'of time', temporalis 'temporal', contemporarius, and contemporaneus. English also borrowed temporary and temporal directly.","cn":"拉丁 tempus 词族真实：temporarius“时间的”、temporalis“时间的”、contemporarius、contemporaneus。英语还直接借入 temporary 与 temporal。"},"items":[{"word":"contemporary","structure":"con- (together) + tempor- (time) + -ary (adjective)","meaning":"of the same time, or of the present","meaningCN":"同时代的；当代的","example":"He is a contemporary of the novelist.","exampleCN":"他是那位小说家的同时代人。"},{"word":"contemporaneous","structure":"con- + tempor- + -aneous (adjective)","meaning":"happening at the same time","meaningCN":"同时发生的（-aneous 构成形容词）","example":"The two events were contemporaneous.","exampleCN":"这两个事件同时发生。"},{"word":"contemporaneously","structure":"contemporaneous + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"at the same time","meaningCN":"同时地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The files were contemporaneously recorded.","exampleCN":"这些文件是当时同步记录的。"},{"word":"contemporaneity","structure":"contemporaneous + -ity (noun)","meaning":"the quality of being of the same time or of the present","meaningCN":"同时代性；当代性（-ity 构成抽象名词）","example":"Critics debate the contemporaneity of the play.","exampleCN":"评论家争论这部戏的当代性。"},{"word":"contemporarily","structure":"contemporary + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a contemporary way, or at the present time","meaningCN":"以当代方式；在当代（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The hall was contemporarily furnished.","exampleCN":"大厅的陈设是当代风格。"},{"word":"contemporariness","structure":"contemporary + -ness (noun)","meaning":"the state of being contemporary","meaningCN":"当代性；同时代的状态","example":"The work's contemporariness is its selling point.","exampleCN":"这件作品的当代性正是卖点。"},{"word":"cotemporary","structure":"co- (with) + temporary","meaning":"an older variant of contemporary","meaningCN":"contemporary 的旧式变体","example":"Cotemporary was common in the 18th century.","exampleCN":"cotemporary 在 18 世纪很常见。"},{"word":"temporary","structure":"tempor- (time) + -ary","meaning":"lasting only for a time","meaningCN":"暂时的；临时的（同一词根，无 con-）","example":"She took a temporary job for the summer.","exampleCN":"她夏天做了一份临时工作。"},{"word":"temporal","structure":"tempor- + -al","meaning":"relating to time, or to the worldly world","meaningCN":"时间的；世俗的（同一词根）","example":"The novel plays with temporal order.","exampleCN":"这部小说玩弄时间顺序。"},{"word":"extemporaneous","structure":"ex- (out of) + tempor- + -aneous","meaning":"spoken or done without preparation, literally 'out of time'","meaningCN":"即席的；临场的（字面“时间之外”）","example":"He gave an extemporaneous speech.","exampleCN":"他作了一次即席演讲。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"tempus","structure":"PIE *temp-os (stretch)","meaning":"time, season, portion of time","meaningCN":"时间；季节；一段时间"},{"word":"contemporarius","structure":"com- + temporarius","meaning":"of the same time","meaningCN":"同一时间的；同时代的"},{"word":"contemporaneus","structure":"com- + temporaneus","meaning":"contemporaneous, of the same time","meaningCN":"同时代的；同时发生的"}]}},{"word":"context","ipa_uk":"/ˈkɒntekst/","ipa_us":"/ˈkɑːntekst/","definition_zh":"上下文；语境；背景；环境","definition_en":"the words that come before and after a word, or the situation in which something happens and which gives it meaning","core_image":"一根线把散落的词语前后编织在一起，围住中间那个词","scene":"课文上，荧光笔圈出一个单词，前后两句都被标了线。 Before guessing the meaning, she read the sentences on either side of the word to judge its context.","sceneCN":"这里 context 是「上下文」（第 1、3 个义项：一个词前后的文字、决定其含义的语境）；句意：猜意思之前，她先读了这个词前后的句子，以判断它的上下文。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"上下文；语境；背景；环境"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（计算机）上下文；运行环境"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"in the context of","zh":"在……的背景下；在……语境中"},{"phrase":"out of context","zh":"断章取义；脱离语境"},{"phrase":"historical context","zh":"历史背景"},{"phrase":"social context","zh":"社会背景"},{"phrase":"put something in context","zh":"把某事物放到背景中理解"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"contexts"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contextual","pos":"adj.","zh":"语境的；上下文的；背景的"},{"word":"contextually","pos":"adv.","zh":"从语境上看；在上下文中"},{"word":"contextualize","pos":"vt.","zh":"把……置于语境中；结合背景理解"},{"word":"contextualization","pos":"n.","zh":"语境化；置于背景中"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The words around a word","titleCN":"上下文：一个词前后的文字","definition":"the parts of a text that come immediately before and after a particular word or passage","definitionCN":"紧挨着某个词或段落之前与之后的文本部分","example":"You can guess the word's meaning from the context.","exampleCN":"你可以从上下文猜出这个词的意思。","why":"Latin contexere is com- 'together' + texere 'to weave'. The surrounding words are woven around the unknown one, and the pattern tells you what it must mean.","whyCN":"拉丁语 contexere 由 com-“一起”加 texere“编织”构成。周围的词被编织在未知词四周，图案本身就告诉你它必然是什么意思。"},{"no":"02","title":"The situation something happens in","titleCN":"背景：事情发生的处境","definition":"the circumstances and conditions that surround an event and help explain it","definitionCN":"围绕一个事件并有助于解释它的环境与条件","example":"The decision must be understood in its historical context.","exampleCN":"这个决定必须放到历史背景中才能理解。","why":"The 1560s sense extended from neighbouring words to neighbouring circumstances: whatever surrounds a thing becomes part of its meaning.","whyCN":"16 世纪 60 年代的义项从“相邻的词语”扩展到“相邻的处境”：围绕一个事物的一切，都成为它意义的一部分。"},{"no":"03","title":"The conditions that give meaning","titleCN":"语境：赋予意义的条件","definition":"the set of facts, conventions or beliefs that make a statement meaningful or intelligible","definitionCN":"使一句话有意义或可理解的一组事实、惯例或信念","example":"Without that context, the joke makes no sense.","exampleCN":"没有那个语境，这个笑话完全讲不通。","why":"A sentence alone is a thread without a pattern. Context supplies the other threads that turn it into cloth.","whyCN":"单独一句话是一根没有图案的线。语境提供其余的线，把它织成布。"},{"no":"04","title":"In the context of: within a frame","titleCN":"in the context of：在某个框架内","definition":"the fixed phrase meaning 'considered within the frame of' a subject, period or system","definitionCN":"固定短语，意为“在某个主题、时期或体系的框架内来看”","example":"In the context of climate policy, the tax makes sense.","exampleCN":"在气候政策的背景下，这项税是合理的。","why":"The phrase sets a frame first, then places the thing inside it. Without the frame, the judgement has no scale.","whyCN":"这个短语先设好框架，再把事物放进去。没有框架，判断就没有尺度。"},{"no":"05","title":"Out of context: misrepresented","titleCN":"out of context：断章取义","definition":"quoted or reported in a way that leaves out the surrounding words and so distorts the meaning","definitionCN":"引用或报道时略去周围文字，从而扭曲原意","example":"The quotation was taken out of context and sounded cruel.","exampleCN":"这段引文被断章取义，听起来很刻薄。","why":"Cut a thread out of the cloth and it can be laid into any pattern. Out of context means the surrounding weave has been removed.","whyCN":"把一根线从布上剪下来，它就能被放进任何图案。out of context 的意思是：周围的编织被抽走了。"},{"no":"06","title":"Historical or social context","titleCN":"历史背景、社会背景","definition":"the specific period, culture or social conditions that surround a work, event or idea","definitionCN":"围绕作品、事件或观念的具体时期、文化或社会条件","example":"The novel reflects the social context of the 1930s.","exampleCN":"这部小说反映了 20 世纪 30 年代的社会背景。","why":"Historians use context as a tool: a fact removed from its period cannot be judged, because the standards of judgement were also part of that period.","whyCN":"历史学家把背景当作工具：脱离时代的事实无法被评判，因为评判标准本身也属于那个时代。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contextual: depending on the surroundings","titleCN":"contextual：依赖语境的","definition":"the adjective describing meaning or behaviour that changes with the surrounding situation","definitionCN":"形容词，描述随周围情境而变化的含义或行为","example":"The meaning of 'cool' is highly contextual.","exampleCN":"cool 这个词的含义高度依赖语境。","why":"The -al suffix turns the frame into a property: a word's meaning can be contextual, meaning it cannot be fixed without the weave around it.","whyCN":"-al 后缀把框架变成一种属性：一个词的意义可以是“语境性的”，即离开周围的编织就无法固定。"},{"no":"08","title":"Contextualize: place in a frame","titleCN":"contextualize：把事物放回背景中","definition":"to show or explain something by placing it in its surrounding circumstances","definitionCN":"把某事物放回其周围处境中，以显示或解释它","example":"The exhibition contextualizes the paintings with letters and photographs.","exampleCN":"展览用书信和照片为这些画作提供背景。","why":"The -ize suffix makes a verb of the frame: you build the weave around the object so that others can see it correctly.","whyCN":"-ize 后缀把框架变成动词：你在对象周围搭出编织，让别人能正确地看见它。"},{"no":"09","title":"Context in computing","titleCN":"计算机中的上下文","definition":"in computing, the stored state or environment that a process needs in order to continue correctly","definitionCN":"计算机中，一个进程为正确继续运行而需要保存的状态或环境","example":"The switch saves the context before loading the next task.","exampleCN":"切换前会保存上下文，再载入下一个任务。","why":"A running program is also a thread of events; its context is everything around the current instruction that gives it meaning and lets it resume.","whyCN":"运行中的程序也是一条事件之线；它的上下文就是当前指令周围的一切，赋予它意义并让它能够继续。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Context is Latin contextus 'a joining together', the past participle of contexere 'to weave together', from com- 'together' + texere 'to weave'. Text, textile, texture and pretext are all relatives.","cn":"context 是拉丁语 contextus“编织在一起之物”，即 contexere“一起编织”的过去分词，由 com-“一起”加 texere“编织”构成。text、textile、texture、pretext 都是它的亲属。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Contexere meant 'to weave together, join, connect'. Its past participle contextus meant 'a joining together', and the noun could name the whole fabric of a speech or writing.","cn":"contexere 意为“编织在一起、连接”。其过去分词 contextus 意为“连接在一起”，名词可以指一篇讲话或文章的整体织体。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Texere 'to weave, make' comes from PIE *teks- 'to weave, fabricate'. The same root gives text, textile, texture, tissue and pretext.","cn":"texere“编织、制作”来自原始印欧语 *teks-“编织、制造”。同一词根给出 text、textile、texture、tissue、pretext。"},{"era":"EARLY 15C ENGLISH","en":"English recorded context meaning 'a composition, a chronicle, the entire text of a writing'. The word still meant the whole woven work.","cn":"英语记录的 context 意为“一篇作品、一部编年史、整篇文字”。当时这个词仍指整件编织成的作品。"},{"era":"1560s ENGLISH","en":"The modern sense — 'the parts of a writing which precede or follow, and are directly connected with, some other part referred to or quoted' — is recorded from the 1560s.","cn":"现代义——“一段文字中位于某处之前或之后、并与之直接相连的部分”——记录于 16 世纪 60 年代。"},{"era":"19C–20C ENGLISH","en":"The word expanded from text to situation: historical context, social context and 'the context of an event'. The metaphor of surrounding weave travels easily.","cn":"这个词从文本扩展到情境：historical context、social context、“事件的背景”。周围编织的比喻很容易迁移。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Contextual (1822), contextualize (1934) and the computing sense all keep the same picture: a thing is understood only inside the fabric around it.","cn":"contextual（1822 年）、contextualize（1934 年）以及计算机义都保留同一幅画面：事物只有处在周围的织体里才能被理解。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the texere family plus one near-spelling; the near-meaning group separates surroundings, background and situation.","cn":"形近组是 texere 词族加一个近形词；近义组区分“周围环境”“背景”与“处境”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"contest","ipa":"/ˈkɒntest/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"a competition, or to challenge. Its root is testari 'witness', not texere, so it means 'call to witness', not 'weave'.","definitionCN":"竞赛，或质疑。它的词根是 testari“见证”，不是 texere，所以意思是“传唤证人”，而不是“编织”。"},{"word":"pretext","ipa":"/ˈpriːtekst/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"a false reason given to hide the real one. Prae- 'before' + texere 'weave' = a story woven in front.","definitionCN":"为掩盖真实原因而给出的假理由。prae-“在前”加 texere“编织”＝在前面织出的一层故事。"},{"word":"texture","ipa":"/ˈtekstʃə/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"the feel or arrangement of a surface. It is the noun of texere, the woven quality of a thing.","definitionCN":"表面的手感或排列方式。它是 texere 的名词，指事物被编织出来的质地。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"setting","ipa":"/ˈsetɪŋ/","tag":"place and time","definition":"the place and time in which a story or event occurs. It is the physical or narrative frame, narrower than context.","definitionCN":"故事或事件发生的地点与时间。它是物理或叙事框架，比 context 窄。"},{"word":"background","ipa":"/ˈbækɡraʊnd/","tag":"what lies behind","definition":"the history or conditions behind an event. It is what you need to know beforehand, not what surrounds it now.","definitionCN":"事件背后的历史或条件。它是事先需要知道的东西，而不是此刻围绕它的一切。"},{"word":"circumstances","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkəmstənsɪz/","tag":"conditions","definition":"the facts and conditions affecting a situation. It is concrete and often about money, time or health.","definitionCN":"影响某一情境的事实与条件。它较具体，常涉及金钱、时间或健康。"},{"word":"situation","ipa":"/ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃn/","tag":"state of affairs","definition":"the state of affairs at a particular time and place. It names the scene itself, while context names what gives it meaning.","definitionCN":"特定时间与地点的事态。它命名场景本身，而 context 命名赋予其意义的东西。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: texere 'weave', the relatives text, textile, texture, pretext, and the fixed phrases in context and out of context.","cn":"只用真实构件：texere“编织”，亲属词 text、textile、texture、pretext，以及固定短语 in context、out of context。"},"normal":[{"en":"Texere means 'weave'. Context is the cloth woven around a word; pull the word out and the pattern is lost.","cn":"texere 意为“编织”。context 就是围着一个词织成的布；把词抽出来，图案就没了。"},{"en":"Text, textile and texture all share the same weave: written words, woven cloth, and the feel of a surface.","cn":"text、textile、texture 共享同一个“编织”：写下的文字、织成的布、表面的质地。"},{"en":"Pretext is a weave placed in front to hide something; context is the weave around something that reveals it.","cn":"pretext 是织在前面用来遮掩的布；context 是织在周围、揭示意义的布。"},{"en":"Out of context is a cutting: the thread is real, but the pattern that gave it meaning has been removed.","cn":"out of context 是一块剪下来的布：线是真的，但赋予它意义的图案被抽走了。"},{"en":"In the context of sets a frame first; contextualize is the verb for building that frame for someone else.","cn":"in the context of 先设框架；contextualize 则是为别人搭出这个框架的动词。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a single dark thread in a patterned cloth. Seen alone it is just a line; seen in the weave it is part of a shape.","cn":"想象一块有图案的布中一根深色线。单独看它只是一条线；放回编织里，它就是图形的一部分。"},{"en":"The weave can be made of words (linguistic context), dates (historical context), customs (social context), or saved state (computing context).","cn":"这块编织可以由词语（语言语境）、年代（历史背景）、习俗（社会背景）或保存的状态（计算机上下文）构成。"},{"en":"The word therefore always answers a silent question: 'surrounded by what?'","cn":"所以这个词总在回答一个无声的问题：“被什么包围着？”"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The phrase is ambiguous until you see it in context.","cn":"这句话在看清上下文之前是有歧义的。"},{"en":"His remarks were quoted out of context by the newspaper.","cn":"报纸断章取义地引用了他的话。"},{"en":"The painting needs to be understood in the context of the war.","cn":"这幅画需要放在战争背景下理解。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·泰克斯特”——肯（定）把 text（文字）前后的线索都编到一块儿 → context 上下文、语境","word":"context"},"root":"源自拉丁语 contextus“编织在一起”，出自 contexere（com-“一起”+ texere“编织”），核心是“把周围的词语与情境织成一圈”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of context, all built on one weave. Words, situations, historical periods, social customs and even a computer's saved state are the cloth around a thing; without the cloth, the thread has no pattern.","cn":"context 的九个义项都建立在一块编织上。词语、处境、历史时期、社会习俗，甚至计算机保存的状态，都是围绕某物的布；没有这块布，线就没有图案。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: threads woven around a single strand, giving it a place in a pattern.","cn":"核心意象：许多线围绕一根线编织，使它在一个图案里有位置。"},"chain":["A WORD","SURROUNDING WORDS","WEAVE","MEANING","SITUATION","FRAME"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"LINGUISTIC WEAVE: the words before and after fix the meaning, and in the context of sets that frame first.","cn":"语言编织：前后的词语固定意义，in the context of 则先设好这个框架。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"SITUATIONAL WEAVE: the period, culture and social conditions around an event explain why it happened.","cn":"情境编织：事件周围的时期、文化与社会条件解释了它为何发生。"},{"senses":"03","en":"MEANING ITSELF: a statement is intelligible only because conventions and beliefs surround it.","cn":"意义本身：一句话之所以可理解，只因为惯例与信念围绕着她。"},{"senses":"05","en":"CUTTING THE WEAVE: out of context removes the surrounding threads, and the same words can then mean something false.","cn":"剪断编织：out of context 抽走周围的线，同样的话就可能表达虚假的意思。"},{"senses":"07 · 08 · 09","en":"THE FRAME AS PROPERTY, ACTION AND STATE: contextual marks dependence, contextualize builds the frame, and computing context stores it.","cn":"框架作为属性、动作与状态：contextual 标记依赖性，contextualize 搭出框架，计算机的 context 则保存框架。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Context is con- + text- (woven) + -Ø. The family adds -ual, -ually, -ualize, -ualization and -ure, all still about weaving and surrounding.","cn":"context 是 con- + text-（编织的）+ -Ø。词族加 -ual、-ually、-ualize、-ualization、-ure，都仍围绕“编织与包围”。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin texere family is large and real: texere, textus 'woven thing', textura 'weaving', contextus, and praetextus 'a woven front'. English borrowed them directly.","cn":"拉丁 texere 词族庞大而真实：texere、textus“织物”、textura“编织”、contextus、praetextus“织在前面的东西”。英语直接借入。"},"items":[{"word":"context","structure":"con- (together) + text- (woven) + -Ø (noun)","meaning":"surrounding words or circumstances","meaningCN":"上下文；语境；背景","example":"The word is clear from context.","exampleCN":"这个词从上下文看很清楚。"},{"word":"contextual","structure":"context + -ual (adjective)","meaning":"relating to or depending on context","meaningCN":"语境的；依赖语境的（-ual 构成形容词）","example":"The meaning is contextual, not fixed.","exampleCN":"这个含义依赖语境，并不固定。"},{"word":"contextually","structure":"contextual + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in terms of context","meaningCN":"从语境上看（-ly 构成副词）","example":"Contextually, the reply was polite.","exampleCN":"从语境看，这个回答是礼貌的。"},{"word":"contextualize","structure":"contextual + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to place something in its context","meaningCN":"把……置于语境中（-ize 构成动词）","example":"The teacher contextualized the poem.","exampleCN":"老师把这首诗放回背景中讲解。"},{"word":"contextualization","structure":"contextualize + -ation (noun)","meaning":"the act of placing something in context","meaningCN":"语境化；置于背景中（-ation 构成名词）","example":"The film offers a contextualization of the war.","exampleCN":"这部影片为那场战争提供了背景说明。"},{"word":"contexture","structure":"con- + text- + -ure (noun)","meaning":"the way something is woven together; an interwoven whole","meaningCN":"织法；交织成的整体（-ure 构成名词）","example":"The contexture of the argument is complex.","exampleCN":"这个论证的织构很复杂。"},{"word":"text","structure":"text- (woven) + -Ø","meaning":"written or printed words, literally 'that which is woven'","meaningCN":"文本；文字（同一词根，字面“编织之物”）","example":"The text is printed in two columns.","exampleCN":"正文分两栏排印。"},{"word":"textile","structure":"text- + -ile (adjective and noun)","meaning":"woven cloth, or relating to weaving","meaningCN":"纺织品；纺织的（同一词根）","example":"The town was famous for its textiles.","exampleCN":"这个镇曾以纺织品闻名。"},{"word":"texture","structure":"text- + -ure (noun)","meaning":"the feel or arrangement of a surface","meaningCN":"质地；纹理（同一词根）","example":"The bread has a coarse texture.","exampleCN":"这面包质地粗糙。"},{"word":"pretext","structure":"prae- (before) + text- (woven)","meaning":"a false reason woven in front of the real one","meaningCN":"借口；托词（prae- 表在前，字面“织在前面的东西”）","example":"He left early under the pretext of illness.","exampleCN":"他借口生病提前离开了。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"contexere","structure":"con- + texere","meaning":"to weave together, join, connect","meaningCN":"编织在一起；连接"},{"word":"texere","structure":"PIE *teks-","meaning":"to weave, fabricate","meaningCN":"编织；制造"},{"word":"contextus","structure":"past participle of contexere","meaning":"a joining together; the woven whole","meaningCN":"连接；编织成的整体"}]}},{"word":"contract","ipa_uk":"/ˈkɒntrækt/","ipa_us":"/ˈkɑːntrækt/","definition_zh":"合同；契约；签订合同；收缩；感染","definition_en":"a legal agreement, the act of making one, or to draw together, shrink or catch an illness","core_image":"两双手把一根绳子从两端拉紧，绳子变短、两端靠拢","scene":"会议室里，两方代表在文件末尾签下名字，交换副本并握手。主持者说：Both parties have signed the contract.","sceneCN":"这里 contract 是「合同、契约」（第 1 个义项：双方订立的正式协议）；句意：双方都已签署合同。图中可辨识物件：合同文本、签字笔、印章、双方代表。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"合同；契约；承包合同"},{"tag":"vi./vt.","zh":"签订合同；收缩；感染（重音后移）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"sign a contract","zh":"签署合同"},{"phrase":"breach of contract","zh":"违约"},{"phrase":"contract with","zh":"与……签订合同"},{"phrase":"contract a disease","zh":"感染疾病"},{"phrase":"a binding contract","zh":"有约束力的合同"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"contracts"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contraction","pos":"n.","zh":"收缩；缩略形式；（分娩）宫缩"},{"word":"contractor","pos":"n.","zh":"承包商；承包人"},{"word":"contractual","pos":"adj.","zh":"合同的；契约规定的"},{"word":"contracture","pos":"n.","zh":"挛缩（肌肉或关节的永久收缩）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A legal agreement","titleCN":"合同：把双方绑在一起的协议","definition":"a legally binding agreement between two or more parties to do or not do something","definitionCN":"两方或多方之间就做或不做某事达成的具有法律约束力的协议","example":"The contract runs for three years.","exampleCN":"这份合同有效期为三年。","why":"Latin contrahere means 'draw together'. An agreement draws two parties into one binding relation, which is why contract names both the drawing and the document.","whyCN":"拉丁语 contrahere 意为“拉到一起”。协议把两方拉进一种有约束的关系，所以 contract 既指“拉拢”这个动作，也指文件本身。"},{"no":"02","title":"To make a legal agreement","titleCN":"签订：把协议拉成事实","definition":"to enter into a formal agreement, usually with with","definitionCN":"订立正式协议，通常与 with 连用","example":"The firm contracted with a local supplier.","exampleCN":"这家公司与当地供应商签订了合同。","why":"The verb sense 'make an agreement' is recorded from the early 15th century, slightly after the noun. The parties are drawn together by the terms.","whyCN":"动词义“订立协议”记录于 15 世纪早期，比名词稍晚。双方被条款拉到一起。"},{"no":"03","title":"Shrink: draw in physically","titleCN":"收缩：体积或长度变小","definition":"to become smaller, shorter or tighter, as a material or muscle does","definitionCN":"像材料或肌肉那样变短、变小或变紧","example":"Metal contracts as it cools.","exampleCN":"金属冷却时会收缩。","why":"This is the oldest verb sense (late 14c.): 'to draw into a smaller compass'. Trahere 'draw' is the same pulling in the noun.","whyCN":"这是最古老的动词义（14 世纪晚期）：“拉进更小的范围”。trahere“拉”正是名词里那个“拉”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Catch an illness","titleCN":"感染：疾病“缠上”身体","definition":"to catch or become infected with a disease","definitionCN":"染上或感染某种疾病","example":"He contracted malaria while travelling.","exampleCN":"他旅行时感染了疟疾。","why":"The sense 'acquire as by habit or contagion' is from the 1590s. Illness is pictured as something that draws itself onto the body and tightens its hold.","whyCN":"“像习惯或传染那样获得”这一义项始于 16 世纪 90 年代。疾病被想象成主动缠上身体、并收紧抓握的东西。"},{"no":"05","title":"Acquire a habit or a debt","titleCN":"养成习惯、欠下债务","definition":"to acquire a habit, a debt or an obligation, often unintentionally","definitionCN":"获得习惯、债务或义务，常指无意中形成","example":"She contracted the habit of checking her phone at dawn.","exampleCN":"她养成了天一亮就看手机的习惯。","why":"A habit, like a disease, is something you pick up and then cannot easily drop. The 'draw together' becomes a bond you did not sign.","whyCN":"习惯和疾病一样，是你沾上之后不容易甩掉的东西。“拉到一起”变成了你并未签字的束缚。"},{"no":"06","title":"Draw together: muscles and brows","titleCN":"皱起、收紧：肌肉与眉头","definition":"of a muscle, the brow or a facial feature, to tighten or draw together","definitionCN":"（肌肉、眉头或面部特征）收紧、聚拢","example":"He contracted his brow and read the line again.","exampleCN":"他皱起眉头，把那行字又读了一遍。","why":"Here the physical pulling is visible: two edges of skin or muscle are drawn toward each other, exactly as the Latin verb describes.","whyCN":"这里那种物理拉扯看得见：皮肤或肌肉的两边被拉向彼此，正是拉丁动词所描述的动作。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contraction: shortening a word","titleCN":"缩略：把词拉短","definition":"in grammar, the shortened form of a word or phrase, such as don't from do not","definitionCN":"语法中词或短语的缩略形式，如 don't 由 do not 缩成","example":"'Can't' is a contraction of 'cannot'.","exampleCN":"can't 是 cannot 的缩略形式。","why":"The grammatical sense is from about 1600: letters are drawn together and some are dropped. The word literally shrinks.","whyCN":"语法义约始于 1600 年：字母被拉到一起，有些被省掉。这个词字面上就是“收缩”了。"},{"no":"08","title":"Contraction: the shrinking itself","titleCN":"contraction：收缩过程、宫缩","definition":"the noun for the act of shrinking, or a tightening of a muscle, including labour contractions","definitionCN":"指收缩的动作，或肌肉的收紧，包括分娩时的宫缩","example":"The contraction of the market lasted two years.","exampleCN":"市场萎缩持续了两年。","why":"The -tion noun names the pulling-in as an event, whether in an economy, a material or a womb.","whyCN":"-tion 名词把“往里拉”命名成一个事件，无论发生在经济、材料还是子宫里。"},{"no":"09","title":"Contractor: the party who contracts","titleCN":"contractor：立约做工程的一方","definition":"a person or company that agrees by contract to supply work, services or goods at a price","definitionCN":"按合同以某个价格提供工程、服务或商品的个人或公司","example":"The contractor finished the roof ahead of schedule.","exampleCN":"承包商提前完成了屋顶工程。","why":"The -or suffix marks the one who enters the contract. The word is recorded from the 1540s, with the business sense from 1724.","whyCN":"-or 后缀标记订立合同的一方。该词记录于 16 世纪 40 年代，商业义始于 1724 年。"},{"no":"10","title":"Contractual: fixed by the contract","titleCN":"contractual：合同规定的","definition":"the adjective for duties, rights or terms that the contract establishes","definitionCN":"形容词，指由合同确立的义务、权利或条款","example":"The refund is a contractual right, not a favour.","exampleCN":"退款是合同权利，不是人情。","why":"The -ual suffix turns the agreement into a source of rules: whatever the document draws together becomes legally owed.","whyCN":"-ual 后缀把协议变成规则来源：文件把什么拉到一起，什么就成为法律上应付的东西。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Contract comes from Latin contractus, the past participle of contrahere 'draw several things together; shorten; make an agreement', from com- 'together' + trahere 'to draw'. The noun entered English first, the verb soon after, and both 'shrink' and 'agreement' grew from the same pulling.","cn":"contract 来自拉丁语 contractus，即 contrahere“把几样东西拉到一起；缩短；订立协议”的过去分词，由 com-“一起”加 trahere“拉”构成。名词先进入英语，动词紧随其后；“收缩”与“协议”都从同一个“拉”长出来。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Contrahere meant 'to draw several objects together; draw in, shorten, lessen, abridge', and metaphorically 'make a bargain, make an agreement'.","cn":"contrahere 意为“把几样东西拉到一起；收进、缩短、减小、删节”，并隐喻为“做交易、订立协议”。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Trahere 'to draw, pull' comes from PIE *tragh- 'to draw, drag, move'. The same root gives tract, traction, tractor, extract, subtract and abstract.","cn":"trahere“拉、拖”来自原始印欧语 *tragh-“拉、拖、移动”。同一词根给出 tract、traction、tractor、extract、subtract、abstract。"},{"era":"EARLY 14C ENGLISH","en":"The noun contract is recorded in the early 14th century, originally especially of marriage: 'agreement between two or more persons to do or not do some particular thing'.","cn":"名词 contract 记录于 14 世纪早期，最初尤指婚姻：“两方或多方就做或不做某件特定事情达成的协议”。"},{"era":"LATE 14C–15C ENGLISH","en":"The verb appears in the late 14th century meaning 'shrink, become smaller', and in the early 15th century meaning 'make an agreement'. Both draw on the same image of pulling inward.","cn":"动词在 14 世纪晚期出现，意为“收缩、变小”；15 世纪早期又出现“订立协议”义。两者都依赖同一个“向内拉”的意象。"},{"era":"1590s–1610s ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'acquire as by habit or contagion' dates from the 1590s, and 'the written document containing the agreement' from the 1610s.","cn":"“像习惯或传染那样获得”始于 16 世纪 90 年代；“载有协议的书面文件”义始于 17 世纪 10 年代。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English separates the forms by stress: CON-tract is the noun, con-TRACT the verb. Contract also keeps its medical and grammatical senses of shrinking.","cn":"现代英语用重音区分形式：CON-tract 是名词，con-TRACT 是动词。contract 还保留“收缩”的医学与语法义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group contains one tangere neighbour and two trahere relatives; the near-meaning group separates legal agreements from shrinking and catching.","cn":"形近组包含一个 tangere 近邻和两个 trahere 亲属；近义组区分法律协议、收缩与感染。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"contact","ipa":"/ˈkɒntækt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"touching or communication. Its root is tangere 'touch', not trahere, so it means contact rather than a drawn-together agreement.","definitionCN":"接触或联系。它的词根是 tangere“触碰”，不是 trahere，所以是“接触”而非“拉在一起的协议”。"},{"word":"subtract","ipa":"/səbˈtrækt/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to take one number away from another. Sub- 'under, away' + trahere 'draw' = draw away from.","definitionCN":"从一个数中减去另一个数。sub-“在下、离开”加 trahere“拉”＝从……拉走。"},{"word":"traction","ipa":"/ˈtrækʃn/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"the grip of a wheel or the pulling force in medicine. It is the noun of trahere, pulling.","definitionCN":"车轮的抓地力，或医学上的牵引。它是 trahere“拉”的名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"agreement","ipa":"/əˈɡriːmənt/","tag":"arrangement","definition":"an arrangement that people accept. It can be informal; a contract is the legally binding written form.","definitionCN":"人们接受的安排。它可以是非正式的；contract 是具法律约束力的书面形式。"},{"word":"deal","ipa":"/diːl/","tag":"informal agreement","definition":"an informal business agreement. It is conversational, while contract is formal and enforceable.","definitionCN":"非正式的商业协议。它偏口语，而 contract 正式且可强制执行。"},{"word":"shrink","ipa":"/ʃrɪŋk/","tag":"get smaller","definition":"to become smaller in size. It is the everyday verb, while contract is technical and often about metal, muscle or market.","definitionCN":"尺寸变小。它是日常动词，而 contract 较技术化，常用于金属、肌肉或市场。"},{"word":"catch","ipa":"/kætʃ/","tag":"get an illness","definition":"to become infected with a disease. It is the plain verb; contract is formal and used in medical writing.","definitionCN":"染上疾病。它是普通动词；contract 较正式，多用于医学写作。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: trahere 'draw', the same-root family traction, tractor, extract, subtract, and the stress pair CON-tract / con-TRACT.","cn":"只用真实构件：trahere“拉”，同根词族 traction、tractor、extract、subtract，以及重音对 CON-tract / con-TRACT。"},"normal":[{"en":"Trahere means 'draw, pull'. A contract draws two parties together; a contraction draws a material together.","cn":"trahere 意为“拉、拖”。contract 把两方拉到一起；contraction 把材料拉到一起。"},{"en":"Contract, contact and contradict are three different roots: draw together (trahere), touch (tangere), speak against (dicere).","cn":"contract、contact、contradict 是三个不同词根：拉到一起（trahere）、触碰（tangere）、反着说（dicere）。"},{"en":"Traction, tractor, extract and subtract all show the same pull: grip, pulling machine, pull out, pull away.","cn":"traction、tractor、extract、subtract 都展示同一个“拉”：抓地、牵引机、拉出来、拉走。"},{"en":"Stress tells you which word you have: CON-tract is the paper, con-TRACT is the act of shrinking or signing.","cn":"重音告诉你拿到的是哪个词：CON-tract 是那份纸，con-TRACT 是收缩或签约的动作。"},{"en":"Contract a disease is the same pull: the illness draws itself onto you and holds.","cn":"contract a disease 是同一个“拉”：疾病把自己拉到你身上并抓住不放。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a rope with two people at the ends, each pulling. The rope shortens, and the two are now bound to one length.","cn":"想象一根绳子两端各有一人拉扯。绳子变短，两个人从此被绑在同一段长度上。"},{"en":"The same shortening can be physical (metal), legal (an agreement), grammatical (an apostrophe), or biological (a muscle).","cn":"同一种缩短可以是物理的（金属）、法律的（协议）、语法的（撇号）或生物的（肌肉）。"},{"en":"A contract is therefore not just a document: it is a relation in which two parties can no longer move independently.","cn":"所以合同不只是一份文件：它是一种关系，其中两方不再能各自独立移动。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The lease is a two-year contract with a fixed rent.","cn":"这份租约是一份租金固定的两年期合同。"},{"en":"The company contracted with a foreign builder.","cn":"这家公司与一家外国建筑商签订了合同。"},{"en":"Most metals contract when they freeze.","cn":"大多数金属凝固时会收缩。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·吹克特”——肯（定）吹（着）克（服）特（别长的）条款把两方拉到一起签合同 → contract 合同；动词“拉紧、收缩”","word":"contract"},"root":"源自拉丁语 contrahere“拉到一起、缩短、订约”，由 com-“一起”+ trahere“拉”构成，核心是“把两端往中间拉”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses of contract, all built on one pull. Two parties, two edges of metal, a muscle, a word and a disease are each drawn together; the agreement and the shrinking are the same gesture seen from different sides.","cn":"contract 的十个义项都建立在同一个“拉”上。两方当事人、金属的两边、肌肉、一个词和一种疾病都被拉到一起；协议与收缩是同一个动作从不同侧面看到的样子。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two hands pulling a rope tight, shortening it and binding the ends together.","cn":"核心意象：两双手把绳子拉紧，绳子变短，两端被绑在一起。"},"chain":["TWO ENDS","DRAW","TOGETHER","SHORTER","BOUND","AGREEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02 · 09 · 10","en":"BINDING PEOPLE: drawing two parties together produces a contract, the act of making it, the contractor and the contractual duties.","cn":"把人绑在一起：把两方拉到一起就产生合同、签约行为、承包商和合同义务。"},{"senses":"03 · 07 · 08","en":"BINDING MATTER AND WORDS: metal, muscle and written words shorten, and contraction names the event.","cn":"把物质与文字收紧：金属、肌肉和书面词语变短，contraction 命名这一事件。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"BINDING THE BODY: a disease or a habit attaches itself and then holds on.","cn":"缠住身体：疾病或习惯附着上来，然后抓住不放。"},{"senses":"06","en":"VISIBLE PULLING: a contracted brow shows two edges of skin drawn toward each other.","cn":"看得见的拉扯：皱起的眉头显示皮肤的两边被拉向彼此。"},{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"ONE ROOT, TWO NOUNS: the agreement (contract) and the shrinking (contraction) both come from contrahere, 'draw together'.","cn":"一个词根，两个名词：协议（contract）与收缩（contraction）都来自 contrahere“拉到一起”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Contract is con- + tract- + -Ø, with stress alternating between noun and verb. English derivatives add -ion, -or, -ual, -ure, and prefixes build subtract, extract and abstract on the same root.","cn":"contract 是 con- + tract- + -Ø，名词与动词重音交替。英语派生词加 -ion、-or、-ual、-ure，前缀则在同根上构成 subtract、extract、abstract。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin trahere family is large: trahere, tractus 'a drawing, a tract', contractus, subtractus, extractus, abstractus. English borrowed the whole set.","cn":"拉丁 trahere 词族庞大：trahere、tractus“拉、地带”、contractus、subtractus、extractus、abstractus。英语整套借入。"},"items":[{"word":"contract","structure":"con- (together) + tract- (drawn) + -Ø (noun or verb)","meaning":"a binding agreement; to agree, shrink or catch","meaningCN":"合同；签订；收缩；感染","example":"They signed the contract at noon.","exampleCN":"他们中午签了合同。"},{"word":"contraction","structure":"contract + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of shrinking; a shortened word form; a labour pain","meaningCN":"收缩；缩略形式；宫缩（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The contraction of the economy was severe.","exampleCN":"经济萎缩很严重。"},{"word":"contractor","structure":"contract + -or (person who does)","meaning":"one who agrees to supply work or goods","meaningCN":"承包商；承包人（-or 表施动者）","example":"The contractor hired twenty workers.","exampleCN":"承包商雇了二十名工人。"},{"word":"contractual","structure":"contract + -ual (adjective)","meaning":"required or defined by a contract","meaningCN":"合同规定的（-ual 构成形容词）","example":"There is a contractual deadline in June.","exampleCN":"合同规定的截止日期在六月。"},{"word":"contractually","structure":"contractual + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"according to the contract","meaningCN":"按合同规定地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"They are contractually bound to deliver.","exampleCN":"按合同他们必须交付。"},{"word":"contracture","structure":"contract + -ure (noun of result)","meaning":"a permanent tightening of muscle or joint","meaningCN":"挛缩；永久性收缩（-ure 构成名词）","example":"The injury left a contracture in his hand.","exampleCN":"这次受伤让他的手留下了挛缩。"},{"word":"subcontract","structure":"sub- (under) + contract","meaning":"to give part of contracted work to another firm","meaningCN":"分包（sub- 表在下、次级）","example":"They subcontracted the wiring to a small firm.","exampleCN":"他们把布线分包给一家小公司。"},{"word":"traction","structure":"tract- (drawn) + -ion (noun)","meaning":"the grip of a wheel, or a pulling force","meaningCN":"牵引；抓地力（同一词根的名词）","example":"The tires lost traction on the ice.","exampleCN":"轮胎在冰上失去抓地力。"},{"word":"extract","structure":"ex- (out) + tract- (drawn)","meaning":"to draw out, or something drawn out","meaningCN":"提取；摘录（ex- 表向外，字面“拉出来”）","example":"The machine extracts oil from seeds.","exampleCN":"这台机器从种子中榨油。"},{"word":"abstract","structure":"abs- (away) + tract- (drawn)","meaning":"existing as an idea; to draw away the essential part","meaningCN":"抽象的；提取（abs- 表离开，字面“拉走”）","example":"Beauty is an abstract idea.","exampleCN":"美是一个抽象概念。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"contrahere","structure":"con- + trahere","meaning":"to draw together, shorten, make an agreement","meaningCN":"拉到一起；缩短；订立协议"},{"word":"trahere","structure":"PIE *tragh-","meaning":"to draw, pull, drag","meaningCN":"拉；拖"},{"word":"contractus","structure":"past participle of contrahere","meaning":"drawn together; a contract","meaningCN":"拉到一起的；合同"}]}},{"word":"contradict","ipa_uk":"/ˌkɒntrəˈdɪkt/","ipa_us":"/ˌkɑːntrəˈdɪkt/","definition_zh":"反驳；否认；与……相矛盾；自相矛盾","definition_en":"to say the opposite of what someone has said, or to be inconsistent with something else","core_image":"两支箭头从同一点射出，指向完全相反的两个方向","scene":"法庭上，证人先说是九点，随后又改口说是十一点。律师说：You just contradicted your earlier statement.","sceneCN":"这里 contradict 是「反驳、与先前说法相矛盾」（第 1、4 个义项：说出相反的话、自相矛盾）；句意：你刚刚与先前的陈述自相矛盾。图中可辨识物件：证人席、记录稿、两个时间点、律师。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"反驳；否认；与……相矛盾"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"自相矛盾；说法不一致"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"contradict oneself","zh":"自相矛盾"},{"phrase":"contradict a claim","zh":"反驳某项主张"},{"phrase":"contradict the evidence","zh":"与证据相矛盾"},{"phrase":"contradictory statements","zh":"相互矛盾的陈述"},{"phrase":"in direct contradiction to","zh":"与……直接矛盾"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"contradicts"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"contradicted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"contradicted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"contradicting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contradiction","pos":"n.","zh":"矛盾；反驳；矛盾之处"},{"word":"contradictory","pos":"adj.","zh":"相互矛盾的；对立的"},{"word":"contradictor","pos":"n.","zh":"反驳者；提出相反说法的人"},{"word":"self-contradiction","pos":"n.","zh":"自相矛盾"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Say the opposite of what someone said","titleCN":"反驳：把对方的话反过来说","definition":"to state that what someone has just said is wrong, and give the opposite account","definitionCN":"指出某人刚说的话是错的，并给出相反的说法","example":"She contradicted him in front of the whole committee.","exampleCN":"她当着整个委员会的面反驳了他。","why":"Latin contra dicere is literally 'to speak against'. The word does not merely disagree; it places a second statement directly opposite the first.","whyCN":"拉丁语 contra dicere 字面就是“反着说”。这个词不只是不同意，而是把第二句话直接放在第一句话的对面。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of statements: be inconsistent","titleCN":"相互矛盾：两句话不能同时成立","definition":"of two statements or facts, to be incompatible so that both cannot be true at once","definitionCN":"（两句话或两个事实）互不相容，不能同时为真","example":"The two reports contradict each other on the date.","exampleCN":"两份报告在日期上互相矛盾。","why":"When two statements are set opposite each other, there is no ground on which both can stand. This 'be inconsistent with' sense is recorded from about 1600.","whyCN":"当两句话被放到彼此对面，就没有任何一块地面能让两者同时站住。这一“与……不一致”义约记录于 1600 年。"},{"no":"03","title":"Deny a claim or an accusation","titleCN":"否认：直接说它不成立","definition":"to deny the truth of a claim, accusation or rumour","definitionCN":"否认某项主张、指控或传闻的真实性","example":"The company contradicted the rumour of a merger.","exampleCN":"公司否认了合并的传闻。","why":"The sense 'deny the words or assertions of' is recorded from about 1600. Denial is the negative half of speaking against.","whyCN":"“否认某人的话或断言”这一义项约记录于 1600 年。否认是“反着说”的否定那一半。"},{"no":"04","title":"Contradict oneself","titleCN":"自相矛盾：自己前后打起来","definition":"to make two statements that cannot both be true, so that one cancels the other","definitionCN":"说出两句不能同时为真的话，使一句抵消另一句","example":"He contradicted himself twice during the interview.","exampleCN":"他在采访中两次自相矛盾。","why":"The reflexive form turns the opposition inward: the speaker is now both parties, and the two statements pull against each other inside one mouth.","whyCN":"反身形式把对立转向内部：说话者现在同时是两方，两句话在同一张嘴里面互相拉扯。"},{"no":"05","title":"Contradictory: mutually opposed","titleCN":"contradictory：相互对立的","definition":"the adjective describes two things that cannot both be true or both be accepted","definitionCN":"形容词描述两件不能同时为真或同时被接受的事","example":"The witness gave two contradictory accounts.","exampleCN":"证人给出了两份相互矛盾的陈述。","why":"The -ory suffix marks a relation of opposition: each item points away from the other, like the two arrows from one point.","whyCN":"-ory 后缀标记对立关系：两项各自背离对方，就像从同一点射出的两支反向箭头。"},{"no":"06","title":"Contradiction: the opposing statement","titleCN":"contradiction：那一句相反的话","definition":"the noun for a statement that denies or opposes another statement","definitionCN":"指否定或反对另一句话的那句陈述","example":"His calm reply was a contradiction of everything she had said.","exampleCN":"他平静的回答是对她所说一切的否定。","why":"The -tion noun names the second statement itself. In logic it is the proposition that asserts the negation of another.","whyCN":"-tion 名词命名第二句话本身。在逻辑中，它就是断言另一命题之否定的那个命题。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contradiction in logic","titleCN":"逻辑矛盾：同时肯定与否","definition":"in logic, the relation between a statement and its negation, which cannot both be true","definitionCN":"逻辑中一个命题与其否定之间的关系，两者不能同时为真","example":"The proof ends in a contradiction, so the assumption is false.","exampleCN":"证明以矛盾收尾，所以那个假设是假的。","why":"Philosophy uses contradiction as a tool: if assuming P leads to P and not-P, then P must be rejected. Two arrows cannot both be the true direction.","whyCN":"哲学把矛盾当作工具：若假设 P 会推出 P 与非 P，则 P 必须被否定。两支箭头不可能同时是正确方向。"},{"no":"08","title":"Contradict the evidence or the record","titleCN":"与证据、记录相反","definition":"of a fact or statement, to be contrary to what the evidence or record shows","definitionCN":"（事实或陈述）与证据或记录所显示的内容相反","example":"His version of events contradicts the phone records.","exampleCN":"他对事件的描述与通话记录相矛盾。","why":"Here the second party is not a person but a record. The record 'speaks' too, and the verb treats it as an opposing voice.","whyCN":"这里的第二方不是人，而是一份记录。记录也会“说话”，动词把它当成一个对立的声音。"},{"no":"09","title":"Contradict the trend or expectation","titleCN":"与趋势、预期相反","definition":"to be contrary to a general pattern, expectation or rule, often surprisingly","definitionCN":"与一般模式、预期或规则相反，常含出人意料之意","example":"The results contradict the usual pattern of growth.","exampleCN":"这些结果与通常的增长模式相反。","why":"This extension drops the human speaker entirely: any fact can stand opposite a pattern, and the pattern is what is contradicted.","whyCN":"这一延伸完全去掉了人类说话者：任何事实都能站在某个模式对面，而被反驳的是那个模式。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Contradict comes from Latin contradicere, in classical Latin two words: contra 'against' + dicere 'to say, speak'. It is literally 'speak against', and its relatives dictation, predict and verdict all keep the 'say' root.","cn":"contradict 来自拉丁语 contradicere，在古典拉丁语中是两个词：contra“反对”加 dicere“说、讲”。它字面就是“反着说”，其亲属 dictation、predict、verdict 都保留“说”这个词根。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Contra dicere meant 'to speak against'. The prefix contra was originally a comparative form meaning 'in comparison with', which hardened into 'against, opposite'.","cn":"contra dicere 意为“反着说”。前缀 contra 最初是比较级形式，意为“与……相比”，后来固化为“反对、相反”。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Dicere 'to say, speak' comes from PIE *deik- 'to show, pronounce solemnly'. The same root gives dictate, predict, verdict, diction and index.","cn":"dicere“说、讲”来自原始印欧语 *deik-“显示、郑重宣告”。同一词根给出 dictate、predict、verdict、diction、index。"},{"era":"1570s ENGLISH","en":"English recorded contradict in the 1570s meaning 'speak against, oppose' — a sense now obsolete.","cn":"英语在 16 世纪 70 年代记录 contradict，意为“反着说、反对”——这一义项现已废弃。"},{"era":"1580s ENGLISH","en":"From the 1580s it meant 'assert the contrary or opposite of', which is the modern core.","cn":"自 16 世纪 80 年代起，它意为“断言相反或对立的一面”，这是现代的核心义。"},{"era":"c. 1600 ENGLISH","en":"Two senses appear around 1600: 'deny the words or assertions of' and, of statements, 'be inconsistent with'. The word moves from a person's speech to the relation between propositions.","cn":"约 1600 年出现两个义项：“否认某人的话或断言”，以及（就陈述而言）“与……不一致”。这个词从人的言语转向命题之间的关系。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps person-against-person (contradict a witness) and fact-against-fact (the data contradict the theory). Contradict is the only one of the con- verbs built on 'speak'.","cn":"现代英语同时保留“人对人”（contradict a witness）与“事实对事实”（数据与理论相矛盾）。在 con- 系列动词里，contradict 是唯一建在“说”之上的。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the dicere root from two near-spellings; the near-meaning group ranks kinds of opposition from simple denial to logical refutation.","cn":"形近组把 dicere 词根与两个近形词分开；近义组按对立程度排列，从简单否认到逻辑反驳。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"contract","ipa":"/ˈkɒntrækt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"an agreement, or to shrink. Its root is trahere 'draw', so it means 'draw together', not 'speak against'.","definitionCN":"协议，或收缩。它的词根是 trahere“拉”，所以是“拉到一起”，不是“反着说”。"},{"word":"contravene","ipa":"/ˌkɒntrəˈviːn/","tag":"same prefix, different root","definition":"to break a rule or law. Contra- 'against' + venire 'come' = come against, so it opposes a rule rather than a statement.","definitionCN":"违反规则或法律。contra-“反对”加 venire“来”＝迎面而来，所以它反对的是规则，而不是陈述。"},{"word":"diction","ipa":"/ˈdɪkʃn/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"the way words are chosen and pronounced. It is the noun of dicere, the 'saying' side without contra-.","definitionCN":"用词与发音的方式。它是 dicere 的名词，是“说”的一面，没有 contra-。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"deny","ipa":"/dɪˈnaɪ/","tag":"say it is not true","definition":"to state that something is not true. It is the simple negative act; contradict adds the opposing statement or the clash between two claims.","definitionCN":"声称某事不真实。它是简单的否定行为；contradict 还加上“相反的说法”或“两种主张的冲突”。"},{"word":"oppose","ipa":"/əˈpəʊz/","tag":"be against","definition":"to be against a plan, person or idea. It is broader and can be silent; contradict must be spoken or written.","definitionCN":"反对计划、人或观念。它范围更广，可以不出声；contradict 必须说出或写出。"},{"word":"refute","ipa":"/rɪˈfjuːt/","tag":"prove wrong","definition":"to prove a claim false with evidence. It is stronger than contradict, which only asserts the opposite.","definitionCN":"用证据证明某主张为假。它比 contradict 更强，后者只是断言相反。"},{"word":"conflict","ipa":"/kənˈflɪkt/","tag":"be incompatible","definition":"of facts, interests or statements, to be incompatible. It is the neutral verb for the clash, without the 'speaking' image.","definitionCN":"（事实、利益或陈述）互不相容。它是描述冲突的中性动词，没有“说话”的意象。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: contra 'against' + dicere 'say', the same-root family predict, dictate, verdict, diction, and the fixed phrase contradict oneself.","cn":"只用真实构件：contra“反对”+ dicere“说”，同根词族 predict、dictate、verdict、diction，以及固定搭配 contradict oneself。"},"normal":[{"en":"Contra means 'against' and dicere means 'say'. To contradict is simply to say against.","cn":"contra 意为“反对”，dicere 意为“说”。contradict 就是“反着说”。"},{"en":"Predict is 'say before', dictate is 'say for writing', and verdict is 'truly said'. All keep the dic- root.","cn":"predict 是“提前说”，dictate 是“说给别人写”，verdict 是“如实说出”。它们都保留 dic- 词根。"},{"en":"Contradict, contract and contact look alike but rest on three roots: speak against (dicere), draw together (trahere), touch (tangere).","cn":"contradict、contract、contact 形似但立足三个词根：反着说（dicere）、拉到一起（trahere）、触碰（tangere）。"},{"en":"Contradict oneself is the same opposition turned inward: you are both the speaker and the one spoken against.","cn":"contradict oneself 是同一个对立转向内部：你既是说话者，也是被反驳的那个人。"},{"en":"Contradictory is the adjective of two arrows; contradiction is the second arrow itself.","cn":"contradictory 是两支箭的形容词；contradiction 就是第二支箭本身。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture one point with two arrows leaving it in exactly opposite directions. Only one of them can point where the truth is.","cn":"想象一个点射出两支方向完全相反的箭。只有一支能指向真相所在的方向。"},{"en":"The arrows can be two people, two reports, a claim and a record, or a theory and its data.","cn":"这两支箭可以是两个人、两份报告、一项主张与一份记录，或一个理论与它的数据。"},{"en":"Because the word means 'speak against', even a silent record 'speaks' when it contradicts a claim; English lends a voice to the evidence.","cn":"因为这个词本义是“反着说”，所以连沉默的记录在与主张冲突时也“说话”；英语把声音借给了证据。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She contradicted the official account of the accident.","cn":"她反驳了官方对事故的说法。"},{"en":"The two witnesses contradicted each other.","cn":"两名证人彼此的说法相互矛盾。"},{"en":"His actions contradict everything he says about saving money.","cn":"他的行为与他关于省钱的言论完全矛盾。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·戳·迪克特”——肯（定）戳（穿）迪克特（dict 说）的话，把它反过来讲 → contradict 反驳、矛盾","word":"contradict"},"root":"源自拉丁语 contra dicere“反着说”，由 contra“反对”+ dicere“说”构成，核心是“把一句话放到另一句话的正对面”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of contradict, all built on two arrows. A person, a rumour, one's own earlier words, a logical proposition, a record, an expectation — each can be placed opposite something that claims to be true.","cn":"contradict 的九个义项都建立在两支箭上。一个人、一则传闻、自己先前的话、一个逻辑命题、一份记录、一种预期——每一个都能被放到某个自称真实之物的对面。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two arrows leaving one point in exactly opposite directions.","cn":"核心意象：两支箭从同一点射向完全相反的方向。"},"chain":["A CLAIM","AGAINST","SPEAK","OPPOSITE CLAIM","CLASH","NO COMMON GROUND"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"SPEAKING AGAINST: a person denies or opposes what another has said, and the second voice is the answer.","cn":"反着说：一个人否认或反对另一个人所说的话，第二个声音就是回答。"},{"senses":"02 · 08 · 09","en":"FACTS AGAINST FACTS: two reports, a version against a record, a result against a trend — none of them has a mouth, yet they clash.","cn":"事实对事实：两份报告、一种说法对一份记录、一个结果对一种趋势——它们都没有嘴，却发生了冲突。"},{"senses":"04","en":"TURNED INWARD: self-contradiction places both arrows inside one speaker.","cn":"转向内部：自相矛盾把两支箭都放进同一个说话者体内。"},{"senses":"05 · 06 · 07","en":"THE LOGICAL FORM: contradictory marks the relation, contradiction names the opposing statement, and logic uses it as a proof tool.","cn":"逻辑形式：contradictory 标记关系，contradiction 命名那句相反的话，逻辑则把它当作证明工具。"},{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THE ROOT: contra 'against' + dicere 'say' is visible in every sense; English extends the 'say' to records and data.","cn":"词根本身：contra“反对”+ dicere“说”在每个义项里都看得见；英语把“说”扩展到了记录与数据。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Contradict is contra- + dict- + -Ø. English adds -ion, -ory, -or and -able, and the broader dic- family keeps the 'say' meaning.","cn":"contradict 是 contra- + dict- + -Ø。英语加 -ion、-ory、-or、-able，而更广的 dic- 词族保留“说”的意义。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin dicere family is very large: dicere, dictus 'said', contradictio, dictio 'a saying', praedicere 'foretell', and verdictum 'truly said'.","cn":"拉丁 dicere 词族非常庞大：dicere、dictus“说过的”、contradictio、dictio“说法”、praedicere“预言”、verdictum“如实说出”。"},"items":[{"word":"contradict","structure":"contra- (against) + dict- (said) + -Ø (verb)","meaning":"to speak against; to be inconsistent with","meaningCN":"反驳；与……矛盾","example":"He contradicted the witness calmly.","exampleCN":"他平静地反驳了证人。"},{"word":"contradiction","structure":"contradict + -ion (noun of action or result)","meaning":"a statement that opposes another; the state of clashing","meaningCN":"矛盾；反驳；矛盾之处（-ion 构成名词）","example":"There is a contradiction between the two clauses.","exampleCN":"两个条款之间存在矛盾。"},{"word":"contradictory","structure":"contradict + -ory (adjective)","meaning":"mutually opposed; unable to be true together","meaningCN":"相互矛盾的（-ory 构成形容词）","example":"The witness gave contradictory answers.","exampleCN":"证人给出了相互矛盾的回答。"},{"word":"contradictor","structure":"contradict + -or (person who does)","meaning":"a person who contradicts or opposes","meaningCN":"反驳者（-or 表施动者）","example":"His main contradictor was the junior minister.","exampleCN":"他主要的反驳者是那位副部长。"},{"word":"contradictable","structure":"contradict + -able (adjective)","meaning":"able to be contradicted or denied","meaningCN":"可被反驳的（-able 表可能）","example":"That claim is not easily contradictable.","exampleCN":"那个主张不容易被反驳。"},{"word":"self-contradiction","structure":"self + contradiction (compound)","meaning":"the state of contradicting one's own words","meaningCN":"自相矛盾（复合名词）","example":"The memo is a self-contradiction.","exampleCN":"这份备忘录自相矛盾。"},{"word":"predict","structure":"pre- (before) + dict- (say)","meaning":"to say what will happen before it happens","meaningCN":"预测；预言（pre- 表之前，同一词根）","example":"Scientists predict a rise in sea level.","exampleCN":"科学家预测海平面会上升。"},{"word":"dictate","structure":"dict- (say) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to say words for someone to write; to give orders","meaningCN":"口述；命令（同一词根）","example":"She dictated the letter to her assistant.","exampleCN":"她向助理口述了这封信。"},{"word":"verdict","structure":"ver- (truly) + dict- (said)","meaning":"the decision a jury gives, literally 'truly said'","meaningCN":"裁决（字面“如实说出”，同一词根）","example":"The jury reached a verdict at noon.","exampleCN":"陪审团中午作出了裁决。"},{"word":"diction","structure":"dict- (say) + -ion (noun)","meaning":"the choice and use of words; pronunciation","meaningCN":"措辞；发音（同一词根）","example":"The poem's diction is deliberately old-fashioned.","exampleCN":"这首诗的措辞刻意古旧。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"contradicere","structure":"contra + dicere","meaning":"to speak against, oppose","meaningCN":"反着说；反对"},{"word":"dicere","structure":"PIE *deik-","meaning":"to say, speak, show","meaningCN":"说；讲；显示"},{"word":"contra","structure":"from *com-teros (comparative)","meaning":"against, opposite, in comparison with","meaningCN":"反对；相反；与……相比"}]}},{"word":"contribute","ipa_uk":"/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈtrɪbjuːt/","definition_zh":"捐献；贡献；促成；投稿；出力","definition_en":"to give money, goods, effort or ideas to something shared, or to be one of the causes of a result","core_image":"许多人把各自手里的一份东西放进同一个大箱子","scene":"募捐木箱摆在门口，登记清单上已经写了好几行。 At the food drive every resident contributed one bag of rice to the shared box.","sceneCN":"这里 contribute 是「拿出一份、汇入公共之物」（第 1、5 个义项：捐献财物、各出己份）；句意：在食物募捐活动中，每位居民都向公共木箱捐出一袋米。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"捐献；贡献；投（稿）"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"促成；起作用；出一份力"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"contribute to","zh":"促成；有助于；向……捐献"},{"phrase":"contribute money","zh":"捐钱"},{"phrase":"contribute ideas","zh":"贡献想法"},{"phrase":"contribute an article","zh":"投一篇稿"},{"phrase":"contribute significantly to","zh":"对……有显著促成作用"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"contributes"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"contributed"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"contributed"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"contributing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"contribution","pos":"n.","zh":"贡献；捐款；投稿；促成作用"},{"word":"contributor","pos":"n.","zh":"贡献者；捐献者；投稿人"},{"word":"contributory","pos":"adj.","zh":"促成的；起作用的；有贡献的"},{"word":"contributing","pos":"adj.","zh":"起促成作用的（如 contributing factor）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Give money or goods to a shared fund","titleCN":"捐钱捐物：放进公共的钱箱","definition":"to give money, food or other goods to a fund or cause that many people support","definitionCN":"把钱、食物或其他物品捐给许多人共同支持的基金或事业","example":"Each family contributed a bag of rice to the relief fund.","exampleCN":"每户人家向救济基金捐了一袋米。","why":"Latin contribuere is com- 'together' + tribuere 'to allot, grant'. The first move is to put one's allotment in with the others, so the word begins with a gift that joins a common store.","whyCN":"拉丁语 contribuere 是 com-“共同”加 tribuere“分配、给予”。第一个动作就是把自己分得的那份放进别人的份里，所以这个词从“把礼物汇入公共储备”开始。"},{"no":"02","title":"Give ideas or effort to a project","titleCN":"贡献才智：给出想法与力气","definition":"to give ideas, skills or work to help a group project succeed","definitionCN":"为帮助一个团队项目成功而给出想法、技能或劳动","example":"She contributed several designs to the new campaign.","exampleCN":"她为新活动贡献了好几个设计方案。","why":"The thing placed in the common store need not be money. Ideas and hours are allotments too, and the verb treats them as goods handed over.","whyCN":"放进公共储备的不必是钱。想法与工时也是一种“份”，动词把它们当作交出来的货物。"},{"no":"03","title":"Be one of the causes of a result","titleCN":"促成：成为结果的一个原因","definition":"to be one of several causes that together produce an effect, in the phrase contribute to","definitionCN":"作为若干原因之一共同造成某种结果，用于 contribute to","example":"Poor sleep contributes to weight gain.","exampleCN":"睡眠不足会促成体重增加。","why":"When many causes each add their share to one outcome, the outcome is a common fund of causes. This 'conduce to' sense is recorded in English from the 17c.","whyCN":"当许多原因各自把一份加到同一个结果上，这个结果就是原因的共同储备。这一“有助于、促成”义自 17 世纪起记录于英语。"},{"no":"04","title":"Write for a publication","titleCN":"投稿：把文字交给刊物","definition":"to write an article, story or picture for a newspaper, magazine or book","definitionCN":"为报纸、杂志或书籍撰写文章、故事或图片","example":"He contributes a monthly column to the magazine.","exampleCN":"他每月为该杂志撰写一篇专栏。","why":"The publication is the common store, and the writer hands in a piece to be added to it. The 'write for' sense appears in English in the 17c.","whyCN":"刊物就是那个公共储备，作者交上一篇文章被加进去。“为刊物撰稿”这一义项在 17 世纪出现在英语中。"},{"no":"05","title":"Pay one's share","titleCN":"各出己份：分摊自己那一份","definition":"to pay or provide one's proper share of a cost or duty","definitionCN":"支付或提供自己应承担的那一份费用或责任","example":"Everyone contributed ten dollars toward the gift.","exampleCN":"每个人都为这份礼物出了十美元。","why":"This is the most literal reading of tribuere 'allot': the total is divided, and each person hands over the portion allotted to them.","whyCN":"这是 tribuere“分配”最字面的读法：总额被分开，每个人把自己被分到的那一份交出来。"},{"no":"06","title":"Contribution: the thing given","titleCN":"contribution：交出来的那一份","definition":"the noun for something given to a common fund, or the act of giving it","definitionCN":"指捐给公共基金的某物，或捐助这一行为的名词","example":"Her contribution to the fund was anonymous.","exampleCN":"她对基金的捐助是匿名的。","why":"The -ion noun names the result of the verb: the share that now sits in the common store. It also names the act of putting it there.","whyCN":"-ion 名词命名动词的结果：现在躺在公共储备里的那一份。它也命名把它放进去的行为。"},{"no":"07","title":"Contributor: the person who gives","titleCN":"contributor：出份的人","definition":"a person who gives money, goods, ideas or writing to a shared thing","definitionCN":"把钱、物、想法或文字交给共有之物的人","example":"She is a regular contributor to the journal.","exampleCN":"她是该期刊的常驻撰稿人。","why":"The -or suffix marks the doer. In publishing the word leans toward 'writer', because the article is the share that person hands in.","whyCN":"-or 后缀标记施动者。在出版语境中这个词偏向“撰稿人”，因为文章就是那个人交上的那一份。"},{"no":"08","title":"Contributory: helping to cause","titleCN":"contributory：起促成作用的","definition":"the adjective for something that helps to produce a result, often as one factor among several","definitionCN":"形容某事物帮助产生某种结果，常为若干因素之一","example":"Speed was a contributory factor in the crash.","exampleCN":"超速是这起撞车事故的一个促成因素。","why":"The -ory suffix turns the adding of a share into a property: the factor is 'share-adding' with respect to the outcome.","whyCN":"-ory 后缀把“加进一份”的动作变成一种属性：这个因素相对于结果而言是“在加份”的。"},{"no":"09","title":"Contributing: the factor that adds to a result","titleCN":"contributing：正在加份的因素","definition":"the present participle used adjectivally for a cause that adds to an effect","definitionCN":"现在分词作形容词，指对结果起加份作用的原因","example":"Fatigue was a contributing cause of the error.","exampleCN":"疲劳是造成这个错误的一个原因。","why":"The -ing form keeps the action live: the cause is still in the act of adding its share, rather than being a settled property.","whyCN":"-ing 形式让动作保持进行：这个原因仍在加自己那一份，而不是一个已经定型的属性。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Contribute comes from Latin contribuere, com- 'together' + tribuere 'to allot, assign, grant'. The root tribuere goes back to tribus, a division of the Roman people; the deeper origin of tribus is uncertain.","cn":"contribute 来自拉丁语 contribuere，即 com-“共同”加 tribuere“分配、指派、给予”。词根 tribuere 可追溯到 tribus（罗马人民的部落分区）；tribus 更深层的来源不确定。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Contribuere meant 'to bring together, add, contribute', from assimilated com- 'with, together' + tribuere 'to allot, assign, bestow'.","cn":"contribuere 意为“汇集、添加、贡献”，由同化的 com-“共同”加 tribuere“分配、指派、赐予”构成。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Tribuere came from tribus 'a tribe, a division of the Roman people'. The original image is dividing something among the tribes; the further origin of tribus is source uncertain.","cn":"tribuere 来自 tribus“部落、罗马人民的分区”。最初的意象是把东西分给各部落；tribus 更早的来源不确定。"},{"era":"1520s ENGLISH","en":"English borrowed contribute in the 1520s with the sense 'to give or grant in common with others'.","cn":"英语在 16 世纪 20 年代借入 contribute，义为“与他人共同给予或授予”。"},{"era":"17C. ENGLISH","en":"Two extensions appear: 'to be a factor, conduce to' (contribute to a result) and 'to write for a publication'. Both treat the outcome or the journal as a common fund.","cn":"出现两个延伸义：“成为因素、有助于”（contribute to a result）与“为刊物撰稿”。两者都把结果或刊物当作一个公共储备。"},{"era":"18C.–19C.","en":"The noun contribution and the agent noun contributor spread, especially in charity, publishing and science.","cn":"名词 contribution 与施动名词 contributor 普及开来，尤其在慈善、出版与科学领域。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses contribute for money, ideas, effort, writing and causes. The fixed phrase contribute to is the most common pattern, and it can mean either 'give to' or 'help cause'.","cn":"现代英语用 contribute 覆盖金钱、想法、劳动、写作与原因。固定搭配 contribute to 是最常见模式，既可表示“捐给”，也可表示“促成”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the tribuere family into its 'give out', 'give to' and 'give back' branches; the near-meaning group orders kinds of giving from money to authorship.","cn":"形近组把 tribuere 词族分成“分发出去”“分给”“给回”三支；近义组按给予方式排列，从给钱到给文字。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"distribute","ipa":"/dɪˈstrɪbjuːt/","tag":"same root, opposite direction","definition":"to give out shares to many people. Dis- 'apart' + tribuere 'allot' is the opposite motion to contribute, which brings shares together.","definitionCN":"把份额分发给许多人。dis-“分开”加 tribuere“分配”，方向与 contribute 相反：后者把各份汇集起来。"},{"word":"attribute","ipa":"/əˈtrɪbjuːt/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to say that something is caused by or belongs to someone. Ad- 'to' + tribuere 'assign' means 'assign to', not 'give together'.","definitionCN":"把某事归因于或归属于某人。ad-“向”加 tribuere“指派”意为“指派给”，不是“共同给予”。"},{"word":"tribute","ipa":"/ˈtrɪbjuːt/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"money paid to a stronger power, or words of praise. It is the noun of tribuere, 'that which is allotted or paid'.","definitionCN":"向强者缴纳的贡品，或赞美之词。它是 tribuere 的名词，指“被分配或缴纳之物”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"donate","ipa":"/dəʊˈneɪt/","tag":"money or goods","definition":"to give money or goods to a charity or good cause. It is narrower than contribute and usually implies no share is expected back.","definitionCN":"把钱或物捐给慈善机构或公益事业。它比 contribute 窄，通常暗示不指望回报。"},{"word":"bestow","ipa":"/bɪˈstəʊ/","tag":"formal gift","definition":"to give something valuable to someone, often formally or as an honour. It stresses the giver's generosity, not a common fund.","definitionCN":"把贵重之物正式地或作为荣誉给予某人。它强调给予者的慷慨，而不是公共储备。"},{"word":"subscribe","ipa":"/səbˈskraɪb/","tag":"pay regularly","definition":"to pay regularly for a service or publication. It joins the 'give money to a publication' side of contribute, but as a standing payment.","definitionCN":"定期付费订阅服务或刊物。它对应 contribute 中“给刊物出钱”的一面，但指长期固定付费。"},{"word":"conduce","ipa":"/kənˈdjuːs/","tag":"formal, lead to","definition":"to help to bring about a result, used with to. It is the formal near-synonym of contribute to in the 'cause' sense.","definitionCN":"有助于带来某种结果，与 to 连用。它是 contribute to 在“促成”义上的正式近义词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: com- 'together' + tribuere 'allot', the same-root family tribute, distribute, attribute, and the two patterns contribute to a fund / contribute to a result.","cn":"只用真实构件：com-“共同”+ tribuere“分配”，同根词族 tribute、distribute、attribute，以及 contribute to a fund（捐给基金）与 contribute to a result（促成结果）两种搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Com- means 'together' and tribuere means 'allot'. To contribute is to put your allotted share in with everyone else's.","cn":"com- 意为“共同”，tribuere 意为“分配”。contribute 就是把自己分到的那份放进大家的那堆里。"},{"en":"Distribute sends shares apart; contribute gathers shares together. The prefixes dis- and con- point in opposite directions.","cn":"distribute 把份额分出去，contribute 把份额汇集起来。前缀 dis- 与 con- 指向相反方向。"},{"en":"Attribute is 'assign to' (ad- 'to'), so it names a cause or owner; contribute is 'give with', so it names a giver among givers.","cn":"attribute 是“指派给”（ad-“向”），所以它命名原因或归属者；contribute 是“共同给予”，所以它命名众给予者中的一位。"},{"en":"The same verb covers money, ideas and articles: in each case a share is handed to a common store.","cn":"同一个动词覆盖金钱、想法与文章：每种情况下都是把一份交给公共储备。"},{"en":"Contribute to + noun can mean either 'give to' or 'help cause'. Read the noun: a fund takes money, a disease takes causes.","cn":"contribute to + 名词既可表示“捐给”，也可表示“促成”。看名词：基金收钱，疾病收原因。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a single large box at the front of a hall. Each person walks up with one thing and drops it in. Nothing is complete until the last share arrives.","cn":"想象大厅前方有一只大箱子。每个人拿着一样东西走上去放进箱里。直到最后一份到达，整体才完整。"},{"en":"The box can be a charity, a project, a journal, or a result. The gesture is the same: a part is surrendered to a whole.","cn":"这只箱子可以是慈善、项目、期刊或一个结果。动作都一样：把一部分交出去，归入一个整体。"},{"en":"Because tribuere once meant dividing among tribes, contributing still carries a quiet arithmetic: the whole is counted in shares.","cn":"因为 tribuere 曾经指“分给各部落”，contribute 至今带有一种安静的算术感：整体是按份额来计算的。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Every student contributed an idea to the class project.","cn":"每个学生都为班级项目贡献了一个想法。"},{"en":"Air pollution contributes to thousands of early deaths each year.","cn":"空气污染每年促成数千例过早死亡。"},{"en":"She has contributed to the newspaper for over ten years.","cn":"她为该报撰稿已超过十年。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·吹·笔优特”——肯（定）吹着号角，把笔和优特（特产）一起交上去 → contribute 贡献、捐献","word":"contribute"},"root":"源自拉丁语 contribuere“汇集、添加”，由 com-“共同”+ tribuere“分配、给予”构成，核心是“把自己那一份放进公共之物”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of contribute, all built on one gesture: a share is handed into a common store. Money, ideas, effort, articles and causes are the different things that can be placed in the box.","cn":"contribute 的九个义项都建立在一个动作上：把一份交给公共储备。金钱、想法、劳动、文章与原因，就是可以放进这只箱子的不同东西。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: many hands putting one share each into the same box.","cn":"核心意象：许多只手各拿一份，放进同一只箱子。"},"chain":["MANY PEOPLE","ONE SHARE EACH","HAND IT IN","COMMON STORE","SHARED RESULT","EACH PART COUNTS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 05","en":"MONEY AND GOODS: the share is cash or food, and the common store is a fund or relief box.","cn":"钱与物：这一份是现金或食物，公共储备是基金或救济箱。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"IDEAS AND WORDS: the share is a design or an article, handed to a project or a publication.","cn":"想法与文字：这一份是一个设计或一篇文章，交给项目或刊物。"},{"senses":"03","en":"CAUSES: many factors each add a share, and the result is the common store they build.","cn":"原因：许多因素各加一份，结果就是它们共同建起的储备。"},{"senses":"06 · 07 · 08 · 09","en":"THE SHARE NAMED: contribution is the share, contributor is the giver, contributory and contributing describe the share-adding.","cn":"被命名的份：contribution 是那一份，contributor 是给份的人，contributory 与 contributing 描述“在加份”的状态。"},{"senses":"01 · 03","en":"THE ROOT: com- 'together' + tribuere 'allot' is visible in every sense; the word always joins a part to a whole.","cn":"词根本身：com-“共同”+ tribuere“分配”在每个义项里都看得见；这个词始终把部分接到整体上。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Contribute is con- + trib- + -ute. English adds -ion, -or, -ory and -ing, and the wider tribuere family includes tribute, distribute and attribute.","cn":"contribute 是 con- + trib- + -ute。英语加 -ion、-or、-ory、-ing，更广的 tribuere 词族还包括 tribute、distribute、attribute。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin tribuere family: contribuere 'bring together', tribuere 'allot', tribus 'tribe', tributum 'that which is paid', and distribuere 'deal out'.","cn":"拉丁 tribuere 词族：contribuere“汇集”、tribuere“分配”、tribus“部落”、tributum“被缴纳之物”、distribuere“分发”。"},"items":[{"word":"contribute","structure":"con- (together) + trib- (allot) + -ute (verb)","meaning":"to give a share to something shared","meaningCN":"贡献；捐献；促成","example":"They contributed to the fund.","exampleCN":"他们向该基金捐了款。"},{"word":"contribution","structure":"contribute + -ion (noun of action or result)","meaning":"the act of giving a share, or the share given","meaningCN":"贡献；捐款；促成作用（-ion 构成名词）","example":"Her contribution was decisive.","exampleCN":"她的贡献是决定性的。"},{"word":"contributor","structure":"contribute + -or (person who does)","meaning":"a person who gives money, ideas or writing","meaningCN":"贡献者；捐献者；投稿人（-or 表施动者）","example":"He is a frequent contributor.","exampleCN":"他是常投稿的人。"},{"word":"contributory","structure":"contribute + -ory (adjective)","meaning":"helping to cause a result","meaningCN":"促成的；起作用的（-ory 构成形容词）","example":"It was a contributory factor.","exampleCN":"这是一个促成因素。"},{"word":"contributing","structure":"contribute + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"adding a share to an effect, used as an adjective","meaningCN":"起促成作用的（-ing 分词作形容词）","example":"Fatigue was a contributing cause.","exampleCN":"疲劳是一个促成原因。"},{"word":"tribute","structure":"trib- (allot) + -ute (noun)","meaning":"payment to a stronger power; praise offered as due","meaningCN":"贡品；敬意（同一词根）","example":"The conquered city paid tribute.","exampleCN":"被征服的城市缴纳贡品。"},{"word":"distribute","structure":"dis- (apart) + trib- (allot) + -ute","meaning":"to give out shares to many people","meaningCN":"分发；分配（dis- 表分开，同一词根）","example":"Volunteers distributed blankets.","exampleCN":"志愿者分发了毯子。"},{"word":"attribute","structure":"at- (to) + trib- (assign) + -ute","meaning":"to assign a cause or quality to someone","meaningCN":"把……归因于；归属于（同一词根）","example":"They attribute the delay to weather.","exampleCN":"他们把延误归因于天气。"},{"word":"tributary","structure":"tribut- (paid) + -ary (adjective/noun)","meaning":"a stream that flows into a larger river; formerly, one who pays tribute","meaningCN":"支流；旧指进贡者（同一词根）","example":"The creek is a tributary of the river.","exampleCN":"这条小溪是那条河的支流。"},{"word":"retribution","structure":"re- (back) + tribut- (allot) + -ion","meaning":"something given back as punishment","meaningCN":"报应；惩罚（re- 表回，同一词根）","example":"They feared retribution.","exampleCN":"他们害怕遭到报应。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"contribuere","structure":"com- + tribuere","meaning":"to bring together, add, contribute","meaningCN":"汇集；添加；贡献"},{"word":"tribuere","structure":"from tribus 'tribe'","meaning":"to allot, assign, grant","meaningCN":"分配；指派；给予"},{"word":"tribus","structure":"origin uncertain","meaning":"a tribe, a division of the Roman people","meaningCN":"部落；罗马人民的分区（来源不确定）"}]}},{"word":"controversial","ipa_uk":"/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃl/","ipa_us":"/ˌkɑːntrəˈvɜːrʃl/","definition_zh":"有争议的；引起争论的；有争议性的","definition_en":"causing or likely to cause public disagreement, or belonging to a matter that people argue about","core_image":"同一张桌子两侧的人把同一份文件推向相反方向","scene":"校务会上，是否取消期末考试把会议室分成两派；校长看了看表：This is a controversial proposal.","sceneCN":"这里 controversial 是「引起争论的」（第 1、3 个义项：决定与议题引发对立意见）；句意：这是一个有争议的提案。图中可辨识物件：会议桌、两侧座位、提案文件、时钟。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"有争议的；引起争论的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"争议性的；属于争论话题的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a controversial decision","zh":"有争议的决定"},{"phrase":"a controversial issue","zh":"争议性议题"},{"phrase":"a controversial figure","zh":"争议人物"},{"phrase":"highly controversial","zh":"极具争议的"},{"phrase":"politically controversial","zh":"政治上敏感的"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more controversial"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most controversial"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"controversy","pos":"n.","zh":"争论；争议；论战"},{"word":"controversialist","pos":"n.","zh":"争论者；好争辩的人"},{"word":"controversially","pos":"adv.","zh":"有争议地；引起争论地"},{"word":"uncontroversial","pos":"adj.","zh":"无争议的；不会引起争论的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Of a decision: causing disagreement","titleCN":"决定有争议：赞成与反对同时出现","definition":"of a decision or action, causing strong disagreement among people","definitionCN":"（决定或行动）在人群中引起强烈分歧","example":"The council made a controversial decision to close the library.","exampleCN":"市政会作出了关闭图书馆这一有争议的决定。","why":"Latin controversus means 'turned in the opposite direction'. A decision that is controversial has been turned against itself by a second group, so the disagreement is built into the word.","whyCN":"拉丁语 controversus 意为“被转向相反方向”。一个有争议的决定被另一群人转向了它的反面，因此分歧就写在这个词里。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of a person: attracting criticism","titleCN":"人有争议：赞誉与批评同时存在","definition":"of a person, often criticized and defended in roughly equal measure","definitionCN":"（人）常同时受到批评与支持，且批评与辩护程度相当","example":"She remains a controversial figure in the party.","exampleCN":"她在党内仍是一个争议人物。","why":"A person can be the pivot of two opposed camps. The adjective does not say the person is wrong; it says opinion about the person is turned in two directions.","whyCN":"一个人可以成为两个对立阵营的轴心。这个形容词并不说此人是错的，而是说关于他的意见被转向两个方向。"},{"no":"03","title":"Of a topic: publicly argued","titleCN":"议题有争议：公共讨论持续不断","definition":"of a subject, one that people publicly and repeatedly argue about","definitionCN":"（话题）人们公开且反复争论的","example":"Immigration is a controversial topic in many countries.","exampleCN":"移民在许多国家都是争议性话题。","why":"The -al adjective is formed on controversy, the noun for an ongoing public dispute. A topic is called controversial when the dispute has become a standing feature of it.","whyCN":"这个 -al 形容词由 controversy（持续公共争论的名词）构成。当一个话题的争论已成为它的长期特征，它就被称为 controversial。"},{"no":"04","title":"Of a claim: challenged by others","titleCN":"主张有争议：不断被质疑","definition":"of a claim, theory or finding, disputed by experts or the public","definitionCN":"（主张、理论或发现）受到专家或公众质疑","example":"The study's controversial findings were retested twice.","exampleCN":"这项研究有争议的发现被重复检验了两次。","why":"Here the word marks an epistemic status: the claim has not settled, and rival accounts still push against it. Turning is still happening.","whyCN":"这里这个词标记一种认识论状态：该主张尚未落定，对立说法仍在推挤它。“转向”仍在进行。"},{"no":"05","title":"Controversy: the dispute itself","titleCN":"controversy：争论本身","definition":"the noun for a prolonged public dispute, especially about a matter of opinion","definitionCN":"指持久的公共争论，尤指关于意见分歧之事","example":"The new tax sparked a national controversy.","exampleCN":"新税引发了全国性的争论。","why":"The -y noun names the whole state of being turned against each other. It is not one argument but a field of opposing statements.","whyCN":"-y 名词命名“彼此被转向对面”的整个状态。它不是一次辩论，而是一片对立陈述构成的场。"},{"no":"06","title":"Controversialist: the habitual debater","titleCN":"controversialist：惯于争论的人","definition":"a person who takes part in or enjoys public controversy","definitionCN":"参与或喜欢公共争论的人","example":"He was a famous controversialist in the press.","exampleCN":"他是新闻界有名的争论者。","why":"The -ist suffix marks a role. Such a person is defined by living inside the opposing turn, rather than by holding one settled view.","whyCN":"-ist 后缀标记一种角色。这种人的定义就是生活在“对立转向”之中，而不是持有一个已定的观点。"},{"no":"07","title":"Uncontroversial: not open to dispute","titleCN":"uncontroversial：没有争议的","definition":"not causing disagreement; accepted without argument","definitionCN":"不引起分歧的；无需争论即被接受的","example":"The wording was changed to make the clause uncontroversial.","exampleCN":"措辞被修改，以使该条款不引起争议。","why":"The negative prefix un- cancels the turning: nothing is pushed to the opposite side, so the matter stands in one place.","whyCN":"否定前缀 un- 取消了“转向”：没有任何东西被推到对面，所以这件事只站在一个位置。"},{"no":"08","title":"Controversially: in a disputed way","titleCN":"controversially：以引起争议的方式","definition":"the adverb for doing something in a way that provokes disagreement","definitionCN":"以引发分歧的方式做某事","example":"She controversially awarded the prize to a student.","exampleCN":"她把奖颁给一名学生，此举引起争议。","why":"The -ly adverb attaches the dispute to the manner of the act: the doing itself is what turns people against one another.","whyCN":"-ly 副词把争议接到行为方式上：正是这个做法本身让人们彼此对立。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Controversial is an English adjective built on controversy + -al in the 1580s. Controversy goes back to Latin controversia, from controversus 'turned in an opposite direction', literally contra- 'against' + versus 'turned'.","cn":"controversial 是 16 世纪 80 年代由 controversy 加 -al 构成的英语形容词。controversy 可追溯到拉丁语 controversia，来自 controversus“被转向相反方向”，字面为 contra-“反对”+ versus“被转”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Controversia meant 'a dispute, contention, debate'. It came from controversus 'turned in an opposite direction', the adjective of the verb controversum, from contra 'against' + versus 'turned'.","cn":"controversia 意为“争论、争讼、辩论”。它来自 controversus“被转向相反方向”，其构词是 contra“反对”+ versus“被转”。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Versus is the past participle of vertere 'to turn, turn about, convert'. The PIE root is reconstructed as *wert- 'to turn, wind', which also gives verse, version, reverse and vertigo.","cn":"versus 是 vertere“转、转向、变换”的过去分词。原始印欧词根被重构为 *wert-“转、缠绕”，它也给出 verse、version、reverse、vertigo。"},{"era":"1580s ENGLISH","en":"Controversial is recorded in the 1580s, formed in English from controversy + -al, meaning 'relating to controversy'.","cn":"controversial 记录于 16 世纪 80 年代，在英语内部由 controversy + -al 构成，意为“与争论有关的”。"},{"era":"17C.–18C.","en":"The adjective extends from 'relating to a dispute' to 'of the nature of a dispute', describing books, doctrines and persons involved in argument.","cn":"该形容词从“与争论有关的”扩展到“具有争论性质的”，用来描述卷入论战的书籍、学说与人。"},{"era":"19C.","en":"The modern sense 'tending to excite controversy, disputed' becomes the dominant one, used of decisions, policies and public figures.","cn":"现代义“易引发争论的、有争议的”成为主导义，用于决定、政策与公众人物。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English uses controversial for anything that splits opinion. The base noun controversy keeps the older, more formal sense of a prolonged public dispute.","cn":"现代英语用 controversial 形容任何使意见分裂的事物。基础名词 controversy 保留较早、更正式的“持久公共争论”义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates the vertere 'turn' family from a spelling neighbour with a different root; the near-meaning group ranks the strength of disagreement.","cn":"形近组把 vertere“转”词族与一个词根不同的近形词分开；近义组按分歧强度排列。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"controversy","ipa":"/ˈkɒntrəvɜːsi/","tag":"base noun","definition":"a prolonged public dispute. It is the noun that controversial was built on, so the two differ only in part of speech.","definitionCN":"持久的公共争论。它是 controversial 所由构成的名词，两者只差词性。"},{"word":"controversialist","ipa":"/ˌkɒntrəˈvɜːʃəlɪst/","tag":"derived person noun","definition":"a person who argues in public. It adds -ist to controversial and names a role, not a quality.","definitionCN":"在公共场合争论的人。它在 controversial 后加 -ist，命名一种角色，而非性质。"},{"word":"conversational","ipa":"/ˌkɒnvəˈseɪʃənl/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"relating to conversation. Its root is conversari 'to keep company', not vertere 'to turn'.","definitionCN":"与谈话有关的。它的词根是 conversari“交往”，不是 vertere“转”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"contentious","ipa":"/kənˈtenʃəs/","tag":"argumentative","definition":"causing or likely to cause argument; also describing a person who argues readily. It stresses the readiness to fight.","definitionCN":"引起或可能引起争论的；也形容爱争论的人。它强调随时准备开战。"},{"word":"disputed","ipa":"/dɪˈspjuːtɪd/","tag":"challenged","definition":"of a fact, claim or area, that people disagree about. It is narrower and more factual than controversial.","definitionCN":"（事实、主张或地区）人们存在分歧的。它比 controversial 更窄、更事实化。"},{"word":"debatable","ipa":"/dɪˈbeɪtəbl/","tag":"open to argument","definition":"open to argument, not settled. It suggests reasonable people may debate, without the public heat of controversial.","definitionCN":"可争论的、未定的。它暗示理性的人可以辩论，但没有 controversial 那种公共热度。"},{"word":"divisive","ipa":"/dɪˈvaɪsɪv/","tag":"splitting people","definition":"causing people to split into hostile groups. It is stronger than controversial and focuses on the division produced.","definitionCN":"使人们分裂成敌对群体的。它比 controversial 更强，重点在造成的分裂。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: contra- 'against' + versus 'turned', the base noun controversy, the derived pair controversialist / controversially, and the vertere family (convert, divert, invert, reverse).","cn":"只用真实构件：contra-“反对”+ versus“被转”，基础名词 controversy，派生对 controversialist / controversially，以及 vertere 词族（convert、divert、invert、reverse）。"},"normal":[{"en":"Controversial is controversy + -al. The noun is the dispute; the adjective describes anything that carries that dispute.","cn":"controversial 是 controversy + -al。名词是争论本身；形容词描述带着这场争论的任何东西。"},{"en":"Versus means 'turned'. Controversus is 'turned against'. A controversial issue is one where two sides have turned against each other.","cn":"versus 意为“被转”。controversus 是“被转向反面”。controversial issue 就是两侧已经转向彼此对立的问题。"},{"en":"The same vers- root appears in convert ('turn together'), divert ('turn aside'), invert ('turn in') and reverse ('turn back').","cn":"同一个 vers- 词根出现在 convert（“转到一起”）、divert（“转向一边”）、invert（“向内转”）、reverse（“转回”）。"},{"en":"Conversational is the trap: its root is conversari 'keep company', which has nothing to do with turning against.","cn":"conversational 是陷阱：它的词根是 conversari“交往”，与“转向对立”无关。"},{"en":"Uncontroversial cancels the turning: un- removes the opposition, leaving a matter that stands in one place.","cn":"uncontroversial 取消了转向：un- 去掉对立，留下一个只站在一处的事情。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a document on a table. Two hands press it in opposite directions, and the paper stays flat only because the pushes are equal.","cn":"想象桌上有一份文件。两只手朝相反方向压它，纸之所以还平，只因为两股推力相等。"},{"en":"The word does not tell you which side is right. It only tells you that the object is held between two turns.","cn":"这个词不告诉你哪边对。它只告诉你：这个对象被夹在两个转向之间。"},{"en":"A controversial person is not a person with two faces, but one point that two camps have each turned toward themselves.","cn":"一个有争议的人不是有两张脸，而是一个点，被两个阵营各自转向自己那一边。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The proposal to raise tuition was highly controversial.","cn":"提高学费的提案极具争议。"},{"en":"He is one of the most controversial coaches in the league.","cn":"他是联赛中最具争议的教练之一。"},{"en":"Scientists continue to debate the controversial theory.","cn":"科学家们继续辩论这一有争议的理论。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“看戳·我·湿”——看谁戳到我，衣服湿了，两边就吵起来 → controversial 有争议的","word":"controversial"},"root":"源自拉丁语 controversus“被转向相反方向”，由 contra“反对”+ versus“被转”（vertere“转”）构成；英语在 controversy 后加 -al，核心是“同一件事被两边转向对立”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of controversial, all built on the image of a thing turned against itself. A decision, a person, a topic, a claim and the dispute itself each show a different stage of that opposition.","cn":"controversial 的八个义项都建立在“某物被转向自身反面”的意象上。决定、人物、话题、主张以及争论本身，各自展示这种对立的不同阶段。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one document pushed from opposite sides by two hands.","cn":"核心意象：一份文件被两只手从相反方向推着。"},"chain":["ONE MATTER","TWO SIDES","TURNED AGAINST","PUBLIC DISPUTE","LASTING ARGUMENT","DISPUTED STATUS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01","en":"A DECISION: an act of authority becomes the object both camps push against.","cn":"决定：一项权威行为成为两个阵营都去推的对象。"},{"senses":"02","en":"A PERSON: one figure becomes the pivot around which praise and criticism turn.","cn":"人物：一个人成为轴心，赞誉与批评绕着他转。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"A TOPIC OR CLAIM: the dispute is now a standing property of the subject itself.","cn":"话题或主张：争论已成为该对象本身的一种长期属性。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"THE DISPUTE NAMED: controversy is the whole field of opposition, and a controversialist lives inside it.","cn":"被命名的争论：controversy 是整个对立场，而 controversialist 就生活在其中。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"THE OPPOSITION MARKED: un- cancels the turning, while -ly attaches the dispute to the manner of an act.","cn":"对立被标记：un- 取消转向，而 -ly 把争议接到行为方式上。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Controversial is contra- + vers- + -ial, built in English on controversy. The vertere family supplies -vers-/-vert- words such as convert, divert, invert and reverse.","cn":"controversial 是 contra- + vers- + -ial，在英语内部由 controversy 构成。vertere 词族提供 -vers-/-vert- 系列词，如 convert、divert、invert、reverse。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin vertere family: vertere 'to turn', versus 'turned', controversia 'dispute', conversio 'a turning around', divertere 'turn aside', invertere 'turn in'.","cn":"拉丁 vertere 词族：vertere“转”、versus“被转”、controversia“争论”、conversio“转向”、divertere“转开”、invertere“转入”。"},"items":[{"word":"controversial","structure":"contra- (against) + vers- (turned) + -ial (adjective)","meaning":"causing or marked by public disagreement","meaningCN":"有争议的；引起争论的","example":"It was a controversial ruling.","exampleCN":"那是一项有争议的裁决。"},{"word":"controversy","structure":"contro- (against) + vers- (turned) + -y (noun)","meaning":"a prolonged public dispute","meaningCN":"争论；争议（-y 构成名词）","example":"The plan caused controversy.","exampleCN":"该计划引发了争议。"},{"word":"controversialist","structure":"controversial + -ist (person who)","meaning":"a person who engages in public dispute","meaningCN":"争论者（-ist 表人）","example":"He was a notorious controversialist.","exampleCN":"他是个出了名的争论者。"},{"word":"controversially","structure":"controversial + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a way that causes disagreement","meaningCN":"有争议地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She controversially rejected the offer.","exampleCN":"她拒绝了那份提议，此举引起争议。"},{"word":"uncontroversial","structure":"un- (not) + controversial","meaning":"not causing disagreement","meaningCN":"无争议的（un- 表否定）","example":"The change was uncontroversial.","exampleCN":"这一改动没有引起争议。"},{"word":"controvert","structure":"contro- (against) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to argue against; to deny","meaningCN":"反驳；否认（同一词根）","example":"He controverted the official account.","exampleCN":"他反驳了官方说法。"},{"word":"incontrovertible","structure":"in- (not) + controvertible (able to be disputed)","meaning":"impossible to deny or dispute","meaningCN":"无可争议的；不容置疑的","example":"The evidence was incontrovertible.","exampleCN":"证据无可争议。"},{"word":"convert","structure":"con- (together) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn something into another form or belief","meaningCN":"转变；转换（同一词根）","example":"They converted the barn into a studio.","exampleCN":"他们把谷仓改成了工作室。"},{"word":"divert","structure":"di- (aside) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn something aside","meaningCN":"使转向；转移（同一词根）","example":"Traffic was diverted around the bridge.","exampleCN":"车辆被引导绕过那座桥。"},{"word":"invert","structure":"in- (in) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn upside down or inside out","meaningCN":"使颠倒；使反转（同一词根）","example":"Invert the bowl to release the cake.","exampleCN":"把碗倒扣过来取出蛋糕。"},{"word":"reverse","structure":"re- (back) + vers- (turned)","meaning":"to turn back; the opposite direction","meaningCN":"颠倒；反向（同一词根）","example":"The car reversed slowly.","exampleCN":"汽车缓缓倒车。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"controversia","structure":"contro- + vers- + -ia","meaning":"a dispute, contention, debate","meaningCN":"争论；争讼；辩论"},{"word":"controversus","structure":"contra + versus","meaning":"turned in an opposite direction","meaningCN":"被转向相反方向的"},{"word":"vertere","structure":"PIE *wert-","meaning":"to turn, turn about","meaningCN":"转；转向"}]}},{"word":"conventional","ipa_uk":"/kənˈvenʃənl/","ipa_us":"/kənˈvenʃənl/","definition_zh":"传统的；惯例的；常规的；非核的；（符号）约定俗成的","definition_en":"following established custom, or being the ordinary standard kind rather than a special or new one","core_image":"一群人围坐一圈，反复走同一条路线，地面上被踩出一条清晰的路径","scene":"婚礼上，长辈提醒新人按老规矩切蛋糕、换戒指、向双方父母鞠躬。司仪说：We follow the conventional order.","sceneCN":"这里 conventional 是「按惯例的、约定俗成的」（第 1、7 个义项：遵从社会习俗、约定做法）；句意：我们按惯例顺序进行。图中可辨识物件：婚礼蛋糕、戒指、双方父母、流程单。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"传统的；惯例的；常规的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"（武器、医学等）常规的；非核的；主流正统的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"conventional wisdom","zh":"普遍看法；传统智慧"},{"phrase":"conventional weapons","zh":"常规武器（非核武器）"},{"phrase":"conventional medicine","zh":"常规医学；正统医学"},{"phrase":"conventional method","zh":"常规方法"},{"phrase":"conventional standards","zh":"传统标准；惯例标准"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more conventional"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most conventional"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"convention","pos":"n.","zh":"惯例；习俗；公约；大会"},{"word":"conventionally","pos":"adv.","zh":"按惯例地；传统地"},{"word":"conventionality","pos":"n.","zh":"因循守旧；合乎惯例"},{"word":"unconventional","pos":"adj.","zh":"非常规的；不按惯例的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Following social custom","titleCN":"遵从社会习俗：按大家认可的方式做","definition":"behaving in the way that most people in a society accept as proper","definitionCN":"以社会中多数人认可为得体的方式行事","example":"His conventional manners made him popular with older relatives.","exampleCN":"他循规蹈矩的举止让长辈们很喜欢他。","why":"Latin convenire is 'to come together'. What people agree on when they come together becomes a convention, and conventional behaviour is behaviour that follows that agreement.","whyCN":"拉丁语 convenire 是“走到一起”。人们聚到一起时达成的东西就成为 convention（惯例），而 conventional 行为就是遵从这一协议的行为。"},{"no":"02","title":"Ordinary, standard, not special","titleCN":"常规的：普通标准，不加特殊设计","definition":"of a thing or method, ordinary and standard rather than new, special or experimental","definitionCN":"（事物或方法）普通而标准，而非新颖、特殊或实验性的","example":"The builder chose a conventional design for the house.","exampleCN":"建造者为这栋房子选择了常规设计。","why":"Once a custom settles, it becomes the default path. A conventional design is simply the one everyone expects, so the word slides from 'agreed' to 'ordinary'.","whyCN":"一种习俗一旦落定，就成了默认路径。conventional design 就是人人预期的那种，于是这个词从“约定”滑向“普通”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Conventional wisdom: the accepted view","titleCN":"conventional wisdom：被普遍接受的看法","definition":"the body of ideas that most people accept, often without examining them","definitionCN":"多数人接受的一套观念，且常未经检验","example":"Conventional wisdom says that prices always rise in winter.","exampleCN":"普遍看法认为冬季物价总会上涨。","why":"The phrase treats a whole set of beliefs as a settled agreement. It can be neutral or sceptical: accepted does not mean proved.","whyCN":"这个短语把一整套信念当作已落定的共识。它可以是中性的，也可以带怀疑：被接受并不等于被证明。"},{"no":"04","title":"Conventional weapons: non-nuclear","titleCN":"常规武器：非核的那一类","definition":"of weapons, ordinary non-nuclear arms such as guns, tanks and bombs","definitionCN":"（武器）普通的非核武器，如枪炮、坦克与常规炸弹","example":"The treaty limits conventional forces in the region.","exampleCN":"该条约限制该地区的常规兵力。","why":"The contrast is with nuclear weapons. Here conventional marks the standard category, the one that existed before the exceptional technology appeared.","whyCN":"这里对照的是核武器。conventional 标记标准类别，即在那项特殊技术出现之前就已存在的那一类。"},{"no":"05","title":"Conventional medicine: mainstream treatment","titleCN":"常规医学：主流正统治疗","definition":"the mainstream medical treatment accepted by hospitals and licensed doctors, as opposed to alternative medicine","definitionCN":"医院与执业医生所接受的主流医学治疗，与替代医学相对","example":"She tried conventional medicine before turning to herbs.","exampleCN":"她先尝试了常规医学，之后才转向草药。","why":"The word again picks out the established institution. What is conventional is what the recognised community of practice agrees to use.","whyCN":"这个词再次指认已确立的制度。所谓 conventional，就是被认可的专业共同体同意使用的东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"Based on an agreed sign or rule","titleCN":"约定俗成的：符号或规则靠共识","definition":"of a sign, symbol or unit, having a meaning fixed by agreement rather than by nature","definitionCN":"（符号、标记或单位）意义由约定固定，而非由自然决定","example":"The red triangle is a conventional sign for danger.","exampleCN":"红色三角是表示危险的约定符号。","why":"This is the oldest layer of the word: a convention is literally a coming-together, an agreement. A conventional sign has no natural link to its meaning; people simply settled on it.","whyCN":"这是这个词最古老的一层：convention 字面就是“走到一起”，即协议。约定符号与它的意义没有自然联系；人们只是把它定下来。"},{"no":"07","title":"Convention: an accepted custom","titleCN":"convention：被接受的习俗","definition":"the noun for a customary way of doing things that a group accepts","definitionCN":"指一个群体所接受的惯常做法","example":"It is a convention to shake hands at the start of a meeting.","exampleCN":"会议开始时握手是一种惯例。","why":"The noun names the agreement itself. It is the settled pattern that conventional behaviour then follows.","whyCN":"名词命名协议本身。它是 conventional 行为随后遵从的那个已落定模式。"},{"no":"08","title":"Convention: a large formal meeting","titleCN":"convention：大型正式会议","definition":"a large organised meeting of people with a shared profession or interest","definitionCN":"同一行业或兴趣的人举行的大型有组织会议","example":"The annual medical convention drew ten thousand doctors.","exampleCN":"年度医学大会吸引了一万名医生。","why":"This sense returns to the physical root: people literally come together. The meeting is the coming-together; the customs are what the coming-together produces.","whyCN":"这个义项回到物理词根：人们真的走到一起。会议就是“走到一起”本身；习俗则是“走到一起”所产生的产物。"},{"no":"09","title":"Unconventional: breaking the expected pattern","titleCN":"unconventional：打破惯例的","definition":"not following the usual or accepted way; deliberately different","definitionCN":"不遵循通常或公认方式的；刻意不同的","example":"Her unconventional approach surprised the committee.","exampleCN":"她非常规的做法让委员会感到意外。","why":"The negative prefix un- removes the agreement. Without a settled convention, behaviour has no expected path, and difference becomes the point.","whyCN":"否定前缀 un- 去掉了协议。没有落定的惯例，行为就没有预期路径，而“不同”本身就成了重点。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Conventional comes from Late Latin conventionalis, 'pertaining to a convention or agreement', from convenire 'to come together, meet, agree'. The prefix con- 'together' + venire 'come' is the same root as convene and event.","cn":"conventional 来自晚期拉丁语 conventionalis“与约定或协议有关的”，后者出自 convenire“走到一起、会面、同意”。前缀 con-“共同”+ venire“来”，与 convene、event 同根。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Convenire meant 'to come together, meet, assemble; to agree, accord'. The agreement sense grew out of the physical meeting: people who come together settle matters.","cn":"convenire 意为“走到一起、会面、聚集；同意、一致”。协议义从物理会面生长出来：走到一起的人把事定下来。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN","en":"Conventionalis 'pertaining to a convention or agreement' is formed on conventio (genitive conventionis), the noun of convenire meaning 'a meeting, covenant, agreement'.","cn":"conventionalis“与约定或协议有关的”由 conventio（属格 conventionis）构成；conventio 是 convenire 的名词，意为“会议、契约、协议”。"},{"era":"LATE 15C. ENGLISH","en":"English records conventional in the late 15c. with the sense 'of the nature of an agreement'.","cn":"英语在 15 世纪晚期记录 conventional，义为“具有协议性质的”。"},{"era":"16C.–17C.","en":"The sense widens from formal agreements to social custom: what a community has agreed to do becomes 'conventional' even without a written contract.","cn":"词义从正式协议扩展到社会习俗：一个群体商定要做的事，即使没有书面契约，也成了“conventional”。"},{"era":"19C.","en":"The evaluative sense 'formal, ordinary, not natural or original' becomes common, and conventional is used for standard weapons and mainstream medicine by contrast with newer or exceptional kinds.","cn":"评价性含义“拘泥形式、普通、不自然或无原创性”变得常见；conventional 也用来指标准武器与主流医学，与更新或特殊类别相对。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English keeps both the neutral 'agreed standard' sense and the mildly critical 'unoriginal' sense. The noun convention splits into custom and large meeting.","cn":"现代英语同时保留中性的“约定标准”义与略带批评的“缺乏新意”义。名词 convention 则分为“习俗”与“大型会议”两支。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates three convenire relatives from a spelling neighbour with a different root; the near-meaning group runs from neutral standard to positively old-fashioned.","cn":"形近组把三个 convenire 亲属与一个词根不同的近形词分开；近义组从中性的“标准”排到偏贬的“老派”。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"convention","ipa":"/kənˈvenʃn/","tag":"base noun","definition":"a custom, an agreement, or a large meeting. It is the noun behind conventional and keeps all three strands.","definitionCN":"习俗、协议或大型会议。它是 conventional 背后的名词，保留全部三条脉络。"},{"word":"convenient","ipa":"/kənˈviːniənt/","tag":"same root, different meaning","definition":"useful or easy to use; suiting someone's needs. It is literally 'coming together' with one's plans, not 'following custom'.","definitionCN":"方便有用的；合某人需要的。它字面是“与某人的安排合到一起”，不是“遵从习俗”。"},{"word":"convent","ipa":"/ˈkɒnvənt/","tag":"same root, place noun","definition":"a community of nuns or monks, or the building they live in. It is a place where people come together.","definitionCN":"修女或修士团体，或他们居住的建筑。它是人们走到一起的地方。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"traditional","ipa":"/trəˈdɪʃənl/","tag":"handed down","definition":"following practices passed down from earlier generations. It stresses time and inheritance; conventional stresses current agreement.","definitionCN":"遵循从前辈传下的做法。它强调时间与传承；conventional 强调当下的共识。"},{"word":"customary","ipa":"/kʌˈstəməri/","tag":"usual practice","definition":"usual for a particular person, group or place. It is more descriptive and less evaluative than conventional.","definitionCN":"对某个个人、群体或地方来说通常的做法。它比 conventional 更描述性、更少评价色彩。"},{"word":"orthodox","ipa":"/ˈɔːθədɒks/","tag":"approved doctrine","definition":"following the officially approved beliefs of a religion or field. It is stronger and more doctrinal than conventional.","definitionCN":"遵循宗教或领域内官方认可的信念。它比 conventional 更强、更具教义性。"},{"word":"standard","ipa":"/ˈstændəd/","tag":"fixed norm","definition":"the usual accepted model or level. It is neutral and technical, while conventional can also imply 'unimaginative'.","definitionCN":"通常被接受的型号或水平。它中性且技术化，而 conventional 还可暗示“缺乏想象力”。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: con- 'together' + venire 'come', the noun convention, the derived set conventionally / conventionality / unconventional, and the same-root family convene, convenient, convent.","cn":"只用真实构件：con-“共同”+ venire“来”，名词 convention，派生组 conventionally / conventionality / unconventional，以及同根词族 convene、convenient、convent。"},"normal":[{"en":"Con- means 'together' and venire means 'come'. A convention is people coming together and agreeing; conventional is what follows that agreement.","cn":"con- 意为“共同”，venire 意为“来”。convention 是人们走到一起并达成一致；conventional 就是遵从这一致的东西。"},{"en":"Convene, convenient and convent all come from the same 'come together' root, but only conventional carries the 'custom' meaning.","cn":"convene、convenient、convent 都出自同一个“走到一起”的词根，但只有 conventional 带“习俗”义。"},{"en":"The noun convention has two visible branches: an agreement/custom, and the meeting where people actually come together.","cn":"名词 convention 有两条看得见的分支：协议／习俗，以及人们真正聚到一起的会议。"},{"en":"Conventional weapons are the standard non-nuclear kind; conventional medicine is the mainstream kind. Both mean 'the established category'.","cn":"conventional weapons 是标准的非核武器；conventional medicine 是主流医学。两者都表示“已确立的类别”。"},{"en":"Unconventional is the deliberate refusal of the agreed path: un- removes the convention, and difference becomes the point.","cn":"unconventional 是刻意拒绝那条共识路径：un- 去掉惯例，于是“不同”本身成了重点。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a lawn where everyone walks the same line to the door. After a month the grass is worn into a path. Nobody wrote the rule; the coming-together made it.","cn":"想象一片草坪，所有人都沿同一条线走向门口。一个月后，草被踩出一条路。没人写下这条规则；是“走到一起”造出了它。"},{"en":"A convention is invisible until someone steps off the path. Then the path becomes visible as a rule.","cn":"惯例在无人偏离之前是看不见的。一旦有人走开，那条路才作为规则显现出来。"},{"en":"The word carries both comfort and criticism: the path is safe because many walked it, and dull for the same reason.","cn":"这个词同时带着安心与批评：这条路安全，因为很多人走过；也正因如此而乏味。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"They live a conventional life in the suburbs.","cn":"他们在郊区过着传统安稳的生活。"},{"en":"Conventional wisdom underestimates the cost of delay.","cn":"普遍看法低估了拖延的代价。"},{"en":"The army still relies on conventional weapons.","cn":"这支军队仍依赖常规武器。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·文·神诺”——肯背文书的绅士都按老规矩来 → conventional 传统的、惯例的","word":"conventional"},"root":"源自晚期拉丁语 conventionalis“与约定有关的”，出自 convenire“走到一起、同意”，由 con-“共同”+ venire“来”构成，核心是“大家走到一起商定后形成的做法”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of conventional, all built on people coming together and settling on a way. The same word then marks social custom, the ordinary standard, agreed symbols, mainstream institutions, and the meeting where the agreement happens.","cn":"conventional 的九个义项都建立在“人们走到一起并商定一种做法”上。同一个词随后标记社会习俗、普通标准、约定符号、主流制度，以及达成协议的那场会议。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a crowd walking the same line until the grass becomes a path.","cn":"核心意象：一群人反复走同一条线，直到草地被踩成一条路。"},"chain":["PEOPLE","COME TOGETHER","AGREE","SETTLED CUSTOM","STANDARD FORM","EXPECTED WAY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"SOCIAL CUSTOM: the agreement becomes behaviour, and convention is the custom people follow.","cn":"社会习俗：协议变成行为，convention 就是人们遵从的习俗。"},{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"THE DEFAULT: what everyone expects becomes the ordinary design and the accepted body of belief.","cn":"默认路径：人人预期的东西变成普通设计与被接受的信念体系。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"THE ESTABLISHED CATEGORY: conventional weapons and conventional medicine are the standard kinds, defined against the exceptional.","cn":"已确立的类别：常规武器与常规医学是标准类别，相对于特殊类别而被定义。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"THE AGREEMENT ITSELF: a conventional sign is fixed by consensus, and a convention is also the literal coming-together of a large meeting.","cn":"协议本身：约定符号由共识固定，而 convention 也字面指大型会议的“走到一起”。"},{"senses":"09","en":"THE PATH REFUSED: un- cancels the agreement, making unconventional behaviour visible as a choice.","cn":"拒绝路径：un- 取消协议，使 unconventional 行为作为一种选择显现出来。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Conventional is con- + vent- + -ional, built on the noun convention. The venire family supplies convene, convenient, convent, covenant and event.","cn":"conventional 是 con- + vent- + -ional，建立在名词 convention 上。venire 词族提供 convene、convenient、convent、covenant、event。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin convenire family: convenire 'come together', conventio 'agreement', conventionalis 'of an agreement', conventus 'assembly', and convenientia 'harmony, agreement'.","cn":"拉丁 convenire 词族：convenire“走到一起”、conventio“协议”、conventionalis“协议的”、conventus“集会”、convenientia“和谐、一致”。"},"items":[{"word":"conventional","structure":"con- (together) + vent- (come) + -ional (adjective)","meaning":"following established custom; standard rather than special","meaningCN":"传统的；惯例的；常规的","example":"It is a conventional solution.","exampleCN":"这是一个常规解决办法。"},{"word":"convention","structure":"con- + vent- + -ion (noun)","meaning":"a custom, an agreement, or a large meeting","meaningCN":"惯例；公约；大会（-ion 构成名词）","example":"The convention was signed in 1950.","exampleCN":"该公约于 1950 年签署。"},{"word":"conventionally","structure":"conventional + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in the accepted or usual way","meaningCN":"按惯例地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The dish is conventionally served cold.","exampleCN":"这道菜按惯例是冷食。"},{"word":"conventionality","structure":"conventional + -ity (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being conventional","meaningCN":"因循守旧；合乎惯例（-ity 构成名词）","example":"He disliked the conventionality of the office.","exampleCN":"他不喜欢办公室的因循守旧。"},{"word":"unconventional","structure":"un- (not) + conventional","meaning":"not following accepted custom","meaningCN":"非常规的（un- 表否定）","example":"She took an unconventional route.","exampleCN":"她走了一条非常规的路。"},{"word":"convene","structure":"con- (together) + ven- (come)","meaning":"to call people together for a meeting","meaningCN":"召集开会（同一词根）","example":"The chairman convened the board.","exampleCN":"主席召集了董事会。"},{"word":"convenient","structure":"con- (together) + veni- (come) + -ent (adjective)","meaning":"suited to one's needs; easy to use","meaningCN":"方便的；合适的（同一词根）","example":"The hotel is convenient for the station.","exampleCN":"这家旅馆去车站很方便。"},{"word":"convent","structure":"con- (together) + vent- (come)","meaning":"a religious community living together","meaningCN":"修道院；修会（同一词根）","example":"She entered a convent at twenty.","exampleCN":"她二十岁进了修道院。"},{"word":"covenant","structure":"co- (together) + ven- (come) + -ant","meaning":"a formal binding agreement","meaningCN":"契约；圣约（同一词根，经古法语）","example":"They signed a covenant to share the water.","exampleCN":"他们签署了共享水源的契约。"},{"word":"event","structure":"e- (out) + vent- (come)","meaning":"something that happens, literally 'that which comes out'","meaningCN":"事件（字面“出来之事”，同一词根）","example":"The festival is a yearly event.","exampleCN":"这个节日是一年一度的事件。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"convenire","structure":"con- + venire","meaning":"to come together, meet, agree","meaningCN":"走到一起；会面；同意"},{"word":"conventio","structure":"convent- + -io","meaning":"a meeting, covenant, agreement","meaningCN":"会议；契约；协议"},{"word":"conventionalis","structure":"convention- + -alis","meaning":"pertaining to a convention or agreement","meaningCN":"与约定或协议有关的"}]}},{"word":"convert","ipa_uk":"/kənˈvɜːt/","ipa_us":"/kənˈvɜːrt/","definition_zh":"转换；改变；改建；皈依；兑换","definition_en":"to change something into another form, use, unit or belief, or to cause someone to change their belief","core_image":"一只杯子在手中翻转过来，杯口朝下，里面装的东西换成了另一种","scene":"厨房里，厨师把一锅清水加热、加米、加盖，二十分钟后盛出一碗粥。他说：We converted water and rice into porridge.","sceneCN":"这里 convert 是「把某物转变成另一形态」（第 1 个义项：改变形态或性质）；句意：我们把水和米变成了粥。图中可辨识物件：锅、米袋、清水、盛出的粥碗。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"转换；改变；改建；使皈依；兑换"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"转变；皈依"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"皈依者；改变信仰的人"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"convert A into B","zh":"把 A 转变成 B"},{"phrase":"convert to","zh":"改信（宗教）；改用；转换为"},{"phrase":"convert a building","zh":"改建一栋建筑"},{"phrase":"convert currency","zh":"兑换货币"},{"phrase":"convert a file","zh":"转换文件格式"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"converts"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"converted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"converted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"converting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"conversion","pos":"n.","zh":"转变；转换；改建；皈依；兑换"},{"word":"converter","pos":"n.","zh":"转换器；变流器；转换者"},{"word":"convertible","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"可转换的；可折叠车篷的敞篷车"},{"word":"convert","pos":"n.","zh":"皈依者；改变信仰或立场的人"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Change one form into another","titleCN":"转变形态：把 A 变成 B","definition":"to change something from one form, substance or state into another","definitionCN":"把某物从一种形态、物质或状态变成另一种","example":"The body converts sugar into energy.","exampleCN":"身体把糖转化成能量。","why":"Latin convertere is com- (intensive) + vertere 'to turn'. The core gesture is a full turn: what was facing one way now faces another, so the same thing appears in a new form.","whyCN":"拉丁语 convertere 是 com-（加强）+ vertere“转”。核心动作是一次完整的翻转：原来朝一个方向的东西现在朝向另一边，于是同一个东西以新形态出现。"},{"no":"02","title":"Turn a building to a new use","titleCN":"改建：让建筑换一种用途","definition":"to change a building or room so that it can be used for a different purpose","definitionCN":"改变建筑或房间，使其可用于另一种用途","example":"They converted the old mill into a museum.","exampleCN":"他们把旧磨坊改建成了博物馆。","why":"The building is not destroyed; it is turned toward a new function. The 'into' phrase marks the new face the same structure now presents.","whyCN":"建筑并未被拆毁，而是被转向一种新功能。into 短语标记同一结构现在呈现的新面孔。"},{"no":"03","title":"Adopt a new religion or belief","titleCN":"皈依：自己转向新的信仰","definition":"to change one's religion or set of beliefs, often in the phrase convert to","definitionCN":"改变自己的宗教或信念体系，常用于 convert to","example":"He converted to Buddhism in his thirties.","exampleCN":"他三十多岁时皈依了佛教。","why":"A conversion is a turning of the whole person. The word keeps the physical image: the self turns away from one creed and faces another.","whyCN":"皈依是整个人的转向。这个词保留物理意象：自我背对一种信条，转向另一种。"},{"no":"04","title":"Cause someone else to change belief","titleCN":"使皈依：让别人转向","definition":"to persuade someone to adopt a religion, belief or political position","definitionCN":"说服某人接受某种宗教、信念或政治立场","example":"Missionaries tried to convert the villagers.","exampleCN":"传教士试图让村民们皈依。","why":"Here the verb is transitive: one person turns another. The image gains a second body, and the turn is applied from outside.","whyCN":"这里动词是及物的：一个人把另一个人转过来。意象多了一个身体，转向是从外部施加的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Exchange one currency or unit for another","titleCN":"兑换：把钱或单位换成另一种","definition":"to change money, measurements or values from one system or unit into another","definitionCN":"把钱、度量或数值从一种体系或单位换成另一种","example":"We converted our dollars into euros at the airport.","exampleCN":"我们在机场把美元换成了欧元。","why":"Money and units have no substance to change, only a scale to turn on. Converting is applying the exchange rate, so that the same value is re-read in a new system.","whyCN":"钱与单位没有实质可改，只有一把可以转动的标尺。兑换就是套用汇率，使同一个价值在新体系中被重新读出。"},{"no":"06","title":"Change a file or format","titleCN":"转换格式：让数据换一种编码","definition":"to change data, a file or a recording from one format into another","definitionCN":"把数据、文件或录音从一种格式转换为另一种","example":"The software converts the video to MP4.","exampleCN":"该软件把视频转换成 MP4。","why":"This is the modern technical extension of the same turn: the content stays, the encoding is turned into another readable form.","whyCN":"这是同一个“转向”的现代技术延伸：内容不变，编码被转成另一种可读形式。"},{"no":"07","title":"Score after a try or touchdown","titleCN":"附加得分：把机会转成分数","definition":"in rugby or American football, to add the extra points that follow a try or touchdown","definitionCN":"在橄榄球或美式橄榄球中，在达阵之后追加额外分数","example":"The fly-half converted the try from the touchline.","exampleCN":"飞卫从边线把达阵的附加分踢进了。","why":"Sport borrows the financial sense of 'turn into': a try is an opportunity, and the kick converts it into points. Success in one form is turned into success in another.","whyCN":"体育借用了“变成”的金融义：达阵是一个机会，而踢球把它变成分数。一种形式的成功被转成另一种形式的成功。"},{"no":"08","title":"A convert: the person who has turned","titleCN":"convert：转过身来的那个人","definition":"a person who has changed their religion or beliefs, or newly supports a cause","definitionCN":"改变宗教或信念的人，或新近支持某项事业的人","example":"She is a recent convert to vegetarianism.","exampleCN":"她最近成了素食主义者。","why":"The noun is recorded from the 1560s. It names the person by the completed turn: the one who now stands on the other side.","whyCN":"这一名词记录于 16 世纪 60 年代。它用已完成的转向来命名这个人：现在站在另一边的那位。"},{"no":"09","title":"Conversion: the act or process","titleCN":"conversion：转变的过程","definition":"the noun for the act or process of changing form, use, belief or currency","definitionCN":"指改变形态、用途、信仰或货币的行为或过程","example":"The conversion of the warehouse took two years.","exampleCN":"这座仓库的改建花了两年。","why":"The -sion noun names the turning as a process and a result. It is used across religion, finance, chemistry and building because the same turn underlies them all.","whyCN":"-sion 名词把转向命名为一个过程与结果。它在宗教、金融、化学与建筑中通用，因为同一个“转”支撑着它们全部。"},{"no":"10","title":"Convertible: able to be turned","titleCN":"convertible：可以被转的","definition":"the adjective for something that can be converted, and the noun for a car with a folding roof","definitionCN":"形容可被转换的事物；名词指车篷可折叠的敞篷车","example":"The bond is convertible into shares.","exampleCN":"该债券可转换为股票。","why":"The -ible suffix means 'able to be'. A convertible car is one whose roof can be turned back, the most literal everyday image of the root.","whyCN":"-ible 后缀意为“可被……的”。convertible 汽车就是车篷可以被翻转回去的车，这是该词根最字面的日常意象。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Convert comes from Old French convertir, from Latin convertere 'to turn around, transform', com- (intensive) + vertere 'to turn'. It is a close relative of controversy, reverse and divert, and should not be confused with convey, which comes from a different root.","cn":"convert 来自古法语 convertir，再上溯拉丁语 convertere“翻转、转变”，即 com-（加强）+ vertere“转”。它与 controversy、reverse、divert 是近亲，不要与词根不同的 convey 混淆。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Convertere meant 'to turn around, turn upside down, transform, convert'. The prefix com- here is intensive rather than strictly 'together', so the sense is a complete turn.","cn":"convertere 意为“翻转、倒转、转变、改变”。这里的前缀 com- 是加强语气而非严格“共同”，所以词义是一次完整的转。"},{"era":"LATIN ROOT","en":"Vertere 'to turn' comes from PIE *wert- 'to turn, wind'. The same root gives versus, reverse, divert, invert, vertigo and controversy.","cn":"vertere“转”来自原始印欧语 *wert-“转、缠绕”。同一词根给出 versus、reverse、divert、invert、vertigo、controversy。"},{"era":"c. 1300 ENGLISH","en":"English borrowed convert around 1300 from Old French, first meaning 'to turn one's steps, direct oneself', then 'to change, transform'.","cn":"英语约 1300 年从古法语借入 convert，最初意为“转身、转向自己去的方向”，随后意为“改变、转变”。"},{"era":"14C.–15C.","en":"The religious sense 'to change to a new faith' develops, first of the person converting and later of the person who converts another.","cn":"宗教义“改信新信仰”发展出来，先指本人皈依，后指使他人皈依。"},{"era":"1560s ENGLISH","en":"The noun convert 'one who has changed religion' is recorded in the 1560s. The technical senses of exchanging currency and changing units follow much later.","cn":"名词 convert“改变宗教的人”记录于 16 世纪 60 年代。兑换货币与换算单位的技术义则晚得多。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern English extends convert to buildings, data files, sports scores and energy. The core remains 'turn a thing so that it presents another form'.","cn":"现代英语把 convert 扩展到建筑、数据文件、体育比分与能源。核心仍是“把某物转过来，使它呈现另一种形态”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group separates a same-root twin (converse) from two words with unrelated roots (convey, convent); the near-meaning group ranks how complete the change is.","cn":"形近组把同根双式词 converse 与两个词根无关的词 convey、convent 分开；近义组按变化的彻底程度排列。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"converse","ipa":"/kənˈvɜːs/","tag":"same root, different sense","definition":"to talk with someone; as an adjective, 'opposite'. Both come from convertere, but the everyday verb means conversation, not conversion.","definitionCN":"交谈；作形容词时意为“相反的”。两者都出自 convertere，但日常动词义是交谈，不是转变。"},{"word":"convey","ipa":"/kənˈveɪ/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"to carry or communicate something. Its root is vehere 'to carry', not vertere 'to turn', so nothing is turned.","definitionCN":"运送或传达某物。它的词根是 vehere“运送”，不是 vertere“转”，所以没有任何“转”的动作。"},{"word":"convent","ipa":"/ˈkɒnvənt/","tag":"near spelling, different root","definition":"a religious community living together. It comes from convenire 'come together', not from vertere.","definitionCN":"共同生活的修会。它出自 convenire“走到一起”，不是 vertere。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"transform","ipa":"/trænsˈfɔːm/","tag":"complete change","definition":"to change something completely in form or nature. It is stronger than convert and stresses the new shape.","definitionCN":"彻底改变某物的形态或性质。它比 convert 更强，强调新的形状。"},{"word":"alter","ipa":"/ˈɔːltə/","tag":"partial change","definition":"to change something in part, without making it a different kind of thing. It is weaker and more general than convert.","definitionCN":"部分地改变某物，而不使它变成另一类东西。它比 convert 更弱、更泛。"},{"word":"adapt","ipa":"/əˈdæpt/","tag":"fit to new use","definition":"to change something so that it fits a new purpose or situation. It stresses usefulness, while convert stresses the change of form.","definitionCN":"改变某物使其适应新用途或新情况。它强调适用性，而 convert 强调形态的改变。"},{"word":"proselytize","ipa":"/ˈprɒsələtaɪz/","tag":"recruit believers","definition":"to try to persuade others to join one's religion or cause. It covers only the 'cause someone to convert' sense and is often disapproving.","definitionCN":"试图说服他人加入自己的宗教或事业。它只覆盖“使他人皈依”这一义项，且常含贬义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: con- (intensive) + vertere 'turn', the noun conversion, the -ible adjective convertible, and the vertere family converse, invert, revert, divert, reverse.","cn":"只用真实构件：con-（加强）+ vertere“转”，名词 conversion，-ible 形容词 convertible，以及 vertere 词族 converse、invert、revert、divert、reverse。"},"normal":[{"en":"Con- here intensifies, and vertere means 'turn'. To convert is to turn a thing completely so that it shows another form.","cn":"这里的 con- 表加强，vertere 意为“转”。convert 就是把一个东西彻底转过来，使它呈现另一种形态。"},{"en":"Conversion is the turning as a process; a convert is the person who has finished turning; convertible is what can still be turned.","cn":"conversion 是作为过程的转；a convert 是已经转完的人；convertible 是还可以被转的东西。"},{"en":"Convert, converse and controversy share the vers-/vert- root; convey and convent do not, because their roots are vehere 'carry' and venire 'come'.","cn":"convert、converse、controversy 共享 vers-/vert- 词根；convey 与 convent 不共享，因为它们的词根分别是 vehere“运送”与 venire“来”。"},{"en":"The same verb covers rice into porridge, a mill into a museum, dollars into euros, and a video into MP4: content stays, form turns.","cn":"同一个动词覆盖米变成粥、磨坊变成博物馆、美元变成欧元、视频变成 MP4：内容留下，形式转过去。"},{"en":"Convert to is the pattern for a new faith or system; convert into is the pattern for a new form or use.","cn":"convert to 是转向新信仰或新体系的搭配；convert into 是转向新形态或新用途的搭配。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a cup turned over in one motion. Nothing is added and nothing is lost; only the side that faces up has changed.","cn":"想象一只杯子在一个动作里被翻转。没有添加，也没有失去；改变的只是朝上的那一面。"},{"en":"Sometimes the cup keeps its contents (a mill becomes a museum), sometimes the contents change (rice becomes porridge), and sometimes only the label changes (dollars become euros).","cn":"有时杯子保留内容（磨坊变成博物馆），有时内容改变（米变成粥），有时只换标签（美元变成欧元）。"},{"en":"The word always implies a before and an after that can still be recognised as the same thing under a new face.","cn":"这个词始终暗示一个“之前”和一个“之后”，而两者仍能被认出是同一事物换了副面孔。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Solar panels convert sunlight into electricity.","cn":"太阳能板把阳光转化为电能。"},{"en":"The family converted an old barn into a guest house.","cn":"这家人把旧谷仓改建成了客房。"},{"en":"He converted to Islam while working abroad.","cn":"他在国外工作期间皈依了伊斯兰教。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“肯·沃特”——肯把沃特（water 水）变成冰，再变成汽 → convert 转换、转变","word":"convert"},"root":"源自拉丁语 convertere“翻转、转变”，由 com-（加强）+ vertere“转”构成，核心是“把同一个东西彻底转过来，使它以另一种形态出现”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses of convert, all built on one complete turn. A substance, a building, a believer, a currency, a file and a score can each be turned so that the same thing appears under a new form.","cn":"convert 的十个义项都建立在一次完整的转上。物质、建筑、信徒、货币、文件与比分，每一个都能被转过来，使同一事物以新形态出现。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a cup turned over in one motion, same object, new face.","cn":"核心意象：一只杯子在一个动作里翻转，同一物件，新的朝向。"},"chain":["ONE THING","HELD IN A FORM","TURNED","NEW FORM","NEW USE OR BELIEF","CHANGED STATE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 06","en":"SUBSTANCE AND DATA: sugar becomes energy, a video becomes MP4; the content stays and the encoding turns.","cn":"物质与数据：糖变成能量，视频变成 MP4；内容留下，编码转过去。"},{"senses":"02","en":"BUILDING: the same structure is turned toward a new function, as a mill becomes a museum.","cn":"建筑：同一结构被转向新功能，如磨坊变成博物馆。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"BELIEF: one person turns, or one person turns another; the whole self faces a new creed.","cn":"信仰：一个人自己转，或一个人把另一个人转过来；整个自我朝向新的信条。"},{"senses":"05 · 07","en":"VALUE AND SCORE: currency and points are re-read in another system, so the same worth appears in a new unit.","cn":"价值与比分：货币与分数在另一套体系中重新读出，同一价值以新单位出现。"},{"senses":"08 · 09 · 10","en":"THE TURN NAMED: a convert is the person after the turn, conversion is the process, convertible is what can still be turned.","cn":"被命名的转：convert 是转完之后的人，conversion 是过程，convertible 是还能被转的东西。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Convert is con- + vert- + -Ø. English adds -sion, -er, -ible and -ibility, and the vertere family gives converse, invert, revert, divert, avert and pervert.","cn":"convert 是 con- + vert- + -Ø。英语加 -sion、-er、-ible、-ibility，vertere 词族给出 converse、invert、revert、divert、avert、pervert。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin vertere family: convertere 'turn around', conversio 'a turning', vertere 'turn', inversio 'a turning in', diversio 'a turning aside', reversio 'a turning back'.","cn":"拉丁 vertere 词族：convertere“翻转”、conversio“转向”、vertere“转”、inversio“转入”、diversio“转开”、reversio“转回”。"},"items":[{"word":"convert","structure":"con- (intensive) + vert- (turn) + -Ø (verb)","meaning":"to turn something into another form, use or belief","meaningCN":"转换；改变；使皈依","example":"They converted the attic into an office.","exampleCN":"他们把阁楼改成了办公室。"},{"word":"conversion","structure":"convert + -sion (noun of process or result)","meaning":"the act or result of changing form, use or belief","meaningCN":"转变；转换；改建；皈依（-sion 构成名词）","example":"The conversion took two years.","exampleCN":"改建花了两年。"},{"word":"converter","structure":"convert + -er (person or thing that does)","meaning":"a device or person that converts something","meaningCN":"转换器；转换者（-er 表施动者或工具）","example":"A voltage converter is needed here.","exampleCN":"这里需要一个电压转换器。"},{"word":"convertible","structure":"convert + -ible (able to be)","meaning":"able to be converted; a car with a folding roof","meaningCN":"可转换的；敞篷车（-ible 表可能）","example":"The loan is convertible into shares.","exampleCN":"这笔贷款可转换为股票。"},{"word":"convertibility","structure":"convertible + -ity (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being able to be converted","meaningCN":"可兑换性；可转换性（-ity 构成名词）","example":"Currency convertibility was restored.","exampleCN":"货币可兑换性恢复了。"},{"word":"converse","structure":"con- + vers- (turned)","meaning":"to talk together; the opposite statement","meaningCN":"交谈；相反的说法（同一词根）","example":"They conversed quietly.","exampleCN":"他们低声交谈。"},{"word":"invert","structure":"in- (in) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn upside down or reverse the order","meaningCN":"使颠倒；使反转（同一词根）","example":"Invert the image to see the hidden text.","exampleCN":"把图像反转就能看到隐藏文字。"},{"word":"revert","structure":"re- (back) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to return to a former state","meaningCN":"恢复；回到（同一词根）","example":"The system reverted to its default.","exampleCN":"系统恢复到了默认状态。"},{"word":"divert","structure":"di- (aside) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn something aside; to entertain","meaningCN":"转移；使转向（同一词根）","example":"Funds were diverted to repairs.","exampleCN":"资金被转用于维修。"},{"word":"avert","structure":"a- (away) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn away; to prevent","meaningCN":"避开；防止（同一词根）","example":"Quick action averted a disaster.","exampleCN":"迅速行动避免了一场灾难。"},{"word":"pervert","structure":"per- (thoroughly) + vert- (turn)","meaning":"to turn something away from its proper use or meaning","meaningCN":"歪曲；使堕落（同一词根）","example":"He perverted the meaning of the rule.","exampleCN":"他歪曲了规则的含义。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"convertere","structure":"com- + vertere","meaning":"to turn around, transform","meaningCN":"翻转；转变"},{"word":"vertere","structure":"PIE *wert-","meaning":"to turn, turn about","meaningCN":"转；转向"},{"word":"conversio","structure":"convers- + -io","meaning":"a turning around, conversion","meaningCN":"转向；转变"}]}}]);
